window.TAROT=window.TAROT||{};
window.TAROT.cards=[{"name":"The Fool","num":0,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":82,"end":84,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Child","Task":"Trying out new things without any bias","Element":"AIR","Crystal Guidance":"Quartz, Green Tourmaline","Color Guidance":"Yellow"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"As Card 0, the Fool lies at the beginning of the Major Arcana, but also somewhat apart from the other cards. In a few traditions of Tarot thought its regarded as Card No 22 who has completed the journey to Completion. There is an inherent wisdom and detachment in this card that in a way is a metaphorical allegory to soul freedom."},{"t":"p","x":"A male figure stands at the edge of the cliff. He has a dreamy smile on his face and is looking up at the sky, lost in his own thoughts. At the very next step, of he is not cautious, he would step over into the steep ravine, to calamitous results. He carries a hobo’s sack over his shoulder which seems light and basic. There is a small dog nipping at his feet, the voice of caution. It is warning him of the danger ahead. The Fool does not seem to be cognizant of the warning bells. The Fool is an archetypal traveller who stays just long enough to break old patterns and set new ones. He hides a deep wisdom that comes from having an unconventional, observant eye and standing on the periphery rather than in main stream."},{"t":"p","x":"The Fool is an eternal optimist and travels through life with no emotional baggage and assumptions from past experiences. He is receptive, open, innocent, trusting, spontaneous and joyful. He is a man who lives his life on his own terms and has no regard for societal norms and restraints. A Free Soul. This card indicates new beginnings, setting out on a new adventure and being open to novelty in experience after a painful period has gone by. It indicates the blind\"Leap of Faith” that life sometimes demands of us in order to experience the self enlightenment that awaits each of us."},{"t":"p","x":"A thousand mile journey, they say begins with a single step and the Fool is ironically wise because without fear and guilt, he is brave enough to set out his first steps into an unknown world."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside, the Fool may also be read as a reckless or an unplanned action that could lead to losses for self or others. The voice of caution needs to be heeded else you could face destruction. Refusal to acknowledge it is a sign of foolishness."}],"id":"the-fool","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Impractical and naive behaviour. Too much trust in the goodness of people."},{"t":"p","x":"Not listening to wise counsel. Indifferent to Intuition. Impulsive and rash decisions."},{"t":"p","x":"Poor leadership and overconfidence in own vision. Not having individual confidence and being bound by social conventions excessively."}],"astro":{"planet":"Uranus","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Fool tells you to move forward and try a new direction, even if it seems risky. This is your chance to do your own thing, guided by inner confidence / latent talent so take the Leap of Faith ahead. Refrain : Do not listen to others who try to discourage you from taking a chance to try something new."},{"t":"p","x":"Beware of jealousy and possessiveness of those who try to hold you back. Also beware of being arrogant or overconfident. Take the leap only if inner belief is very strong."}]},"crystals":"Lepidolite, Agate, Tourmaline","gems":"","keywords":["Beginnings","Originality","Spirituality","Eccentricity","Unconventional","Folly"],"tone":null,"img":"00-TheFool.png"},{"name":"The Magician","num":1,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":84,"end":87,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Creator, the Master","Task":"Activity, Taking Initiative, Giving Impulses, Accepting Tasks and Mastering them","Element":"AIR, EARTH","Crystal Guidance":"Opal, Garnet","Color Guidance":"Red"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Magician can be male or female but even if female, the energy will be Alpha and very masculine. This figure stands alone and dominates the frame. He has a young face and wise eyes; he is ageless. Dressed in Red, the Color Guidance of power and ambition he was born to create the world that downloads into his mental space and has the divine blessing (symbolized by the Infinity symbol above his head) to manifest it into reality."},{"t":"p","x":"One arm, holding the Crystal Guidance wand, points towards the Heavens indicating his divine connection and high level of imagination. The other arm points towards the Earth indicating his determination coupled with his vision to actually make his dream come alive into reality in the material world. It resembles the Greek letter ‘ALEPH” which translates into\" AS ABOVE, SO BELOW”"},{"t":"p","x":"The belt around his waist is of special importance. In most decks it is a coiled serpent, possibly Ourobouros, (the alchemical serpent swallowing up its own tail or perhaps the serpent that Moses and the Egyptian magicians were able to make come alive from their staffs)."},{"t":"p","x":"Spread out in front is a table with four objects symbolizing the four suits of the Tarot deck. There is a sword, a wand, a pentacle and a cup on the table. These are the resources which the adept has under his control. And that is the essence of this card; all the tools One needs to master Self and the World are within Himself. The abundance all around in the form of blooming flowers and lush greens indicate the prosperity and power inherent in this card’s energy. This card indicates the ability of the individual to use the resources that the Universe has gifted him with. He is blessed with intelligence and analytical mind and must learn to use the suits of the Universe in the perfect proportion like an Alchemist such that what he envisions can be translated into material manifestation."},{"t":"p","x":"The Magician is a card of material success and attributes. It indicates great ambition and foresight as also the blessings that will guide the Magician like person to find his way through the crossroads of life to create a spectacular world for Himself. The Magician indicates great success and power. It stands for high level of will power; self-control; discernment; self-confidence; freedom from control from others and a free imagination and the force of character that is required to establish your identity in the competitive world."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes up, it shows huge potential in the situation or the person being analyzed. Discernment and acumen must be used to translate this potential into bringing trans-formative changes that could positively affect the world.On the downside, this card could bring in misuse of power and the corrupt use of resources under control. The person could be manipulative and deceitful and cause harm to others on personal ascent to success. He could be a liar and a cheat and be engaged in fraudulent activities since he has supreme intelligence coupled with access to resources. He possesses superb communication skills and a subtle comprehension that he uses to his advantage and gain. The Magician is a powerful card, a trans formative Energy and how it plays out depends on the intentions as shown by the surrounding cards."}],"id":"the-magician","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Blockage in Self expression."},{"t":"p","x":"Carrying emotional pain and fears from past and not going with the flow Trapped energy manifesting as physical troubles or depression."},{"t":"p","x":"Poor communication skills and poor negotiation skills. Arrogance and misuse of personal power to dominate others or a situation."}],"astro":{"planet":"Mercury","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Magician tells you to be wise and assess your surroundings wisely & then take your decisions. Use communication skills to build your rapport & manage your responsibilities."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain: Watch out for dishonesty and trickery from others. Be careful about paper work and documentation that you are involved in."}],"yearNumber":1},"crystals":"Amethyst, Tiger’s Eye, Citrine","gems":"Garnet","keywords":["Initiative","Skill","Activity","Cleverness","Contructive Power"],"tone":null,"img":"01-TheMagician.png"},{"name":"The High Priestess","num":2,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":87,"end":90,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Queen of Heaven","Task":"Patiently waiting for an inner or outer impulse, silence, receptivity, healing serving as an echo","Element":"WATER","Crystal Guidance":"Aquamarine, Rose Quartz","Color Guidance":"Pale Yellow, Cream"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The High Priestess is denoted as a Female, generally seated on a high backed throne. She is holding a scroll or a book(called Tora) representing the divine law that rules and orders the Universe. The costume is pristine white and on her head is an elaborate Crescent Crown. The symbol of Holy Cross adorns her neck and she sits serenely, with a beatific expression on her face. She sits amidst two columns, black and white. The black column has the letter\" B” emblazoned on it while the black carries the letter”J” on it."},{"t":"p","x":"“B” signifies the word BOAZ which stands for Severity and\"J” stands for JACHIN which indicates Compassion / Mercy. These are Hebrew terms and represent the twin pillars of the Temple of Solomen (the Wise). The pillars act as a portal to the Mysterious. The top of the pillars culminate in lotus - like adornments, the symbols of enlightenment in Hinduism and Judaism. The two pillars bear the inherent duality of Nature which is ever present in our Mind as a tussle. This Dual-Unity we find is the key or evolution of Spirit, and the reason that these two ancient pillars has been preserved in our scriptures. The Human mind is fickle and fallible and oscillates between good and evil, anger and peace, divinity and materialism, detachment and attachment, action and passivity and so many other dualities."},{"t":"p","x":"The High Priestess represents the Wisdom to lead life on moderate terms. The Mind swings in a volatile manner from the extremes of darkness to brightness as it seeks to find divine unity in the duality of the nature of things. The Moon represents our Mind, in the astrological terms, and the High Priestess is the Queen of Emotional Equilibrium as she wears it a Crown upon her head. This signifies control over emotional fluctuations and temptations, recognizing the ingrained Oneness with the rules of the Universe."},{"t":"p","x":"The pomegranate laden background is the entrance to the Divine wisdom. If we make earnest calls to quieten the mind and listen to our Inner Voice, we shall be freed forever from the discord and struggle and be transmuted to harmony and purity. The High Priestess is the female creative force; the mother of all wisdom; the female aspect of God. She teaches that the knowledge and the understanding you seek is within you; the subconscious mind, To tap it, you must bypass your conscious mind, and avoid being seduced by the worldly distractions. The High Priestess expends her inner wisdom to be an excellent teacher or guide to souls in darkness and to nurturing those in need."},{"t":"p","x":"The High Priestess is deep in symbolism and makes us understand beautifully that there are times in life when absolute stillness is required to observe the action and chaos around us. No action is also an action and is required at certain junctures."},{"t":"p","x":"The High Priestess brings us to understand the power of Inner Silence and hearing the voice of the Intuition. It advises us to be patient and wait for the divine signal; not jump to conclusions and wait till all the information is presented before us in Divine timing-much like the waxing and waning of Moon presenting the completion of Moon before us but in divine synchronic timing."},{"t":"p","x":"The Crescent moon at her feet is symbolic of the half processed, impulsive emotions being under under her control and her possessing the grace and maturity to wait. When the High Priestess appears in a reading, its time to be passive and take stock of the situation without displaying any over\u0002reactions. Diplomacy and discretion are the need of the hour. There is also a sign that a higher force is at work so be humble and wait for suitable signals before making any decisions or judgements. The advice of a spiritual or psychological counsellor might be sought for complete comprehension of a situation and an unbiased course of action be given. This card additionally means secret knowledge, study of the Occult sciences, strategic and secret planning, high level of judgement power, spiritual powers and practices, deep research and study of a specialized subject, a female presence who can be intuitive and compassionate, a healing time in life, spending time communing with nature especially near water bodies."},{"t":"p","x":"On the down side the High Priestess displays delays in timing of an event. It shows a person who might be secretive and concealing the truth from you. A note of caution is also there as there might be undercurrents of strategic planning against you. The High Priestess also signifies solitude and loneliness, depressive tendancies, anti-social behaviour, mood swings, unpredictable behaviors, miscarriage and delays in conception."}],"id":"the-high-priestess","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Time to take initiative and make things happen by own energy. Warning that person should not sit passive but take active part in the situation."},{"t":"p","x":"Compulsion to introspect which causes discomfort to many. Miscarriage or abortion Depression and nervous breakdown Secrecy and matters hidden from the world."}],"astro":{"planet":"Moon","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological High Priestess tells you to listen to your Intuition. Be silent and observe rather than being vocal or active."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain: Do not be eager to perform action."},{"t":"p","x":"Think deeply about the situation and wait for divine guidance towards the right moment."},{"t":"p","x":"Listen to the Inner Voice & not be swayed by others’ opinions."}],"yearNumber":2},"crystals":"Aquamarine, Moonstone, Labradorite","gems":"Pearl, Moonstone","keywords":["Secrecy","Intuition","Delays","Spiritual Knowledge","Deep Issues","Things Hidden"],"tone":null,"img":"02-TheHighPriestess.png"},{"name":"The Empress","num":3,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":90,"end":93,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Mother, The Nurturer","Task":"Being fertile; bringing something new in this world","Element":"EARTH, AIR","Crystal Guidance":"Emerald, Green Jade","Color Guidance":"Brown"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Empress is a commanding figure, resplendent in her flowing floral robes, glittering crown on her head; resting attentively yet languidly on her elaborate throne. Lush trees and crops thrive around her and fill the scene with bounty and happiness. She is holding aloft a sparkling Crystal ball topped wand in her right hand and her head is adorned with a 12 gem encrusted crown. The 12 gems signify the 12 zodiac signs of astrology and the twin red rubies embody the union of material and spiritual world. The throne on bottom left is emblazoned with the astrological symbol of planet Venus, the planet for Affluence, lavish lifestyle, material comforts and Passion."},{"t":"p","x":"The Empress is a mother figure, she is both a creative force and the ensurer of unity of elements required for the parables of the world to work in unison and not in opposition to each other. She represents the Earth element, the Mother Earth which is highly productive and compassionate and tends to the nourishment needs of all who reside on her, humans; animals; trees ; all flora and fauna who depend on her generosity and fertility power."},{"t":"p","x":"The Empress signifies a time of abundance and fructification, the result of consistent hard work and dedication. The symbol of Venus rules Taurus (security and determination) and Libra (balanced efforts, harmonising skills and favourable results). This figure can stand for the matriarch of the family or the head of a department or a corporation or a self employed creative entrepreneur. Wherever the Empress features there will be success through a visionary outlook, the patience and tact required to make various resources work in collaboration with each other and the flexibility to enjoy the fruits of the labour with abandon and lavishness."},{"t":"p","x":"She is the symbol of feminine instinct-intuitive flashes that enable you to make right decisions at the right time. The Crystal balled wand she carries gives her a deep imagination and divine flashes. She signifies love and harmony and spreads the message that when we collaborate peacefully and willingly to reach a common vision, the end result is well being and prosperity for all."},{"t":"p","x":"This card is very favourable in queries related to financial security and gains. Shows profitability and all round success. She creates an atmosphere where each person is free to develop their own individual potential. In a reading this advises that for your goal to be achieved, its desirable to take help or counsel from an experienced female figure. She could be wife, daughter, a close female relative, female boss, sister Etal."},{"t":"p","x":"This card also signifies deep and abiding love and passion. In marriage related issues, it promises dedication and commitment to marital vows. In love affairs, a deeply rooted attraction to each other that would become more mature and secure as time progresses. It indicates an upcoming marriage or an engagement in the surrounding environment. In fertility and conception related situation, indicates a time for family expansion and the impending birth of a child. The card comprehensively means fruitfulness of action; beauty and sexuality, domestic harmony, personal development and progress, soul understanding derived from personal experience, a period of success and riches after an unfortunate period; emotional and physical comforts;investments yielding lucrative results, luxuries and a comfortable lifestyle."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside the Empress can show a selfish and self centered human presence, loss of power and control, misfortune and the feeling that stars are not supportive, doubts and difficulties, abortion or inability to conceive, domestic quarrels and inter personal clashes."},{"t":"p","x":"The Empress is a positive and empowering Tarot cards and generally indicates a time of personal glory and growth. As a single card or a significator card, its a direct message to work on your latent talents, self love and to be proud in a humble manner of your achievements and contributions in whatever domain of life you have been ordained to perform."}],"id":"the-empress","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Creative block and fear to express one’s ideas and opinions. Creative flow stagnating example-writer’s block."},{"t":"p","x":"Lack of inspiration and desire to live joyfully Financial difficulties and money flow being blocked. Delays in business bringing returns."},{"t":"p","x":"Problems in relationship with mother or with one’s own children. Sexual block, frigidness, lack of interest in physical proximity"}],"astro":{"planet":"Venus","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Empress tells you to think about your true values. Do nurture your generous and productive side that provides love and nourishment to many."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain : Go easy on flaunting your abundance and propagate the message not only of material assets but of life ethics like hard work, patience and saving resources."},{"t":"p","x":"Control your sensual impulses."}],"yearNumber":3},"crystals":"Rose Quartz, Carnelian, Peridot","gems":"Zircon, Diamond","keywords":["Fertility","Abundance","Sensuality","Nurturing","Happiness","Fruitfulness"],"tone":null,"img":"03-TheEmpress.png"},{"name":"The Emperor","num":4,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":93,"end":96,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Father","Task":"Uncompromisingly turning long held intentions., ideas into reality","Element":"FIRE","Crystal Guidance":"Carnelian, Red Jasper","Color Guidance":"Orange"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Emperor is mature, masculine figure seated on a stone throne. He looks stern and commanding with feet firmly planted on his territorial ground. He wears his robes over a full suit of armour. His throne is outdoors and mountains can be seen in the background. The mountains look stark and forbidding."},{"t":"p","x":"The essence of this card is Defence. The empire of love and bonds that the Empress had created with fortitude is now under threat and so the next milestone on the Fool’s Journey, the Emperor has stepped into the picture strongly. The Emperor is always ready to protect his territory and his beliefs. He is an imposing figure and in the real world will translate into a figure of official authority, a Law enforcement officer, Head of a family, head of a business enterprise or any other variation where resources need to be protected. The Emperor is the metaphorical male protector of the home; the father who guards and guides all those within his care. The Emperor is very strong in his authority and his convictions. He loves to rule over his people and dependancy with absolute control. At times a strict disciplinarian, he has total confidence in his leadership abilities and will not hesistate to turn to the stick in case disciplinary needs demand it. Sometimes a misfit in a rebellious and free-thinking group of people, the Emperor is nevertheless an experienced and reliable person and a gift to have around. He is loyal, wise and protective and is widely acknowledged for his fair and wise decisions."},{"t":"p","x":"He is also an empathetic teacher. The white beard is symbolic of his years of experience, could be actual or a reflection of his deep knowledge of a subject. He is very intelligent and has a keen eye to keep all perspectives in mind while making a judgement."},{"t":"p","x":"He is also very practical and worldly wise. The Emperor card teaches the meaning and use of worldly power. There are forces in the world which will try to thwart you, however fair and ethical you are. You must be prepared, at all times to fight for what you believe is yours or what you believe is right. The Ram’s head on the throne signifies power, force and virility. There are 4 ram heads carved in his throne, showing the stable energy of number 4. The Emperor card leads to creating structure out of chaos and laying down rules, policies and procedures for uniform governance."},{"t":"p","x":"This Major Arcana is associated with the Zodiac sign of Aries which reminds us of the fiery and authoritative energy of Aries Ram. It spells activity, energy and determination and a single minded focus to reach a predecided target or vision. The Emperor card is excellent when there is need for reassurance, whether emotional or material in the face of uncertainty. Where you need specific boundaries, achievement of specific goals, need for an authority figure then the Emperor is a much needed energy."},{"t":"p","x":"He brings logical thought processes that serve goal oriented situations very well."},{"t":"p","x":"This card indicates success and is regarded as a positive card in the deck in situations which need to systemised out of disorder."},{"t":"p","x":"Indicates promotions and financial security, deep understanding in relationships provided one partner gets the upper hand and a high level of expertise for students and career aspirants."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside, when the surrounding energies are independent and calling for flexible contemplation and decision making then The Emperor can be seen as a dogmatic figure. His convictions are strong and he does not wish to change unless very strongly convinced."},{"t":"p","x":"He can also indicate unseen enemies and challenges, dissipation of energy, loss of power, demotions, fall from official grace and an indecisive temperament."},{"t":"p","x":"The Emperor stands for boundaries and ethics and duties. He stabilises and protects the extravagance that life offers. Its an attitude that's a necessity in order to move forward in the journey of self growth"}],"id":"the-emperor","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Breaking of unnecessary social norms."},{"t":"p","x":"Progressive movement. Long delayed work getting accomplished. Flexibility in approach and democratic decision making required."},{"t":"p","x":"A person developing sensitivity to others Loss of control and dominance Demotion or professional difficulty"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Aries","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Aries is about asserting yourself and taking control of your life. Showing who the boss is. High on dogmatism and discipline and self initiated action. The Emperor carries attributes of conservatism and being high handed, not taking in opinions of others. Being single minded and protective and possessive will get you ahead for now, but take care that you do not push others too far."},{"t":"p","x":"Astrological Connotations of the 22 Major Arcana Cards Chapter-6"}],"house":1,"houseName":"House of Self","houseMeaning":"Physique, personality, all beginnings, outlook on life, health and vitality","yearNumber":4},"crystals":"Carnelian, Topaz, Sunstone","gems":"Ruby, Emerald","keywords":["Stability","Power","Authority","Discipline","Boundaries"],"tone":null,"img":"04-TheEmperor.png"},{"name":"The Hierophant","num":5,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":96,"end":99,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Saint","Task":"Paying attention to and respecting what is apparent and what is concealed; the search for meaning","Element":"EARTH","Crystal Guidance":"Blue Topaz, Celestite","Color Guidance":"Deep yellow (mustard)"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"This card is regarded as the male counterpart of the High Priestess. A deep degree of spiritual and moral values is the lordship of the Hierophant card. This card, much like the Emperor also plays the role of the Protector and the Organiser. In the Hierophant imagery, a religious or spiritual guru / teacher is firmly seated on a throne. He is wearing red robes and the underdress is white with clearly demarcated 3 crosses Two fingers of his right hand are pointing upwards towards the Heavens while two fingers are pointing towards the Earth. He also holds in his left hand a scepter bearing the representative symbol of the religious trinity. The three crosses on his white collar indicate the presence of trinity in his speech and in his heart - he Father, The Son and the Holy Spirit."},{"t":"p","x":"It can also be translated as the Hindu Trinity of Brahma-Vishnu\u0002Shiva ; the Creator, the Preserver and the Creative Destroyer. Seated at his feet are two apostles, in a position of surrender and humility. They are awaiting more knowledge or are paying him homage. The inter-crossed golden keys are the keys of our subconscious which the Hierophant can enable us to access to open the portals of our progress."},{"t":"p","x":"The Hierophant is seated between the twin contrasting columns beyond which lies the realm of future growth in material or spirit terms. The Almighty functions at a frequency not discernible to the common man so the High Priest or the Hierophant is emblematic of the human representation of the divine presence in our society. All religions have individuals whose task it is to interpret the divine will for their followers. The more organised or structured the religion, the greater the authority of the Hierophant."},{"t":"p","x":"The Hierophant, in Tarot symbology, represents not just religious authority but also the Search for Truth. He is the interpreter of the secrets of the Universe, the mysteries of the Divine Will, the magician who shows us glimpses of what is our Higher Purpose in this lifetime."},{"t":"p","x":"He has an esoteric role to perform and ascend our knowledge to higher levels. Thus he could appear in our life as a Life coach, Astrologer, Tarot Reader, any Occult or Divination practitioner or a illuminated soul who provides you life guidance when you need it most."},{"t":"p","x":"This figure also symbolizes any philosophical or educational organization that mentors and conditions the minds of its followers/students. When this card appears in a reading, it is time to upgrade our beliefs or existing knowledge levels. The Hierophant has come or is about to come into our life for showing us our potential for growth and we should accept the invitation with humility."},{"t":"p","x":"The Hierophant is not always a favourable card. Unlike the High Priestess who selflessly uses her wisdom and compassion to enable others to find their true path, the High Priest or the Hierophant uses his power to increase his own authority over others. He is an institutionalized figure and may use the power he has over people to manipulate them or to serve his ego needs."},{"t":"p","x":"This card thus also gives the subtle message that in order to grow, we can explore the needs of our own soul or adapt your Self to the requirements of others."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside the Hierophant can indicate religious dogmatism, extreme conservatism, need for social acceptance and approval, blind faith in an authority figure. The Hierophant is a powerful figure. He has the ability to make you or break you. You must decide if the advancement you want is worth placating this individual."}],"id":"the-hierophant","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Introspection of a long standing relationship and willing to cross examine it Rejection of “expected behaviour” and embracing change Out of turn promotions, swift academic/ professional advancement. A fun loving and adventuresome person or situation."},{"t":"p","x":"Taking risks to break the conventional limits and soar higher"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Taurus","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Taurus needs to feel secure and safe and plans far ahead. Bestowed with prudent mind and a strategic intent, he is a careful planner. The Hierophant likewise who upholds traditions and rules in a situation or institution and will remind you constantly of keeping with the norms. But security sometimes can be suffocating and this energy too needs to be mellowed and stop being so fanatical about your goal."}],"house":2,"houseName":"House of Money","houseMeaning":"Financial matters, assets, material possessions, sense of self worth","yearNumber":5},"crystals":"Haematite, Carnelian, Turquoise","gems":"Yellow Sapphire, Yellow Topaz","keywords":["Organised Religion","Test Of Life","Knowledge","Dogmatism","Revelation","Spirituality"],"tone":null,"img":"05-TheHierophant.png"},{"name":"The Lovers","num":6,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":99,"end":101,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Crossroads","Task":"Making a decision of one’s own Free Will and based on what lies at the bottom of the heart","Element":"AIR","Crystal Guidance":"Peridot, Ametrine","Color Guidance":"Green"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"This card represents union of opposites whether between a couple, two contrasting polarities of a paradigm, relationship between two persons and even between two separate ideologies. The desire for union is overwhelming. Our need to be loved is inborn. Our search for the one who complements us and completes us is endless. The urge to express love is universal and gives us the goal and motivation to follow our dreams that lead to our heart’s fulfillment."},{"t":"p","x":"The Lovers card can literally show the attraction and cosmic chemistry between a couple. The male and the female figures shown on the card represent the contrasting Yang and Yin energies whose synthesis leads to more creation and beauty in the Universe. They are naked which indicates their willingness for total commitment and transparency in the relationship."},{"t":"p","x":"This Union is blessed and in a way destined as depicted by the magnanimous Angel with the large wings protecting them while they iron out their differences and reach the zenith of perfect understanding with each other.This card can indicate the start of a new love affair or any new partnership, even a business one where deep and heartfelt exchanges will be required. Business but with a strong emotional bond. Its appearance indicates all is going well on the inter personal front or will turn out to be very pleasant in the near future. It is a reassurance that the relationship you are asking about will soon see more collaborative times and you will be reconciled with each other. The second meaning of this card is about the need to make a choice about something. Very often this involves a form of sacrifice. There is a strong crossroads situation coming up where in order to move ahead, you have to choose between your heart and your mind."},{"t":"p","x":"This choice between logic and emotions can be very painful at times but must be done. This card advises you to go after what your heart desires most of the times as that will ensure that your commitment is coming from a deep space within you. In case the situation requires an ethical choice, then logic would be a more judicious preference."},{"t":"p","x":"The card also speaks of union of elements within yourself. This can be contrasting elements within us like daring and passivity, love and hate, fear and recklessness etc. This card tells us to embrace elements of both and take a decision which is a fusion. That helps us to become whole."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside, indicates failure in personal relationships, inability to make the right choice, Unhappiness and emotional frustrations. This card is a beautiful message of synthesis with outsiders as well as the elements inside us. For growth, we need to amalgamate with grace and commit ourselves to long term goals."}],"id":"the-lovers","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Frustration due to repressed emotions or sexuality. Unsuccessful love affair or marriage proposal. Unable to follow one’s heartfelt desire. Recognize and embrace that that sex and spirituality are interconnected and enrich each other. Feeling of loneliness and social isolation. Low physical self esteem leading to anxiety and fear of rejection. Lack of balance I.e. being over emotional or over analytical"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Gemini","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Gemini ruled by the versatile Mercury seeks variety and constant stimulation. Gemini can make one illusional and always searching for multiple options rather than a focus."},{"t":"p","x":"When the Lovers card appears, its time to make a choice. Are you using your wit and intelligence and banking on your Mind or will you listen to your heart and disregarding the tempting options, narrow your attentions to a single point of focus. The choice is yours and its necessary."}],"house":3,"houseName":"House of Communications","houseMeaning":"Communications, letters and writings, public relations, younger siblings, short journeys, what you know, early learning style","yearNumber":6},"crystals":"Ametrine, Rose Quartz, Banded Agate","gems":"Diamond, Fire Opal","keywords":["Love","Personal Relationships","Choice Between Heart & Mind","Selfless Union","Marriage","Inspiration"],"tone":null,"img":"06-TheLovers.png"},{"name":"The Chariot","num":7,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":101,"end":103,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Departure","Task":"Mastering contradictions, Risking something new","Element":"WATER","Crystal Guidance":"Moonstone, Citrine","Color Guidance":"Ochre"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The card of the Chariot stands for victory and success after the mastery of opposing forces by decisiveness and strength of will."},{"t":"p","x":"A royal male figure, dressed in full uniform of a commander of a territorial leader, is driving a chariot. Its an impressive looking imagery as he is fully in armour, the chariot bears the royal insignia, and a canopy dotted with celestial stars. Two sphinx are pulling at the chariot. In some decks they are depicted as mythical creatures like unicorns or winged-horse like creatures. The two creatures bear contrasting Color palette of black and white."},{"t":"p","x":"They represent our opposite natures that lie nestled within us. They are our own aspects that may work in opposition to each other, but are driving towards the same goal, as in your spiritual and physical natures."},{"t":"p","x":"The twin horses or sphinxes represent the pull of two opposing forces within us, the eternal DILEMMA that is constantly inter\u0002playing in the human mind.. The Chariot in the Tarot symbolizes victory over all who oppose you. Its a card of unmitigated success as it combined speed with intelligence."},{"t":"p","x":"The added feather in the Chariot card is the Focus and concentration which the commander is possessing. He has no distractions and is only single mindedly seeing the goal of conquest. Victory reigns supreme in his Mind and as they say victory over Mind is half the battle won already."},{"t":"p","x":"Since you have drawn strength from within by making your opposites work together, you can now defeat your enemy by identifying its weakness and over riding it with your synthesis\u0002ed strengths. This card in a reading stands for Success and Victory in any area the query is about. The only requirement is to curb your weaknesses, work through them till you can use them as weapons."},{"t":"p","x":"This card also indicates that you will get strong support from able bodied or able minded in your time of need to strengthen your forces so that your march to victory continues. On the downside, this card can show emotional weaknesses, conflict and violence, defeat or disharmony."},{"t":"p","x":"The Chariot is a strong card advising us to have clear goals, harness our internal and external resources after introspection and then go after success with full confidence and might. You are unstoppable."}],"id":"the-chariot","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Abrupt delay in situation Loss of concentration and focus Over emotionalism and possible emotional blackmail. Decisions and verdicts getting delayed. Lack of will power Going with the flow of things and letting destiny take its course"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Cancer","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Cancer years for belongingness and wants to acquire a safe haven for itself at all times. Its a watery emotional sign. When the Cancer attribute is overwhelming, the Chariot card reminds to be single-minded on the goal and forge ahead with ambition and clarity. It needs toughness to acquire and belong."}],"house":4,"houseName":"House of Domestic Life","houseMeaning":"The first home environment, your roots, the mother, the imagination, outcome of contests and litigation, emotions, home, conveyance, comforts of material life","yearNumber":7},"crystals":"Amber, Howlite, Chalcedony","gems":"Ruby, Cat’s Eye","keywords":["Travel","Movement","Ambition","Balance","Self-Assertion"],"tone":null,"img":"07-TheChariot.png"},{"name":"Strength","num":8,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":103,"end":105,"meta":{"Archetype":"Taming the Animal","Task":"Enjoyable acceptance of life, courage and commitment","Element":"FIRE","Crystal Guidance":"Ruby, bloodstone","Color Guidance":"Saffron"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"This card shows a young woman, spiritually dressed in pristine white robes and the divine Infinity symbol floating above her head, prising open the jaws of the lion. This might apparently seem foolish and even dangerous but this card teaches us that the problem we will be faced with looks insurmountable but with adequate faith and calmness, is within our ambit to tackle. Strength calls for both physical stamina and the strength of spirit and feeling. This reflects upon the fact that Strength comes from within, not only by physical prowess but also the inner reserves. Strength card calls for a situation where you will be the only one to execute the solution to the problem and to do so with Fortitude. Heads on, the problem would have to be taken on so summon your bravado, daring and dauntless resolve. The Strength card may indicate that you alone may have the leadership skills so an independent approach and initiative will be needed. Supporters may not be available so face the problem in a fortuitous manner and perform your duty with a sense of idealism. The strength associated with this card is in its purest form, which is expressed in gentle encouragement. This card also brings with it good tidings of recovery from ill health and vitality being restored. This card has links with the Greek myth about the labours of Hercules, who was presented with twelve tasks and who cleverly completed all of them by using his wits."},{"t":"p","x":"When the Strength card appears in the spread, its time to show presence of mind. Stay alert to even the slightest signal, almost as an animal instinct. Do not feel defeated by the magnitude of the problem. Remember that you have been placed in this Divine Time and Divine Place to solve a problem that only you can do and in it is concealed an opportunity for incredible internal growth. So embrace it with surrender and Grace. The allegory in this card also displays the battle between the spiritual and the physical. You are on the road to Spiritual enlightenment."},{"t":"p","x":"To achieve your ends, you must tame your base passions and force them to surrender to your Higher Self. The card spells Triumph provided you do not shirk from the challenge. Go ahead, much like the Leo feminine energy this card represents. Address the issue, and confront the areas that need to be worked upon for resolution. On the downside, this card can signify physical or spiritual weakness, rigidity in accepting problems, despotism, failure and disgrace. This card is putting you in a space of incredible endurance. If your will is stronger than your opponent, you will survive and succeed. If not, you shall be defeated and your growth might be stumped. You will lose only if you choose to quit, so in any recourse stay determined and graceful and you shall be protected."}],"id":"strength","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Gratification of one’s desires Questioning belief in God as sense of self becomes dominant The brave front is only a sham Feeling anxious and jittery from the Insides Giving in to lower energies and also carnal desires. Abuse of power at disposal"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Leo","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Leo wants to be special. When you draw Strength are you under the spotlight, do you like being the center of attention. Or do you feel left out in the cold or immune to praise? If this quality is lacking in you then its time to gently reveal your qualities that make you the ruler. If this quality is overflowing, then restraint is necessary so that spotlight may be shared by the deserving others too."}],"house":5,"houseName":"House of Children","houseMeaning":"Affairs of the heart, children, love affairs, adventures, exciting activities, speculations","yearNumber":8},"crystals":"Citrine, Topaz, Tourmaline","gems":"Diamond, Garnet","keywords":["Self Control","Fortitude","Spiritual Strength","Patience","Self Mastery"],"tone":null,"img":"08-Strength.png"},{"name":"The Hermit","num":9,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":105,"end":107,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Wise old man","Task":"Retreating into oneself, appropriate seriousness, contemplation","Element":"EARTH","Crystal Guidance":"Kyanite, Peridot","Color Guidance":"Gray"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"An old man, with a long white beard is dressed in grim Colored clothes, with his head bent in deep contemplation. The robe is hooded and is bound at the waist by a knotted cord. He is walking alone, lit only by a lamp. This represents the need for introspection to to walk one’s own path, following one’s own light."},{"t":"p","x":"This card refers to the need for the individual to shut out all external voices and noises and to deeply attune to the Silence of the self."},{"t":"p","x":"Sometimes our analytical and intuitive abilities which are in fact best guides for our soul growth get lost in the noises of the increasing socialization processes we are captured by. This card advises is to go back to our solitude self and rely upon the internal voice of wisdom that will bubble up when we focus on hearing it in silence."},{"t":"p","x":"The road to solitude can be unnerving for some, as signified by the barrenness of the white icy cliffs the Hermit is treading on. However this ice is full of purity and a beautiful example of untouched Nature."},{"t":"p","x":"The Hermit is also a card of self-initiation but on an interior level where we are undistracted and take time to gauge where we have been as individuals, where we stand at present and how all our actions will determine the course of our future. The lantern that the Hermit carries in his hand is his internal light, one he must light and then depend upon to tread the road less travelled. The Hermit has no fancy robes or adornments. He is dressed very simply, almost inconspicuous in his Colorless robes. His ego is overthrown and he is one with his Inner Voice. This card shows that solitude and being away from the temptations of civilisations are as much as a search of God and more importantly to find own inner balance."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes in a reading, it is time to be a beacon of light for yourself and if need be, for others. The staff in the Hermit's hand introduces you as wise person, capable of deep contemplation of an issue and being a support system for others in need."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside the Hermit may indicate fraud and deception, lies, miscommunication, misinformation, concealment."},{"t":"p","x":"The Hermit is in search for truth in its pure form, uncorrupted by the ideologies of the self-serving world. Its time to re-evaluate your life. There is little that is comfortable about this card and sometimes the skeletons of your weaknesses may come popping out. This cleansing, its necessary and soul purifying. Detox of the Soul."}],"id":"the-hermit","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Desire to mingle with outside world Superficial way of decision making, without much research Time for team work and collaborative efforts Confused person who is naive and listens to others’ opinions rather than trusting own judgement. Ignoring the truth and change it will bring. Turning away from others who need your counselling"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Virgo","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Virgo is reclusive and critical and often goes deep into analysis when confronted by a situation or an issue. It is also discriminating and detail oriented. When you draw the Hermit ask yourself if you are being too self-critical or critical of others. Are you making too many demands on yourself or others? Its time to turn inwards"}],"house":6,"houseName":"House of Health & Work","houseMeaning":"Job, service, competition, diseases, victory over enemy, responsibilities, mundane work, daily habits","yearNumber":9},"crystals":"Peridot, Bloodstone","gems":"Blue Sapphire, Hessonite (Gomedh)","keywords":["Isolation","Deep Study","Introspection","Wisdom","Inner Counsel","Celibacy"],"tone":null,"img":"09-TheHermit.png"},{"name":"Wheel of Fortune","num":10,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":107,"end":110,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Calling","Task":"Insight into what is necessary, facing one’s task","Element":"FIRE","Crystal Guidance":"Yellow Sapphire, Yellow topaz","Color Guidance":"Golden"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Wheel of Fortune is a wonderful card of unexpected opportunities. It symbolises the forces of Chance and Destiny in all its splendour as well as confusions. It signifies that the Universe is granting us miraculous opportunities to grow and expand to our full potential. Dark times are behind us and the postals of good fortune are benevolently smiling upon us. It is card of new beginnings, new ventures,movement, vision and good fortune. Like the wheel which is constantly moving, this card advises us to keep moving on the path of life. Its a card of higher learning and constantly upgrading our skills. The more we learn about various aspects of life, the more the doors of opportunities open before us and we are ready and equipped to take on the challenges that might come in our life as SYNCHRONICITY (related events happening in a sequence such that life takes a major step forward). The imagery of the Wheel of Fortune shows a massive wheel whose axle is supported by two uprights. There are 3 layers to the wheel which signify the physical, mental and spiritual dimensions of the human life. The spokes in the wheel indicate need for balance in life. The sphinx (half man half lion figure from Egyptian mythology) epitomizes the perfect balance once achieved between the good and evil within us makes us masters of the wheel of time and we can run the course of time as per our intentions."},{"t":"p","x":"The imagery also reflects the four fixed signs of Taurus, Leo, Scorpio and Aquarius displaying the various qualities needed to move on the road of expansion. All the figures are holding books indicating the need for knowledge, ancient and new, to capture the short lived opportunities that come knocking at our door. The salamander, a reptile signifies upwards movement of luck and the snake correspondingly talks of the inevitable downside in the cyclical wheel of Time. We are all connected with the Wheel of Fortune. Some are travelling upwards while others are facing down times while some have mastered the time and remain relatively unaffected by its vagaries. This card is hugely positive in the Tarot language and indicates promotions and success, money windfall gains, love and happiness in relationships and big strides in spiritual evolution, amongst other gains it can bring into your life."},{"t":"p","x":"But the wheel is turning for everyone. The Wheel spares no one and rewards no one. Its impartial and just echoes the primordial ethos of life that CHANGE IS CONSTANT. When this card appears in a spread, be prepared for big positive changes. They will require you to come out of your comfort zone and be proactive. The opportunity will come out of the blue literally but the preparation to capitalize on it has to be human. Your life is being affected by these changes and if you want success, you have to fight to take control of the uncontrollable."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside, the Wheel of fortune can bring in unexpected bad luck, rigid attitude towards change, stagnation in professional and personal matters. The WOF is an incredibly powerful card full of potential to understand the meaning of life and to align your personal energies with the greater life plan that Destiny has in mind for you. It decides your Future and you must take control of your life while the wheel is turning else you will be compelled to stay plateaued and stationary in your present."}],"id":"wheel-of-fortune","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Unexpected turn of events not always fortunate Delays, hindrances, recurring problems and setbacks Complications arising that were not foreseen Difficulty to adjust to change Destiny playing a hand and a situation not much in your control"}],"astro":{"planet":"Jupiter","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Wheel of Fortune tells you take advantage of unexpected or new opportunities. Be aware and vigilant and constantly upgrade yourself to stay relevant. Refrain: Let go of that which pulls you down, Refrain from hanging onto lower forces and develop yourself intellectually. Do not be pessimistic and wait for your time to change for the better."}]},"crystals":"Lapis Lazuli, Amethyst, Aventurine","gems":"Blue Sapphire","keywords":["Unexpected Turn","Expansion","New Horizons","Dame Fortune","A Change","Cycles Of Life"],"tone":null,"img":"10-WheelOfFortune.png"},{"name":"Justice","num":11,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":110,"end":113,"meta":{"Archetype":"Intelligence","Task":"Understanding the laws of this world, passing an intelligent and balanced judgement, personal courage","Element":"AIR","Crystal Guidance":"Blue Sapphire, Lapis Lazuli","Color Guidance":"Dark Blue"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Justice Card represents the Law of Karma, and the victory of righteousness and good conduct in the wheel of life. Its one of the cards of the Major Arcana whose title is succinct. As its name suggests, it indicates the need for fair play. The Goddess of Justice is seated on a throne resplendent in the red power robes indicating she is in a official capacity (granted by her status or her destined role) to take a balanced and judicious decision."},{"t":"p","x":"The sword in one hand and the scales in the other are indicating that the decision needs to be based on facts and evidence, It should be the result of intellectual analytics. It should not be driven by personal ego or emotional factors. Fairness should be the deciding factor above all else. When a situation to make a decision comes in our life, we should not jump to presumptions. We should not be quick to judge situations and people. What has happened is a cause and effect of a particular pattern and we as Justice bearer must understand the nuances and undercurrents of a situation before passing a verdict. Unlike the Lady Justice in modern times, the imagery in the Justice card has the Goddess of Justice with eyes wide open. It describes impartiality and an open mind while reviewing all the aspects of situation under analysis and making the judgement."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears in a reading, you must adopt a systematic approach towards the situation under scrutiny. This task will require all your wits and sincere efforts, It advises you to be disciplined and balanced in your approach. Consider the pros and cons, both of the situation, in case a new project or enterprise or relationship is being considered. How the situation can benefit you and how it can harm you must both be considered in detail before embarking on a new step. Do not be swayed by emotional tides or become a victim of emotional manipulation by the parties involved in the task. Use your own intelligence and analyse the facts form all angles and then decide. Literally the appearance of this card indicates an upcoming litigation, court proceedings, contracts and settlements in your life. If a litigation case has been underway, it calls for swift verdict in the recent future. In case you have been righteous in your karma, then the verdict would surely be in your favour."},{"t":"p","x":"This card is a card of Karmic balance and eulogizes the basic Hindu philosophy of karma being a pivot of cause and effect. If the input has been on the right path, then the rewards shall ensue while if the karmic intentions have been flawed, then the punishments would be swift and justified. On the downside, this card indicates injustice and legal confusion, imbalance in the activities of life, the ambiguity regarding what is right code of conduct, losses in legal cases, false implications and being dragged into law and order situations by external agencies, The Justice Card is a shoutout to all for maintaining Balance and Objectivity in Life. Karma gets its payback, sooner rather than later and one must be cognizant at all times of acting out of fairness and impartiality and applying moderation in life-situations."}],"id":"justice","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Lack of analytical ability and putting blame on situation or just one party Legal or emotional justice denied Need to act out of habit and question the “how” and “why” of a situation Extreme or unfair behaviour Unbalanced decision / poor judgement"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Libra","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Libra seeks balance and diplomacy. If this energy is strong for you now, too much compromise means you are giving up on your own beliefs or opinions just to make others happy. If you believe it is lacking, learn diplomacy to resolve a dilemma and be more civilized about life. Justice seeks to find balance between contrasting aspects of life."},{"t":"p","x":"Use patience, tact and analytical mind to get to root of the problem and then work upon the Truth so found, to bring fairness to the situation."}],"house":7,"houseName":"House of Marriage and open conflict","houseMeaning":"Marriage, lawsuits, partnerships, marital sex life, known enemies, business transactions"},"crystals":"Bloodstone, Jade, Carnelian","gems":"Emerald, Opal","keywords":["Legal Affairs","Karmic Balance","Cause And Effect Laws","Decision","Judgement"],"tone":null,"img":"11-Justice.png"},{"name":"The Hanged Man","num":12,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":113,"end":115,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Test","Task":"Changing one’s way, Insights and willingness to make a sacrifice","Element":"WATER","Crystal Guidance":"Beryl, Sodalite","Color Guidance":"Brown"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Hanged Man carries a vivid and interesting image of a noble looking, mature man hanging upside down from a tree branch. His left leg is bent in a yogic position and the right leg is fastened to the tree. His arms are tied behind his back. The trees are lush and the face of the Hanged Man is aglow with a brilliant radiance of halo around it. This is a special card and a special milestone in the Fool’s Journey on the path of Truth. Its embedded deep in philosophy and lessons one needs to tarry and absorb in order to become a finer version of our human self."},{"t":"p","x":"The point to observe here is that the Hanged Man shows no signs of distress at his uncomfortable position and infact has flexibly adjusted himself in a way that his body is in perfect symmetry to the surrounding environment. His face has a peaceful expression and even carries a hint of inner delight. He is in contemplation and an inner satisfaction radiates on his face as he faces the ordeal with a grace that will grant him a gain or goal he secretly aspires for. This card represents self sacrifice and martyrdom. It shows that in life there will be a necessity to bear flexibility of mind and let go of one’s preconceived ideas and to accept limitations with an open mind and heart. The Hanged Man is a\"Transformative” card teaching us that giving up something we cherish is needed at particular juncture in life in order to gain something more valuable."},{"t":"p","x":"The Hanged Man at first study, might seem like a gray card showing us limitations and constraints. However, when studied in the deeper perspective, its the time to become more holistic in your thinking. It warns against becoming biased or prejudiced. If in conflict with someone, this card is very meaningful as it tells you to rise above your very human emotions and do what is best for everyone concerned. The Hanged Man observes from the other person’s perspective and become more broad based and universal in his understanding of this world. The Hanged Man usually involves some form of compromise of one;s own desires for the sake of benefit of someone else. It may involve a choice and you may be asked to renounce something or someone that’s dear to you."},{"t":"p","x":"The downside of the card could bring up selfishness, self interested behaviour, political machinations, loss of something you want or need. The point is that the Hanged Man’s choice must be yours; and the sacrifice must be made willingly. Its that important milestone where the EGO must be renounced as we are initiated to become more immersed with higher matters. In the Major Arcana journey, from now onwards the cards will focus on cosmic qualities and reflect the movement into higher dimensions of the human soul, leaving the petty and lower concerns of the human existence behind."}],"id":"the-hanged-man","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Over confidence and arrogant behaviour Lack of receptivity Lack of sensitivity and indifference to what other party feels or wants Fear of social conventions or penal action Being inflexible to changes and continuing to be adamant Being stuck to a particular idea or person though it has become non-useful for growth"}],"astro":{"planet":"Neptune","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Hanged Man resonates to the Uranus planet and tells you that it is time to relinquish your attachment to things or people, which serve no purpose to you."},{"t":"p","x":"Change is inevitable and the only constant of life so accept the moving wheel of change and learn to let go and move on."},{"t":"p","x":"Life is filled with other beautiful colors so live your life and enjoy the Divinity in each particle of creation."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain: Do not get so deeply involved with people or things that even when it no longer serves your growth, yo continue to cling on due to insecurity. Take action to let go. The Neptunian element of fatalism that brings stagnation, must be avoided."}]},"crystals":"Beryl, Ametrine, Sodalite","gems":"Blue Sapphire, Blue Hakik","keywords":["Act of Sacrifice","Unconventional Behaviour","Surrender","Flexible Thinking"],"tone":null,"img":"12-TheHangedMan.png"},{"name":"Death","num":13,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":115,"end":117,"meta":{"Archetype":"Death","Task":"Leave taking and descent into the underworld, Withdrawing, Separating","Element":"WATER","Crystal Guidance":"Black Tourmaline, Ametrine","Color Guidance":"Slate Gray"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"In many decks the DEATH card is depicted as a skeleton with a scythe. In Rider Waite Death is riding a white horse with the Flag of Death fluttering in the night sky. The figure of the skeleton, seated atop the horse is grinning, sometimes appearing angry or vengeful."},{"t":"p","x":"The scene is littered with dead bodies while a few symbols of life like a couple of children a holy priest are asking for redemption. Far at the horizon, the bleakness of the scene is cleaved by a pale Sun struggling to find its radiance. The Death card is Absolute and symbolizes a complete severance from the past. A certain aspect of life is undeniably dead and will never again live in the capacity it used to. It could be the death of a relationship, of a career, of a business, of a certain lifestyle or even an old way of thinking or behaviour. An end of old ties and associations. A crossing over from one mode of existence to another."},{"t":"p","x":"Generally this card will entail some loss but it would be a loss that has reached its organic expiry date and needs to either end or be rebirthed in a new form or a higher dimension. For this purpose the Death card is regarded as the TRANSFORMATION or REBIRTH card rather than merely the Death attribute. Its a time of creative destruction and remind of the Tandava of Lord Shiva, the dance of cosmic Resurrection. Some endings are necessary. Unavoidable."},{"t":"p","x":"The lesson is to pick up the teachings from the loss or ending, understand the larger picture of what the future vision entails and then creating with hope and tenderness a new world. Ask Mercy for the sins committed in the past which led to the painful endings. Be innocent and trusting like the children in the imagery whose future can be moulded in any way the higher thinking dictates."},{"t":"p","x":"Death tells you to clear the deadwood in your own life so something new can grow. You may be called to make radical and sweeping changes When this card appears in a reading, a major change is about to happen in your life. Good or Bad, it cannot be avoided. On the downside and this card can be considered one of the darker shades of Gray in the Deck. It spells destruction, Loss, Failure of Plans, Apathy, Loss of Hope This Card is a message of deep Transformations and far reaching changes that could impact the remainder of your life. The Death like experience will leave a profound effect on you and you will emerge from the cocoon to become the Butterfly that the Divine Plan wants you to be."}],"id":"death","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Sense of stagnation and procrastination Life comes to a standstill Philosophical attitude to life as you understand the power of Time and how it will pass on Inability to change and make a fresh start Clinging to old patterns of behaviour, or old situation no longer valid Undergoing pain and dealing with it - physical, emotional"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Scorpio","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Scorpio is about passion and power. When you draw Death, the astrological aspect of this card is the power to Transform your life. To end one cycle that is not working for you and begin again. Life moves in cyclical pattern and the Death card guides on not being fixated in or wallowing in the past; not to hold grudges and to have the power to reinvent and move on. If this energy, you feel, is lacking, check that you are not wielding power just for the sake of it."}],"house":8,"houseName":"House of Death","houseMeaning":"Legacies, death, taxes and partner’s money, spiritual knowledge"},"crystals":"Bloodstone, Amber","gems":"","keywords":["Transformation","Ending","a New Beginning","Life-Lesson","Hope"],"tone":null,"img":"13-Death.png"},{"name":"Temperance","num":14,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":117,"end":120,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Soul Guide","Task":"Trusting the higher guidance, finding the right mixture","Element":"FIRE","Crystal Guidance":"Amethyst, Kunzite","Color Guidance":"Green"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Temperance card depicts an angel balancing two forces. Dressed in pure white and protective wings, the Angelic presence has his right foot in the stream of water and his left foot on earthy threshold. He has two chalices in his hands and with full concentration and enjoyment he is creating a blend of the two liquids such that the most conducive temperature of the blend is reached."},{"t":"p","x":"The yellow triangle on the chest of the Angel symbolizes fire and the flowering blooms all around in his habitat are messengers of abundance and divine governance. These symbols indicate that for abundance to come through, the right proportion of conflicting or contrasting variables must be sought with patience and focus. The Temperance is the card for Harmony, Moderation and Circumspection. It calls for qualities of cooperation and collaboration to come through. A very beneficial card, the Temperance indicates the blessings of the Angels in your life and that your environment is harmonious for your growth and development. Temperance card tells you to find balance and equilibrium in our life. Most of the challenges in our life consist of choices that are not only wise but also should be palatable to responsibly incur them for a long time. These call for constant adjustment in our inner values as also our outward speech and behaviour. Harmony in relationships, a peaceful and calm mind, empathy and patience to listen to the other person and trying to sync your energy with theirs for an amicable working and living environment, are all the indicators for a smoother life that the Temperance card offers as tools. This is also a warning image that any decision taken rapidly or on an impulse can lead to your destruction. It also portends the arrival of a saviour or a wonderful life guide who will bring you out of the darkness of your dilemmas into the light of knowledge and a successful life."},{"t":"p","x":"The card may describe someone who will be a positive influence on you. There may be a helpful friend or a compassionate mentor or counsellor. Temperance teaches the human mind that one can make constructive use of the time that situations simply ask us to wait for the maturation of the outcome. You use these times to consider your actions of the past, explore your own needs and motives, and to let the learnings be assimilated into the psyche."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside, the card can bring up messages of disharmony, competing interests, unfortunate alliances, hormonal imbalances, lopsided collaborative ventures, neglect of health and well being, inability to balance work and home life, imbalanced budgets, inability to balance materialistic and spiritual dimensions of life as one may take precedence. Being receptive to new experiments, being cautious and testing the waters before making a commitment and maintaining your Equipoise in the face of problems are central themes of this 14th card of the Major Arcana reflecting on the inherent energy of Number 5 for balance and communication between contrasting energies."}],"id":"temperance","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Need to act and take pro active actions No time to test the waters and make calibrated judgement Swift decision making Overspending of energy or not putting in enough efforts Lack of adjusting quality Problems in professional and personal life due to communication blockage"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Sagittarius","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Sagittarius is optimistic and explorative."},{"t":"p","x":"When you draw Temperance, you have the opportunity to work on your desires and take the road towards achieving your goals. The flexibility of the Temperance card to be open to various avenues to get to the goal is its strength. So is the constant quest for perfection just like a Sagittarius native."},{"t":"p","x":"If you identify too easily with this energy, then its time to slow down and moderate your plans. Rethink and re-formulate before rushing headlong into something new."}],"house":9,"houseName":"House of Philosophy and Religion","houseMeaning":"Law, philosophy, religion, ideals, higher education, long distance travel, learning we do out of willingness"},"crystals":"Amethyst, Kunzite, Sardonyx","gems":"Opal, Diamond","keywords":["Equilibrium","Adjustment","Balance","Partnership","Good Prospects"],"tone":null,"img":"14-Temperance.png"},{"name":"The Devil","num":15,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":120,"end":123,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Adversary","Task":"Overcoming inner resistance, Insight into unlived shadow aspects, Taking back projections","Element":"EARTH","Crystal Guidance":"Obsidian, Haemetite","Color Guidance":"Black"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Devil is a dark card of the Tarot Deck and totals to Number 6 being the 15th Major Arcana. Its an anti-thesis of the pure synergistic energies of Card Number 6, the Lovers. The Devil is depicted in animalistic form, often as a combination of animals. The Rider Waite shows Satan or a Satanic prototype with huge curved horns towering devilishly over a naked male and female couple who are seen bound in chains. They both have chains wrapped loosely around their necks yet it is obvious that they could easily slip these off and run away. So why have they not done so?.This is the crux of the message that the Devil contains, and it is not always an easy question to answer. If you feel trapped in a chaotic and stressful job that offers no rise for you, you may decide it is better to stay put because atleast you know what you are dealing with. The comfort zone induces in you a kind of lethargy that makes you unable to slip off your chains and look for a better opportunity outside."},{"t":"p","x":"If you are estranged from someone and unhappy about it, you may be adamant that you will not make the first move because the entire situation is the other person’s fault and it is up to them to apologise for it. However the Devil is reminding you that you need to examine your own role in what has transpired and to break free from the imprisonment of your self defeating attitudes."},{"t":"p","x":"The Devil has no links to black magic or voodoo. Its appearance in a spread does not mean the presence of witchcraft. Occasionally it can mean that the querist may be the target or victim of extreme negative energy but the surrounding cards must be studied deeply in that context. Extreme ambition and greed may be on your mind when the Devil pops up. This is displayed by the Pentacles sign on the forehead of the Devil. Any fixation with material assets and becoming ruthless in your pursuit of it is an associated attribute of this Card energy."},{"t":"p","x":"The Devil is more the victory of vices within self than virtues. There is a feeling of being trapped in a situation and inability to break free. However abject the conditions, the human mind and human spirit are capable of courage and this card calls forth to draw upon the inner sense of liberation. There are many addictions to which we all are prey and which operate in more subtle ways. You might be drawn to relationships in which you are always compelled to play the subservient role. This subtle abuse has become your second nature and even though the severity of the abuse might increase, you would have fear and apathy to moving out. You are addicted to your own negative patterns and will not move out of the chains holding you, when needed."},{"t":"p","x":"You could be so used to playing the victim and and basking in other people’s sympathy or playing on the harp of self sympathy that you do not know how to break out of the vicious circle and assert yourself. The Devil card constantly tells us to break out of destructive boundaries and become aware of what is going on and what you can do about it constructively."},{"t":"p","x":"On the downside, the Devil spells excesses and addictions, unethical and illegal behaviors, obsessive thoughts about a person or object, jealousy, lust, crimes and violence. In special cases regarding non commitment, this card may indicate that the connection between two persons in destined and they will keep coming back to each other. The bond of commitment is visible here."},{"t":"p","x":"The Devil can be a life changing card in the reading because it highlights the depth of a problem and that extreme determination may be needed to set yourself free and move to a natural state of divine existence where each human soul is free of bondage of self and others."}],"id":"the-devil","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Sense of liberation as a problem disappears Ending of an addictive pattern Ending of an abusive relationship Professional expansion and willing to move jobs or domains. Resisting temptation Hard work being more important than personal pleasure"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Capricorn","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Capricorn is self-reliant and conventional."},{"t":"p","x":"The Devil card is deeply connected with the Capricorn tendancies to be obsessed about its self interest and ambitious goals. It makes them too conventional and narrow minded about own modus-operandi and way of perceiving the world. Its unhealthy and myopic at times."},{"t":"p","x":"If you draw the Devil card this attribute may be surplus in your life and you need to let go of an obsessive habit or way of doing things. If you feel this energy is lacking then maybe its time to adhere to certain conventions and discipline yourself to achieve your goals without harming those around you."}],"house":10,"houseName":"House of Profession","houseMeaning":"Public life, social status, profession, ambition, fame, the father, honors, social responsibility"},"crystals":"Obsidian, Amethyst, Jet Stone","gems":"Moonstone, White Coral","keywords":["Material Desires","Obsession","Lust","Avarice","Bondage"],"tone":null,"img":"15-TheDevil.png"},{"name":"The Tower","num":16,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":123,"end":125,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Liberation","Task":"Bursting boundaries that are too narrow, Breaking out of the outdated","Element":"FIRE","Crystal Guidance":"Chrysocolla, Haemetite","Color Guidance":"Brown"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Tower card is rather dramatic looking and shows a stone fortress or a light house being struck by lightening from the Heavens. The top of the Tower is sheared off, and the tower is falling to pieces. Fire rages in the background. Two figures are seen falling from the tower towards the ground. They could represent two male figures or a male and female."},{"t":"p","x":"The most famous story from History that corresponds to this imagery is the Fall of the Tower of Babel, They wanted to control the world as a splendidly unified force but had to face God’s wrath and feel to their decline. Simply constructing a heaven-reaching edifice and presuming you are all powerful sooner or later will lead to Fall from Grace and the eventual downfall of the conceited. If you are tempted by the possibility of ruling the world instead of striving for wisdom and spiritual humility, you will lose all you gained."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a gross misuse of the blessing of Free Will. The Falling Tower represents losses and painful endings. The one striking feature of this card is that the Loss will be unexpected and shocking. It could be a loss in relationship, material losses, loss of prestige or achievements."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a card f violent changes of and destruction, of falling apart and leaving the person disoriented and seeking guidance and succour. In the Eastern mythology, it is matched by the destructive rage power of the Kali, who makes space for the new beginnings to grow. She is born when the darkness(of the soul; of the karmas) has grown suffocating and all pervasive and needs to be swept away in a radical manner."},{"t":"p","x":"Though the changes that this Card energy brings is shocking and upsetting, yet it is necessary for the restructuring. When the dust has settled and more understanding of why it happened has entered the querist’s mind, it would be satisfying to redesign your life in a more orderly manner with stronger foundations. The Devil is strongly about the mind and the idea of self perceptions. When this energy strikes, there might be loss of how a person perceives himself or any other. The fall from exaltation and the resultant reality checks are significant steps to march towards the Truth."},{"t":"p","x":"Since this card describes loss of image and embarrassment, it features prominently when professional life is on the downswing, asking for concrete changes in direction and planning. Relationships going astray due to infidelity are characterized by the Tower card. Political loss of face, failure in competitive exams, poor appraisal ratings, demotions, public insults and disgrace can occur when this Card energy is about to strike. This card will bring out the skeletons from the closet and make you face the harsh truth and realign your life on more authentic terms. The edifice is only as strong as the Foundation, whether of the self or an institution or of a relationship."}],"id":"the-tower","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Ending of a troublesome period Pain and problems becoming less severe Recovery / improvement in health situation Repressed emotions Blockage in expressing real feelings leading to confusion or stress Sweet talking and sychophancy"}],"astro":{"planet":"Mars","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Tower tells you that it is the time to shake up the status quo. Get rid of old perceptions, or toxic relationships or wasteful habits. Bring a new lease of freshness into your life and do not be afraid of Change."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain: Do not act explosive or impulsive."},{"t":"p","x":"Assess the situation before making a breakthrough. Use your judicious mind, and not just volatile feelings."}]},"crystals":"Chrysocolla, Obsidian","gems":"Ruby, Garnet","keywords":["Crash of Expectations","Necessary Change","Unfulfilled Expectations","Shocking News"],"tone":null,"img":"16-TheTower.png"},{"name":"The Star","num":17,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":125,"end":128,"meta":{"Archetype":"Wisdom","Task":"Gaining hope. Vision of new future","Element":"AIR","Crystal Guidance":"Sugilite, Turquoise","Color Guidance":"Yellow"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Star card is 17th card of the Major Arcana and is a card of renewal, healing and optimism. Its a card of divine blessings and is a very auspicious omen for any new beginnings. The imagery shows a naked lady bending down on her knees and creating channels of irrigation from the oasis in the desert. She is holding two pitchers, one in each hand, from which she is emptying the water. She dips into the eternal water source on one hand and uses it to fertilize the ground around her. Some of that water is going back to the original source. Above her head are stars, seven in number, arranged in a halo like effect and encircling a big yellow star. This is a celestial configuration and denotes her divine mission on Earth which allows her to dream big and gives her the inner light and vision to manifest it into reality. Astrology teaches us that stars influence our lives and our thoughts and dreams. The North Star has since times ancient, been the guiding light for the travellers to find their way."},{"t":"p","x":"The stars represent the universe in all its mystery and potential for growth, learning and power.The Stars show the opportunity the emancipated human mind can have to chart the course of history and leave a long lasting legacy."},{"t":"p","x":"The background shows an open landscape, which is conducive for abundant results. Its not yet lush and would require sustained and patient efforts to develop by the human figure in the picture."},{"t":"p","x":"The singing birds and the green tree indicate that the results will be fruitful and regenerative in nature."},{"t":"p","x":"The central theme of this card is to return to the source a portion of the blessings that the human has been given. The Star is a incredibly powerful card, pregnant with infinite possibilities. What the Magician in stage 1 was only imagining, the Star now puts you into the exalted status where the stars are aligning themselves to help you on your mission. Its a card of sure-shot success, long lasting fame and deep impact on the heart and minds of history."},{"t":"p","x":"But to gain and retain this power, you must put something back. The lady in the picture is pouring the life force, back into the earth element, even as the skies above are aligning in her favour."},{"t":"p","x":"The beginning of a transformation is near; and this card always brings positive news and good tidings."},{"t":"p","x":"The Star reflects upon our need for having faith in the signals of the Universe and be open to inspiration and guidance, and about having hope in dark places. As a card of fortune, this is beneficial and fortuitous and speaks of God gently guiding us through the bleakness or doubts into a space of clarity. There may be prophetic dreams and omens associated when this card appears in the reading. It advises us to be sensitive to such subtle signals and be in our receptive dimension. For success questions, this Card is very fortunate as it celebrates the inner talents and richness of our personality. Great appreciaiton or felicitation might follow when this card appears."},{"t":"p","x":"The Star appears to be unattainable yet this symbolizes your innermost hopes and aspirations. What the world may seem to find impossible, if you in your deepest core find to be attainable, the Star will give you the divine guidance to work against the odds and the hardships. The only cosmic condition is that you follow the divine signals, your intuition and a deep abiding confidence in the power of the Self. At its downside the Star may portend loss of fame, unfulfilled expectations, frustration and impotence."},{"t":"p","x":"At its best, the Star promises immortality, leaving behind material or intellectual legacy, progress towards goals, connection with the Divine, success in daunting tasks, spiritual enlightenment."}],"id":"the-star","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Loss of optimism and cheerfulness Depression and feeling demotivated in the heart Purposeless life and no desire to contribute to society Focusing on past pains and unable to express negative emotions. No emotional clearing Talent not getting recognition Loss of fame and goodwill"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Aquarius","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Aquarius is idealistic and independent. When you draw the Star and you feel this energy is lacking in your life, its time to believe in yourself. Trust your inner voice and be resilient to doing things your way. The destination may seem far fetched but your self-reliance and the blessings of the heavens that the Star card manifests will give you resounding success. If you identify too readily with this independent energy, then take care that you are not trying to influence others without a thought for their personal needs."}],"house":11,"houseName":"House of Hopes and Wishes","houseMeaning":"Friends, associates, groups, hopes, wishes, aspiration, public festivals"},"crystals":"Sugilite, Moldavite, Turquoise","gems":"Red Coral","keywords":["Solace","Sustained Hard Work","a Gift","Universal Blessing","Insight","Optimism"],"tone":null,"img":"17-TheStar.png"},{"name":"The Moon","num":18,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":128,"end":131,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Night, Daybreak","Task":"The Tightrope walk, cautiously overcoming the threshold of fear,not getting lost or losing oneself","Element":"WATER","Crystal Guidance":"Selenite, Labradorite","Color Guidance":"Aquamarine"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Moon is the 18th card of the Major Arcana and a rather mystical and mysterious one, just like the unfathomable extent of the Mystic Number 9."},{"t":"p","x":"The Moon is shown in both its full and crescent form.There is a face in the Moon, on the left side of the crescent, looking down at the scene below. There are tear shaped rays around the Moon falling from the Moon onto the Earth below, symbolizing the descent of spirit into matter."},{"t":"p","x":"Its interesting to observe that the crescent and the disc is a very old representation of the moon deity. Ancient steles from the Mideast, inscribed in Aramaic show this Lunar symbol as also this imagery is found in excavations of ancient North Africa. This is evidence of the Tarot symbolism, especially the Major Arcana having its archaeological roots to much older than the fourteenth century European culture."},{"t":"p","x":"There is the recurring portal theme of the Tarot in the form of the twin pillars. Two animals are represented here, a wolf and a dog, positioned between the towers and howling up at the Moon. They represent our pagan, animal nature. They are are both in fear and awe of the effects of the Moon, ever affected by it rather than controlling it."},{"t":"p","x":"The bottom of the imagery shows a pool or lake from which is climbing out a clinging lobster or a scorpion. The watery depths denote our subconscious, the deepest part of our emotional self."},{"t":"p","x":"Water is again represented as the life force(as in the Star card) but in this allegory, its also full of unknown and serendipitous dangers, lurking in the shadowy depths. The Moon is our\"Chitta” and stores all the remembered and forgotten impressions through our soul journey."},{"t":"p","x":"The central message of the Moon is that the moonlight plays tricks on us because it alters the appearance of the surrounding environment. In this flavour, its been compared with the abstruse and mystical lights of the underwaters where nothing is as what is seems to be. We are not entirely sure what we are looking at."},{"t":"p","x":"When the Moon appears in a reading, its a complex signal to look at situation in the true light. You are reluctant to acknowledge the truth. It could be because all the facts are not yet revealed before you; more mysteries and clues have to be unfolded before you can grasp the entire picture. It could be due to your latent fears and anxieties that you are sceptical of facing the facts and welcoming clarity into your life."},{"t":"p","x":"Deliberately certain persons around you might be trying to emotionally blackmail you or put a blindfold over your analytical acumen."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a time to be wary and on your guard when the Moon energy is surrounding you in the Tarot."},{"t":"p","x":"The Moon card is tricky and guides you towards the murkiness in the situation. People will not be truthful or will hide the information from you. It will be difficult to decipher what their real intentions are. As the Moon tarot card is the link between our subconscious and the conscious mind, it can refer to all that is concealed and secretive in our life."},{"t":"p","x":"Secrets and fears that you have been trying to push to the back of your mind may start to emerge unbidden, forcing you to confront them."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a favourable card for any creative, poetic, literary and psychological activity and venture. It advises us to explore our subconscious and be confident of our own emotional strengths and to use them to sift through the chaff and come up with the golden grain of reality."},{"t":"p","x":"Its our ability to translate emotions, moods and repressions into the light of our life."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears, pay close attention to your Intuition and the dreamscape. Its giving you strong signals on where the truth lies. Constantly scan your environment for clues on what will help you maneuver the ambiguity surrounding you and to emerge from the murky depths of the emotional cesspool where the dangerous scorpions lurk, waiting to devour you."}],"id":"the-moon","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Will power becoming stronger and desire to be active in material world."},{"t":"p","x":"Clarity in mind after an ambiguous time."},{"t":"p","x":"Time of trust and new networking Calmness and feeling centered."},{"t":"p","x":"Renewal of positivity in a troublesome relationship or life situation Positive card in health and finance situation"}],"astro":{"zodiac":"Pisces","zodiacText":[{"t":"p","x":"Pisces is impressionable and deeply emotional, If you draw the Moon card feel this energy is surplus then you are living in an illusory world of feelings and mental fluctuations. You are being misled by what people around you are saying or making you believe, Do not be so gullible, You could even be beset by doubts and uncertainties to a very large extent. See beyond the empty promises."},{"t":"p","x":"If you believe this energy is lacking in your life then its time to be more in touch with your Intuition and feelings."}],"house":12,"houseName":"House of Bondage","houseMeaning":"Personal limitations, secret desires, frustrated ambitions, unknown enemies, institutions that restrict or confine, karmic lessons, what we know subconsciously, where we escape to, expenditures, losses"},"crystals":"Moonstone, Selenite","gems":"White Sapphire","keywords":["Insight","Organic Change","Hidden Currents","Ambiguity","Distrust"],"tone":null,"img":"18-TheMoon.png"},{"name":"The Sun","num":19,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":131,"end":134,"meta":{"Archetype":"The Day, the Rosy Dawn","Task":"True Reconciliation","Element":"FIRE","Crystal Guidance":"Tiger’s Eye, Bloodstone","Color Guidance":"Bright Yellow"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Sun is the Nineteenth Trump of the Major Arcana and like the numerological counterpart of Number 1, it is the most positive and radiant card of the deck. The Sun is the centre of the solar system and is integral to the continuation of life on this planet. The Sun represents our inner life force, our vitality. Without it, our planet will cease to exist. It will be a mere lump of molten mass, devoid of life and hurtling through darkness. Similarly, the Sun card in the Tarot is its brightest illumination. When the SUN appears in a spread as a person, it shows they bring you happiness, contentment and encouragement. The Sun represents Love and succour. It is essential for our survival. When it disappears from our life, its as if the light has gone out of our life. This is the primary lesson of the milestone card of the Sun. While it represents love, in its pure and unaffected form, it also warns us of co-dependance on a person or a passion to an extent that when we are bereft of them, we cease to live productively."},{"t":"p","x":"The Sun is the lowest aspect of the Divine and the highest aspect of the mundane. It serves as a mediator between the visible light of this world and the divine light."},{"t":"p","x":"How do you combine your own sovereignty (Sun energy symbolizes individuality) while opening yourself to divine light? This question is central to the Sun card when it has been appearing in your spread or Daily Guidance.. Let the Mind expand and Open. Hold the Dream of what brings you JOY? Keep holding it and let its brilliant light enter your Mind to an extent that each muscle is filled with its fulfillment. This is the message of this card-Of envisioning and then continually reflecting on the idea and aligning all your thoughts and actions towards it coming true. The Sun is about making your dream come true."},{"t":"p","x":"The Sun is the most joyful card of the Tarot deck representing happiness, laughter, success, generosity of heart, spontaneity. It can also represent the birth of something joyful whether it is a child, a new relationship, a marriage or a work project that will offer us growth and excitement. If this card springs up when you are going through a difficult time in life, it brings with it massages of hope and recovery of good times. In relationships, this is a very positive card as it talks of times of total and transparent communication. Even if there have been misunderstandings or conflicts in the past, the partners will enter a new phase of understanding the other’s perspective and jointedly work towards solidification of the relationship."},{"t":"p","x":"Recovery after an illness, whether physical or emotional is also a feature of the Sun card. Its as if the clouds have lifted and Destiny has moved into high gear for you to take you on path of reassurance, health and all the means by which you can enjoy your life. The Sun is a perfect card for professional queries. It indicates promotions, accredit-ions and felicitations. You may be publicly rewarded or awarded and gain lot of popularity amongst your group members."},{"t":"p","x":"At its downside, the Sun imparts braggart attitude, arrogance and pompousness in character. The person may suffer from megalomania and be on own thought trip, even behaving with selfishness in pursuit of own goals. The Sun card may also indicate an excess sensation of happiness which as we know in the moderate ideology of Tarot teachings must be earthed in order to balance. The generosity and helpful predisposition of the Sun dominated personality will easily turn to that. The Sun Card is always positive, showing way for a better future."}],"id":"the-sun","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Loss of happiness and joy Health situation taking a downturn Demotion or loss of face publicly Lack of decisiveness and physical/emotional vitality. Loss of confidence Opportunities being denied. You may feel good fortune is evading you"}],"astro":{"planet":"Sun","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Sun card advises you to act positively and with complete confidence in your abilities. Leadership comes naturally to you so perform your administrative and welfare duties with compassion and fareness."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain from acting egoistic and acting out of dictatorship or selfishness."}]},"crystals":"Sunstone, Amber","gems":"Ruby, Diamond","keywords":["Enlightenment","Transparency","Confidence","Success","Joy","Prosperity"],"tone":null,"img":"19-TheSun.png"},{"name":"Judgement","num":20,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":134,"end":137,"meta":{"Archetype":"The World of Transformation","Task":"Redemption, Liberation","Element":"WATER","Crystal Guidance":"Unakite, Onyx","Color Guidance":"Violet"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Judgement is a Karmic card and a significant stopover point of review and appraisal and paybacks before the human soul moves to the final stage of World. In this picture tapestry, a winged angel dominates the skyline, holding the trumpet of judgement in his hands. He is blowing from the trumpet and leans down from the clouds. Below, naked human figures rise out from the coffins or out of earth itself, their faces suffused with wonder and expectation.The symbolism of this card represents that of the raising of the dead, the Last Judgement. This is the time when all the souls will be invoked for accounting of their activities during this lifetime and even earlier(if it has a bearing on this life time’s actions) and when the divine judgement will be passed on their karmic results. The judgement has not been passed yet. This is a significant factor because the human soul, in spite of the strong divine scrutiny here, has the ability to change their results with their judicious use of Free Will."},{"t":"p","x":"The Judgement brings with it memories and account taking of the past. You may be compelled to remember your past experiences and review them. These may be instances where due to your action or non-action someone might have suffered or had a loss. The Judgement will advise you to atone for the same to the afflicted. In case that is not possible, then reprimands and regrets must be gone through. You should be prepared for some transparent sessions, even of experiences that may have become buried in the sands of time in your memory."},{"t":"p","x":"Judgement also symbolizes the end of the old life and beginning of a new one. Whatever change is about to happen, will be for the beginning. The old skin will be shed off and much like transformation, this will entail a purer soul ready to move to the culmination of the Fool’s journey. The changes can be at the spiritual or the mundane level. The Mundane changes could be change in location, change in career, a new romance, leaving behind a relationship; whatever it takes for you to be more in alignment of your soul purpose. At the spiritual level, when this card appears in the reading there are very profound changes."},{"t":"p","x":"You will be faced with evidence that what you have subconsciously known to be your life purpose is very much your Higher Calling. There is no need to merely believe. You will Know. A higher level of psychic awareness will engulf you. Synchronicities will surround you, angel communication and intuitive signals will rain over you and you will experience the presence of the Divine."},{"t":"p","x":"This is a time of total surrender of Self and the Ego which makes you perceive the world from the\"I” perspective needs to be dissolved as you become receptive to the higher level messages being transmitted at you from various directions. Judgement is a positive card symbolizing regeneration, rebirth and understanding. You have a right to these rewards because of your constant faith and your striving despite doubts and adverse situations. On the downside, this card could bring up memories you find yourself unable to face in the present context. Here too the cosmic plan is to enhance your tolerance threshold and move you more towards being accountable and align you with the CAUSAL NEXUS - the philosophy that each of your actions cause results that you will have to face at some stage in your life-journey. No act exists in isolation. It will have its corresponding reaction in your universe one day."}],"id":"judgement","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"The person knows that a chapter has ended but is unwilling to change."},{"t":"p","x":"Non acceptance of situational reality Non willingness to apologize/show regret over a folly committed Disconnect with Higher Self/Divine Over confidence in self and self-karma and denying the role of Destiny Feeling judged yourself and also being judgemental of others"}],"astro":{"planet":"Pluto","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological Judgement card says it is time to let go of the past, to forget your petty resentments and embrace the future. Make the change now while you can and feel liberated. Pluto is the planet of the past and this card brings up issues, unresolved, from the Past. Embrace them, forgive and forget and bring dynamism towards future march."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain: Do not be tied to habits and regrets from the past. Do not be scared to face the past skeletons and injuries and try to resolve them."}]},"crystals":"Malachite, Fluorite","gems":"Cat’s Eye","keywords":["Decision","Change of Direction","Final Settlement","Amendments","Regrets"],"tone":null,"img":"20-Judgement.png"},{"name":"The World","num":21,"arcana":"major","suit":null,"start":137,"end":139,"meta":{"Archetype":"Paradise regained","Task":"Arriving; Taking one’s place","Element":"EARTH","Crystal Guidance":"Malachite, Fluorite","Color Guidance":"Green"},"rating":null,"body":[{"t":"p","x":"This is the last card of the Major Arcana and carries the energy of completion and culmination. The Wheel of the Major Arcana has come a full circle. There is a sense of fulfillment and celebration that will surround you much like the circular wreath that is the mainstay of the World Card image. This celebration could be outwardly manifest accolades, success and felicitations. It could even be an internal deeply satisfying emotion that fills your senses, heart and Mind. Here the celebration is full of gratitude and is quiet and private, in your inner world, in your dialogue with the Divine that is so dear and personal to you."},{"t":"p","x":"The World card foretells of major changes in your life such as change in career, change in direction of education, a relocation abroad, change in partner, recovery after fatal accident or disease, resurgence after a bankruptcy and other life impacting changes."},{"t":"p","x":"This is a very positive card as it spells all round success in life. You may be receiving parallel news about positive developments in different aspects of your life. If you have been going through a difficult period in life, it is indicating to keep striving hard in your desired direction and utilize all your abilities to reach your goal."},{"t":"p","x":"The World card shows strong affiliations with foreign lands. Its appearance in the spread may take you to foreign lands, or become expert in foreign language, or engage in international trade, or even travel to foreign lands or you might even become involved with someone who belongs to a foreign land. You will engage in activities and pursuits that expand and enlarge your understanding of the World.You feel that an unseen force is guiding you and supporting you. This card epitomizes the Akasha element. All the other four elements - fire, water, air, earth originate from it and finally submerge in Akasha itself."},{"t":"p","x":"We note that the books and scriptures that featured in the 4 symbols of the fixed zodiac signs in the Wheel of Fortune (No X card) are no longer present in Card No XXI. The subjects have been mastered, the lessons have been learned, the virtues have been absorbed by the character. The World person is mature and in connection with the Divine blessings in totality. The purple colored fluttering scarf over the nude human body in the picture is indicative of the umbrella protection and the total unity of the human with the elements around. This Trump helps you to expand your horizons. It will encourage you to work on international projects and affiliations. This Trump is a portal into a universalized and continuously expanding consciousness. It enhances a global outlook. Though your physical dimension might not be travelling, the mental and spiritual dimensions are expanding and you may delight in experiential travels of astral travel, out of body travel and past life regressions."}],"id":"the-world","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Being unable to finish a job or a project Feeling disappointed at last minute turn of events. Achieving a small victory but feeling inadequate when comparing to another’s larger victory Clinging to past laurels and not willing to move forward. A strange kind of incompleteness in life, restless, spiritual seeking Minor Arcana"}],"astro":{"planet":"Saturn","planetText":[{"t":"p","x":"The astrological World tells you to face reality, to put your feet on the ground and to accept what is possible and what is not."},{"t":"p","x":"Refrain: Do not limit yourself by perceived limitations. Karma should dictate your freedom from this bondage by sheer grit and clarity of thought and simplicity of behaviour. Accept what what you cannot do but go full force ahead on the aspects you can change in this lifetime. Understand your karmic footprint."}]},"crystals":"Onyx, Unakite","gems":"Opal","keywords":["Completion of a Cycle","Fulfillment","Achievement","Success","Satisfaction"],"tone":null,"img":"21-TheWorld.png"},{"name":"Ace of Wands","num":1,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Ace","start":143,"end":145,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun,Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Root of the Powers of Fire. All Fire Signs Combined -Aries, Leo, Sagittarius","Favourable Color":"Red Brown","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"A Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Ace of Wands is the root card of the Wands suit. This suit stands for fire element of dynamism, growth and constructive expansion."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : A hand holding the wand issuing from a cloud. Ace is club shaped, being rounded at one end showing the power and willingness to fight for the idea. Leaves and branches are springing out of the wand, showing new growth."},{"t":"p","x":"Ace of Wands is a wonderful card of opportunities which are fuelled by internal passion and give the person incredible amount of self confidence to fuel his dream. It quite literally means enthusiasm and new beginnings and could signify a new job, a birth, or a new course of study. Essentially an optimistic card, the Ace of Wands encourages us to bring our passion and insights to coherence in realizing our desires. It signifies the beginning/initiation of a creative or artistic project based on new vision or inspiration."},{"t":"p","x":"It even leads to growth of a new romance or a love affair where the mutual chemistry is very sharp and if provided the correct support, can become a very durable relationship as long term vision and ideology of both the partners is very similar."},{"t":"p","x":"The Feelings as shown by this card are of contentment and triumph. Its an original vision that is taking shape in your Mind and that fills you with energy. It might be a break from an unsuccessful past and that gives you a sense of freedom and solace."},{"t":"p","x":"Your attitude is about to change and expand and your horizons are looking bright as you make new plans for the future."},{"t":"p","x":"The beginning of a new enterprise, involving business or finance or of a personal nature where your heart’s desire is involved."},{"t":"p","x":"Possibly an inheritance, which may be either of money or property, or of the ability needed to make the enterprise begin successfully."}],"id":"ace-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Lack of inspiration and direction, misplaced focus, feeling hyper and restless, delayed starts"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands01.png"},{"name":"Two of Wands","num":2,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Two","start":145,"end":147,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Mars In Aries","Favourable Color":"Red Brown Orange","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"A Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Two of Wands is the execution card of the Wands suit. This suit stands for putting ideas into action. Astrologically it denotes Mars in Aries so the drive and determination are supremely high."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The 2 of wands represents the original spark of the Ace has been combined with planning and organizing and has now become stronger. The merchant in the red robe is looking with focus on his mind with aspirations of global achievements as evident from the Globe in his right hand. With the left he grasps on the new idea/plan while the original conquest is depicted by the fastened wand on his right. Two of Wands encourages you to assess your current achievement and to purposefully plan what you wish to accomplish ahead."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a very relevant card if you are in the early stages of a new venture or a relationship. You must stop a while and assess your initial journey and make the necessary practical adjustments to move ahead, all the while bearing in mind your final vision."},{"t":"p","x":"At times, with initial success, the person may become careless or complacent. This card is a warning / shout out that while the beginning has been strong, due dedication is still required to keep the enterprise in momentum."},{"t":"p","x":"The two of wands also signifies very strongly the needs for working partnerships. You will require the collaboration of various complementary parties to achieve the goal. The rewards shall accrue to all and they would want to work with you in the future too portending well for oncoming professional accomplishments."},{"t":"p","x":"The 2 of wands may also indicate the arrival of someone in your life whom you can learn from and develop a strong respect for. They might have some technical or spiritual knowledge that would guide you tremendously leaving an impact on your work ethos."},{"t":"p","x":"This is a card of astute planning and being in the right place at the right time. Due to your diligence and glowing reputation, more work will flow your way."},{"t":"p","x":"A card where your initial flame of passion is burning brightly and you are working with full sincerity and enthusiasm towards gaining more expertise in your field. The ultimate goal now seems closer."}],"id":"two-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Feel forced to take action while being unprepared, lack of confidence, lack of options, using power in hurtful/abusive way"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands02.png"},{"name":"Three of Wands","num":3,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Three","start":147,"end":149,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Moon in Aries","Favourable Color":"Red, Green Brown, Orange","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"A Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Three of Wands is the card which is seeped in ambition and a strong desire for unlimited growth and fame. Imagery : The merchant has now become clothed in elaborate costume with also a sash proclaiming he is head of a clan or a social group. His headgear also indicates his highly respectable position in the society or the organization he is representing. He looks out over the horizon with his back to us. He has no time for past regrets and only wants his vision fixed tightly on the glorious future. He holds the wand with a firm grasp. He stands elevated on a hillock where gets a bird’s eye view of his entire operations."},{"t":"p","x":"Three of Wands representation traditionally is of a ‘boyar”, one of the wealthy land holding merchant families who exercised great power in Russia’s history. This card astrologically represents Sun in Aries where the brilliant planet becomes exalted and marches ahead with maximum force."},{"t":"p","x":"Here too the merchant has reached the peak of success in reference to current time and is affluent and famous. He stands on an elevation showing also the rise in his thinking and his levels of goal setting which have now risen above the mundane. He is an extraordinary thinker and achiever. The teamwork and cooperation of the previous card has proved highly fruitful This card shows travel is likely in connection with work. Good news is also likely in relation to work expansion."},{"t":"p","x":"A golden period of wish fulfillment is on the cards regarding what you are pursuing. Your enterprise, vision and creativity will bring exciting results. There is still plenty to be accomplished but the beginning has been tremendous."},{"t":"p","x":"The three of wands signifies expansion by problem resolution. If earlier troubles in your pursuit besieged you, they will now be resolved by amicable negotiations. If your problems were solved by interference or opposition of others, you can still resolve them by taking things in firm hands this time. A disciplined approach will be necessary and a professional approach that makes your pursuit systematic and time bound is necessary at this stage."},{"t":"p","x":"If you are considering branching out into a different sphere of your life, the three of wands is a very encouraging signal. It also speaks of family expansion and the entry of a new person in your family on a happy note or a birth in the family. Its a signal of expansion in personal happiness and sense of achievement."}],"id":"three-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Lack of support from people and situations in moving ahead, over impulsive in taking decisions, lack of expansion in job or business, rejection in love"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands03.png"},{"name":"Four of Wands","num":4,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Four","start":149,"end":151,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Venus in Aries","Favourable Color":"Red, Brown","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"A Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Four of Wands is a card of relief and celebrations. Its a fresh burst of oxygen as your system goes into a restful state and its time to pause and celebrate the achievements along with the team and co-helpers who helped you get to the summit. Imagery : The festoon lined canopy with the background of the castle denotes that success and accomplishments now surround you. Its time for thanksgiving and gratitude to the Universe as well as those who helped you along the way to reach your goal. The raised hands of the workers show a sense of victory."},{"t":"p","x":"This card denotes the pleasures that money can buy and can indicate buying of a new property whether residential or commercial. It also encourages purchase of a new vehicle or a grand renovation of the existing assets. It shows weddings and get together in the family or in your social circle. There is a general air of glamour and prosperity all around. The time for relaxation is here. You have been working very hard and you now should take a well deserved rest. You can afford to let the work tarry for a while while you review your past achievements, thank your supporters and share with them the bounty earned and then set into motions expansionary plans for the future."},{"t":"p","x":"Four of wands features frequently as Feeling Card. It represents the reassurance and the sense of satisfaction that comes from doing a job well and being able to have surplus enough to share with others and attract their good wishes. This card also appears when you are emerging from a stressful situation in your life, one of the reasons being you have been working round the clock to meet the pressure or the severe deadlines. Your social life has been compromised greatly and you have had a work-life imbalance lately. This card advises you strongly to feel nurtured and loved again by aligning with your friends and family in a loving environment. Like the Number 4 that it represents, it carries the quality of stabilization and consolidation."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a lovely card for peace and harmony with your partner as you will find many areas to be jointly thankful for. Its the card for emotional security and warmth. Its the classic card for moving house. The new premises will be close to nature and if accompanied by other lush cards like the Empress or Ten of Cups will be spacious and ergonomically very conducive. A time to connect with your roots and your loved ones, this card aligns with the Heart Chakra and makes you feel emotionally strong and vital"}],"id":"four-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Unhappy personal or home life, feeling of lack, feeling of instability, ungratefulness, boredom from responsibilities"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands04.png"},{"name":"Five of Wands","num":5,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Five","start":151,"end":154,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Saturn in Leo","Favourable Color":"Red Brown, Blue","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"A gray card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The five of wands is the first chord of competition in the Wands journey. Its one of those times when your progress is halted by opposing forces, known and unknown."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The imagery shows five able bodied competitors fighting it out with their own wand. They are similarly dressed and of similar build indicating the struggle and opposition coming form surrounding environment."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears, problems beyond your control will suddenly rise up. Carefully made plans by you will be halted or face strange interruptions. You may have to cope with a series of petty disputes with people, especially in your working environment. Competition is a very powerful theme of this card. You will have to prove your point of view in front of a group of sceptical persons and be convincing enough to get through their wall of reluctance."},{"t":"p","x":"In the market space you will face direct competition by your rivals. They might use underhand means to bring down your reputation or would encroach upon your designated areas of expertise. The best way to deal with this strife is to be patient and cope with the surprises being flung at you. Be persevering and deal with one annoyance at a time. Carefully plan your strategy to deal with those who oppose you."},{"t":"p","x":"Remember this kind of strife or combat is a necessary part of your progress in your pursuit. Another lesson with the five of wands is to be flexible in your approach. If a different perspective has come up to counter yours, be patient and listen with an open ear. It could increase your own knowledge and teach you a useful thing or two. So decide on the basis of the merit of the case if this battle is worth fighting or you can give it up in order that the bigger war has to be fought. In that case pick the smaller battles carefully so your energy is conserved for the right purpose."},{"t":"p","x":"5 of wands as a Feeling shows deep disappointment as the events might turn out contrary to your expectations. The people you trust might turn against you. They might openly challenge you or they might be backbiting you. Its a time of treason and betrayal by those you trust. One of your trusted ones might even be sharing your confidences with your opponent or rival. So beware when the five of wands turns up in the reading."},{"t":"p","x":"Travel plans are also thwarted when this card has been appearing in the reading. Its again a reminder to pay attention to small details and documentation. Even the slightest overlooking on your part can give an advantage to your opponent or adversary. Destiny is not really supporting you at this juncture and its a test of your fortitude and combative spirit."},{"t":"p","x":"In a positive spirit this card can show innocuous events like a friendly sports match or appearing for a competitive exam or a public bidding for a project."},{"t":"p","x":"There is a dark side to this card and the fire energy can quickly escalate into trouble so always proceed with caution with this card of Conflict of the Suits wand."}],"id":"five-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Combative situation, emotionally trying times, arguments and being in negative whirlwind, dear ones also opposing your views, need to retreat to silent space"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Wands05.png"},{"name":"Six of Wands","num":6,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Six","start":154,"end":156,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Jupiter in Leo","Favourable Color":"Red Brown Green","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Six of wands is a signal of victory and success after a hard fought battle. Your leadership is publicly acknowledged and felicitated."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The leader is sitting atop a white horse and moving through a cheering crowd. His leadership is proclaimed by the winning wreath on the wand he is holding."},{"t":"p","x":"This card is a very positive card of the Wand series and a clear indication of success, victory and accomplishments. In a reading it shows that your aims will be fulfilled, you will be rewarded with gifts or monetary incentives, you have made or are about to make a significant conquest."},{"t":"p","x":"Long delayed success and pending rewards are also indicated when this card comes in the reading."},{"t":"p","x":"Since it comes after the five of wands which showed fierce combat or competition for the rewards, this six shows the victory of the smartest, the strongest or sometimes even the most fortunate for when Lady Fortune smiles on her favoured one, all competition falls far behind."},{"t":"p","x":"Here is a clear victor who has marched ahead of all others and is extremely delighted about it. As a feeling card, it signals extreme happiness, sense of pride and achievement as also relief at having obtained what you long desired. This card actually describes how the moment of Triumph can be reached. It shows that high amounts of confidence and optimism are required to rise the horse of victory as also popularity. Its the followers who make the leader and thus having a great chemistry and rapport with your followers is also integral to the secret of being a successful leader. The inherent lesson is a leader needs to cooperate rather than compete. In its best representation, the six of wands shows a person who can inspire others with belief and confidence. Another theme of this card is that the accomplishment should be enjoyed at the present but there is lots more to conquer for a leader. The white horse is symbolically slowly moving forward so it advises to not rest on past laurels and not get complacent about the success. Celebrate and feel exhilarated and then keep your mind on the next goal. A winner is always thinking forward."}],"id":"six-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Corruption, megalomania, fall from power, loss in elections, loss in competitive exam, loss of popularity, not getting recognition for your efforts"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands06.png"},{"name":"Seven of Wands","num":7,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Seven","start":156,"end":158,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Mars in Leo","Favourable Color":"Blue, Brown Green","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Gray Card indicating struggle.","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Seven of swords , much like the Five of wands suit is also carrying the message of troublesome times. Stressful times are beckoning and you will need all your inner reserves to face the challenging situation."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The young man is standing atop an elevation in a very defiant posture. With his wand firmly held horizontally across his chest, he is combating against several other wands that are opposing him. His mismatched shoes indicate he is fighting on the backfoot and was not prepared for the onslaught. The 7 of wands is a card that highlights the value of Courage. The astrological signature for this card is Mars in Leo. This is a combination of great dynamism and pulsating will power and desire to dominate and establish own sovereignity. In this card a very tough situation can come to challenge you. The adversary or adversaries are not of a common stature and have the influence to alter your decisions and your way of thinking. They might belong to your family or close circle of contacts, persons whose opinions matter to you. The time for celebration has passed and now you must prove with new and harder challenge that you are upto the task. Its a test of whether you will succeed or whether you will give up and withdraw. This is a card which tests your determination and staying power. A big challenge is flung at you. You may be unprepared or just partially prepared but its imperative that you make a success out of it so you can proceed towards the culmination points of 9 and 10 of wands."},{"t":"p","x":"It shows you are in for a power struggle but the fact that you are elevated as compared to the adversaries shows you having the upper hand. So you must capitalize upon that advantage. Inner battle will be paramount. You will have doubts and conflicts in your mind. Keep your faith. It is said that winning is a result of not only having a view point but also putting all your energy behind sustaining it in face of all conflicting opinions. So make your choice and then defend it with all your might. You have the resilience to make your presence felt with a thump. Very often the struggle depicted in seven of wands takes place inside you. You may feel the burden of other people’s expectations and this will stress you out as you garner all your resources to rise to the occasion. As feelings this card is of confusions and dilemmas and having self doubts. The resultant mental battle will make you stronger and also clearer in your convictions."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can also bring to you a situation where you have achieved a great deal but still have some way to go. You may know that the end is in sight but yet its a struggle to muster the necessary energy for that final effort. The message is not to give up and keep at it doggedly as resilience makes you a better person as also more successful, in the mundane world as well as your soul journey. This card is difficult but when taken in the positive spirit can burn the impurities inside you and make you gold in the fire of trying times."}],"id":"seven-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Lack of self conviction, easily being defeated or persuaded, health deterioration, voices in the head troubling your daily life, powerlessness"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Wands07.png"},{"name":"Eight of Wands","num":8,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Eight","start":158,"end":160,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Mercury in Sagittarius","Favourable Color":"Brown, Blue, Green","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"In the Tarot, the suit of the wands is all about adventure, risk\u0002taking, and creative enterprising. The 8 of this suit represents events unfolding that will help you to take the lead on a situation you are asking the Tarot about."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : Here we see 8 wands moving quickly against a bright and sunny background, with some water in the background showing the passage of time. The wands are facing downwards towards the Earth and there is no human or animal figure in this card indicating that the proceedings are beyond the control of Human will to a large extent. The 8 of Wands is a powerful card for long pending changes which have not been transpiring inspite much effort and desire. The recent past has been plagued by stagnation and the situation is demanding a breakthrough."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears, Big positive changes have already started gaining momentum in the environment. The change will now be swift and decisive. Its a very positive card when one is waiting for a situation to improve or decision to be delivered. This card is also redolent with passion and feelings of attraction. When asked for a relationship issue, it brings welcome news where attachments will become stronger and transparent communication about feelings will be exchanged."},{"t":"p","x":"Travel is surely on the cards when the eight of wands makes an appearance. Air travel is generally indicated but it can encompass swift road travel too. The wands are moving swiftly so plans will be made swiftly. There shall be no obstacles and sometimes it can catch you by surprise because you were not expecting a change in the situation so rapidly and might be caught unawares."},{"t":"p","x":"Some Tarot readers also see a symbol of seasons changing under this card, so you may see a new\"season\" of life in the situation you are asking Tarot about."},{"t":"p","x":"The only thing you know for sure when you see the 8 of Wands is that change is coming, and it is likely coming out of the blue. Being able to roll with unforeseen scenarios in both love and life will be the keys to your success when you see the 8 of Wands. This is not a card to stop and think things through on. Whatever opportunity the Universe presents you with, use it or lose it."},{"t":"p","x":"Eight of wands is also a message of rapid communication. It could be an exchange of ideas in a board meeting or an interview or a debating event or a political showdown. The exchange of ideas will be intellectual and would need to be moderated intelligently and channelized towards a constructive decision."}],"id":"eight-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Excess physical or nervous energy, confusion regarding where to focus efforts, abrupt delay in ongoing work, too many castles in air but lacking groundwork, speaking too quickly so message is not understood, caution in travelling and driving, lack of sleep, over-excitement so lack of attention to details"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands08.png"},{"name":"Nine of Wands","num":9,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Nine","start":160,"end":162,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Moon in Sagittarius","Favourable Color":"Brown Green","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Medium Positive card with note of caution","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Nine of Wands is one of the final cards of the wands suit and displays a cycle that is about to be completed and the feelings of exhaustion or hopelessness that may creep in when a person is about to achieve his goal."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The weary and defensive person is standing against eight wands in the background he holds on to one wand in defence. He is injured and bandaged and may have been afflicted physically or mentally during his long wand journey. The initial fire has been consumed to a large extent and the embers need some stoking so that the fire burns again and the completion point is reached."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can represent life’s resiliency- a [person who has suffered great level of sorrow, or oppression or suppression of innate desires has the ability to come back in a fighting position. Its the card of the underdog, who has suffered enough at the hands of adverse circumstances but finds the last ounce of energy to hit back and race to the finishing line. If you have been feeling exhausted due to previous skirmishes, the card reassures you that not only will you cope with the trying circumstances but also succeed especially if this card is supported by success cards like six of wands or the Sun. Somehow you will find the necessary courage and strength to see things through. You should try to rely on a good adviser or a support system for this critical time to pass through. This card can also indicate jealousy and negativity by people who have been following your success graph till date. They might try to discourage you to take the last step or demoralize you by weakening opinions. Defend yourself; shield yourself against such attackers. Conserve your psychic energy. Stay resilient and strong. You are close to the Goal Point."}],"id":"nine-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Over defensive about something, not accepting necessary cooperation, physical exhaustion, mental over-wroughtness, nervous breakdown, Burn Out"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Wands09.png"},{"name":"Ten of Wands","num":10,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Ten","start":162,"end":165,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Saturn in Sagittarius","Favourable Color":"Brown","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Positive card with caution","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Ten of wands is a card of reaching the end of your wands journey. Its a card spelling achievements and fulfillment of one’s passions. There might have been a price to pay for it though. This card imbues you with the feeling that you can do anything, but also warns not to take things for granted. Imagery : The inspiration for the image of the lone person being weighed down by his ten wands of excessive responsibilities has the astrological reference of Saturn in Sagittarius. The heaviness of Saturn has overcome the joyous freedom of the Sagittarian spirit, which is oppressed within the confines of the material world."},{"t":"p","x":"The excessive burden indicates his sole struggle over a long period of time. He seems fatigued but he is now almost near the destination and will have time to rest and revel. The ten of wands indicates that a long journey full of challenges and struggles is finally over. The destination or goal post is very near. The burden however still remains daunting and it will overwhelm you if you are not cautious. You have clearly taken on more than you can shoulder and now its weighing heavily on you. Your physical or mental health is deteriorating due to the extra pressure."},{"t":"p","x":"This card indicates an obsession with undertaking responsibilities. Sometimes it could be thrust upon you by work exigencies but this card shows the willingness of the person to take on more than he can handle. You have taken on something for which you may be totally equipped. You are feeling the heat of the demands made on you but your dedication to the purpose will make you work harder to fulfill it even though your own health and life quality may be compensated Sometimes its difficult to set your boundaries and the 10 of wands is one such illustration. In your enthusiasm and firm self confidence you may jump in to shoulder projects or obligations without considering if you will be able to handle them long term. You have taken on too much, this card suggests and are now finding it difficult to fulfill your commitments. Another factor which is aggravating the situation is your non desire to delegate or share the responsibilities. You are not sure if any other person will be able to perform the task as well as you can and hence keep on accumulating more and more in your own portfolio till it becomes a one man army. At times the pressure may come to you from a higher authority and you are not in a position to say No. You are simply burdened with over work and not get enough time to recuperate. And the hard worker that you are, you will put your head down and keep slogging at it."},{"t":"p","x":"If you are self employment, this indicates a period where you will be inundated with work and you will be racing against time to complete it. Sometimes your reputation may have increased and thus you become the next big thing in your field and there are many agencies demanding your time, attention and opinions. All of it can be exciting for a wands(fire) driven person like you but will leave you exhausted. As per the image the figure is so immersed in the details of his work that he cannot see ahead. Maybe its the time to step back and see where exactly this work load is taking him and whether he can adjust the responsibilities in a manner that the individual load on him is eased."},{"t":"p","x":"10 of wands advises to share your work load with others in your team. That will help you devise a more practical strategy to bear the load till the end. Else there might be a physical or mental breakdown much before you get to enjoy the results of your achievement."}],"id":"ten-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Time of great relief, unburdening of duties, feeling relaxed and free spirited, accepting cooperation for greater good of all, win-win situation, balancing work and pleasure, health situation improving"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Wands10.png"},{"name":"Page of Wands","num":11,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Page","start":165,"end":168,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Personification of Fire (Element only)","Favourable Color":"Orange Yellow Red Brown","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The page of wands is the young message bearer or initiator of the WANDS suit and carries the seed of new project, new passions and is high on excitement and energy to achieve. Imagery : A well dressed dapper looking young man is holding up the wand and gazing at with speculation on its potential. The landscape is barren where the fire of creativity has yet to fructify the manifestation. The page looks set for travel and adventure as his red feather signal his connection to the spirit realm from where he downloads his messages."},{"t":"p","x":"As a situation the page of wands is a new opportunity or the seed of an idea that is inspired by a passion birthed inside your heart. It signals your deepest attachment to a dream you have always wanted to follow and which keeps the fires of your enthusiasm burning brightly. Its the beginning of an exciting new enterprise, or following a new spiritual endeavour or pursuing a passion that has been dear to you. It can also indicate an exciting new romance or friendship where mutual chemistry is crackling. Its an idea that keeps you awake at nights; it inspires you to that great an extent. Even if you are of a mature age or not very excitable by nature, this is one initiative that is making your heart beat fast again. It males you feel young and full of energy and aspiration. It could be related to pursuing a new course of study or writing a book or creating a design of a new home. Its energizing and achievement oriented and will give you a personal high. Its something you owe to yourself; your ode to self-creation. Right now, with the wand popping up its still at the idea stage and will need careful planning. Do not allow it to fizzle out since it fills you with so much renewed energy and objectivity."},{"t":"p","x":"Page of wands indicates excitement and new experiences coming in your life. It the time to explore the hidden aspects of your personality and not shy away from popularity and good times. Its a time to be free and express yourself in ways that make you feel alive. Travel also is on the cards when this page comes along. Generally it will be a holiday but can indicate relocation too if accompanied by majors of change like the Wheel of Fortune or The World in the spread. Life will also move at a more hectic page, this page denotes. The fire energy is crackling here and your motivation to meet and connect with like minded souls will be greater. There will be more intensity and warmth in your temperament and there will be a lot going in your life and you will be loving the need for being on your toes."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person the page of wands is high on enthusiasm and eager to achieve. He has high levels of physical energy and mental excitement that make him an exciting companion to have around. He takes orders well and has good management skills. He is flexible in his thinking and is willing to travel to achieve his goals. He is intellectually stimulating and willing to try out various options. He is terrific person to have on your team as he is self motivated and keeps the environment upbeat too. Sometimes the Page may bring unexpected news which might compel you to change your pre scheduled plans at the last minute.Life will be at a faster pace and you will need to be buoyant and mentally receptive to live out this phase."}],"id":"page-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Love for thrill and achieving the impossible, finding ways to add excitement to life, holding a new idea close to chest, temper tantrums in frustration or unhappiness, riddled with self-doubts"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands11.png"},{"name":"Knight of Wands","num":12,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Knight","start":168,"end":171,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Scorpio / Sagitarrius","Favourable Color":"Yellow Red Brown","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The knight of wands is that breakthrough moment in life when all the inertia and procrastination that had been with you needs to be shed off, swift decision needs to made and followed up by aggressive, even defiant march to attain your goals."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The knight is in armour and seated on a horse that looks ready for battle action. The legs of this horse are in the air indicating his energy and drive to go straight for the kill. The fire element is most manifest when the Knight of fire/ wands is in action. The horse is orange in colour and his teeth are bared because he is angry."},{"t":"p","x":"The look on the knight’s face is determined. The tassels on his dress, the mane of the horse are all quivering and represent the fiery energy of this element in its prime."},{"t":"p","x":"This is a situation of brimming vitality and unrestrained energy. Be prepared for hectic and bustling times. The targets will be ambitious and the drive to achieve them will be higher. When this knight appears, you have no patience for protocol and rules and want to take swift and cutting action. This card also brings you travel and adventure. The trips will excite you to physical and mental limits of your being as you may experiment with activities that till now you have only admired from afar but not had the courage to get into. Your confidence is high and thrill beckons you."},{"t":"p","x":"You may be going in for long distance road travel or a trip to another country. The trip will seldom feature resting in a secluded spot or luxuriating in a spa. You may be visiting somewhere for the first time and exploration of the local treasures will be high on the agenda."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can also indicate that you would get visitors to visit you from another country. You will be engrossed in keeping them entertained and after a while it might become a bit tiresome for you."},{"t":"p","x":"This constant action is a feature that is often seen with the knight of wands and over a period of time others mind find it difficult to match pace with the frenetic activity level. As a person the knight is a conqueror, of milestones, of hearts, of whatever he sets out to establish his control over. He is very popular with the people due to his vitality that he exudes. His presence itself is energising. Moving and interacting swiftly, he motivates people and mostly towards a higher ideal. His aura and energy is larger than life. His reputation precedes him and people look for opportunities to talk with him because he transfers his unique energy on to whomever he meets. Within minutes he maintains fiery eye contact and motivates those he comes in contact with."},{"t":"p","x":"He is a natural leader and relishes being so. Loves being the centre of attraction where he gains applause and stimulating company. He has many interests and projects, which he supports with enthusiasm. He hates to be bored and loves fun and adventure. Fond of travel, he is an impulsive and daring person who has an inherent attraction to dangerous sports and dare devilry acts."},{"t":"p","x":"His hastiness and unwillingness to listen to others wishes and fears is one of his weaknesses. He wants quick action and quicker results but this impulsiveness may be unpalatable to many. This also makes him the black sheep of the group dynamic at times but he is charming enough and intelligently makes his way back into hearts."},{"t":"p","x":"As a friend and lover, he is exciting company to have around. He will plan with enthusiasm and keep all those around excited with his eagerness to experiment and explore their talents."},{"t":"p","x":"This knight has an unpredictable streak and is capable of galloping alone forward if the inner vision seizes him and his team members are unable to match his energy. He might pursue several projects at one time but may not have the patience to see them through. His interests shift rapidly and he needs constant new challenges to his mind."},{"t":"p","x":"All in all he is a great leader and initiator but his unbridled ebnergy and dynamism needs to be channelized for great achievements to be consolidated."}],"id":"knight-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Love for attention but lacking natural rapport building skills, quick tempered & demanding, creating controversies to be noticed, attention seeker, prone to sudden emotional outbursts, impatient and manipulative"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands12.png"},{"name":"Queen of Wands","num":13,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"Queen","start":171,"end":174,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Pisces / Aries","Favourable Color":"Orange Yellow Red Brown Orange","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The queen of wands is a very remarkable court card in terms of its attributes and achievements. It epitomizes all the qualities of the fire element in the positive, creative and passionate ways. Imagery : This Queen sits proudly on her throne while facing forwards. This is a clear symbol of her confidence and receptivity to the challenges and experiences that lie ahead of her, She is holding a sunflower which is also represented on her throne symbolizing her optimistic outlook on life.In her right hand she holds a wand, starting to blossom and showing the fertility inherent in the situation. She is associated with fidelity, honour and fairness. The black cat represents her links with occultism (some schools says, even witchcraft), but in the modern context it denotes her deep connection with the Divine and the mystic sciences. When the Queen of Wands appears in a spread the situation facing you will require her unique attributes."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a time to claim your leadership. You must be as confident and ambitious of your work goals as you are of yourself nurturing a family. It will be a demanding time, calling for all your strengths and capabilities to prove your worth. If you are working or engaged in a vocation, its time to let the world know of your talents. You must plan events and opportunities to network professionally and establish your identity in the field you are contributing to. Its not a time to just take but also to give orders. So try voraciously for a higher level of responsibility especially if it entails leadership role and mentoring or maintaining a team for its performance. Your fire element is at an all time high and you can achieve whatever you set your mind. You are prepared to take on the extra challenge, the travel and the negotiations that are likely to face you in this time of Ascension. You were born to rule, you will realize with startling clarity and will lay down clear boundaries of acceptable behavior in all your relationships-whether personal or professional. It is time to connect to your Authentic self and recognize what are your deeper aspirations. Try to introspect and discover what makes your passion for life light up. Destiny will now present you unexpected opportunity to express yourself creatively and to have your spacial brand identity and you will be admired for your unique creative or physical or intellectual talents. You may also find excitement in exploring your Divine or Intuitive self. The mysteries of the occult will fascinate you and you will realize that becoming spiritual helps you connect better with the people you manage. It will make you more independent and balanced in your thinking. Leadership comes to you naturally and you will do it with a natural warmth that endears you to all who meet you. Expand yourself and shine in the limelight when this card comes up in your reading. As a person the Queen of WANDS is an inspiring and dynamic figure. She is supremely intelligent but warm-hearted at the same time. Her intelligence would never make her aloof or arrogant. She uses her mental acumen and compassionate heart to shine in her role of leading projects and people. Like a typical Leo woman that this card astrologically represents, she is high on energy and being a perfectionist she achieves an excellent balance between work and domestic life. She is a creative person and her surroundings reflect her eclectic and quirky tastes. She loves travelling and broadening her mental horizons and brings back items from across her travels to create an ambience that is uniquely Her."},{"t":"p","x":"With this queen around, all situations are beautifully managed. She is a high calibre organizer and also a lavish hostess. Irrespective of her financial means, her products and presentations will stand out. She is confident enough to follow the path of her convictions. Se is not aggressive but in her quiet way, her clarity of thought makes her move ahead with alacrity and determination. She shows deep compassion and understanding and possesses the maturity to analyse an issue from multifarious angles and offer her fair advice. She is known for her fairness and a high sense of justice. She takes her role of leadership and counselling people very seriously and practices it with ethics and morality. She may act as a confidante to many because of her combination of understanding nature and an analytical mind."},{"t":"p","x":"At times, she may have a fiery temper but it is short lived. Living true to her fire element, she may become passionate about an issue or an argument but she is also quick to forgive and move on from grudges. When this Queen appears, look forward to a creatively fulfilling and socially hectic time. The queen in you will be noticed and appreciated by many around you so be confident and clear in both your expectations an your boundaries. Success is assured. Move forward with poise and a sense of purpose aligned with your authenticity."}],"id":"queen-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Well respected but not popular, quick to anger and swift decision maker, openly ambitious, restless desire for personal success, domineering and temperamental qualities"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands13.png"},{"name":"King of Wands","num":14,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Wands","rank":"King","start":174,"end":177,"meta":{"Element":"Fire","Planets":"Mars, Sun, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Cancer / Leo","Favourable Color":"Orange Yellow Red Brown Green","Chakra Associated":"Solar Plexus"},"rating":"Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The King of wands is a situation or person in your life with very high levels of ambition, confidence and power. Its a time of success and pure achievements and you may be called upon to explore these qualities in order to mark your leadership presence."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The King sits with supreme authority on his throne and looks confidently ahead. There is no place for past recriminations with this king. Forward is the way to plan and move. The lions and salamanders on his throne represent his ability to regenerate from misfortune and his strength. The robe is bright and orange resembling a flame, while the crown is shaped like a tongue of fire. The wand he holds is blossoming representing his creativity and his passion. The King of wands describes a mature man who may be an important feature in your life at the time of reading. It could be metaphor of a situation you are facing or you yourself may need to bring in the energy of this card to handle your life at the moment of reading. This king epitomizes the use of the staff or the wand that is the traditional symbol of the FIRE SUIT. In medieval Europe the wand represented the power of the State(government) to achieve its goals. The independent city states of Europe had much freedom of action and movement ; the wand / staff of state had the power to bring things to pass."},{"t":"p","x":"When the King of wands comes in the reading you are in for a superb professional opportunity. You are being called upon to take over the mantle of the head of a company or a team or a project as the scale of your professional domain entitles you to be. It will be a strong leadership position where you will be endowed with great amount of discretion in decision making. Its a time to be surrounded by power and triumph. Your working environment will be marked by powerful and influential people who will leave their mark on your thinking and you may feel very invigorated and compelled to make plans for your own growth in life."},{"t":"p","x":"When such great opportunity to rise on the ladder of influence awaits you, you must be at your charming and witty best. Do the networking that will make you matter. Be persuasive in the way you do public dealing. Dame Fortune is smiling at your talent and wants to bless you with golden opportunity. As a person, the king of wands is a dynamic figure. He is so marinated in his own passions and dreams that his dynamism becomes infectious and others also get positively motivated to follow him or to bask in his indefatigable aura. His sense of humour is unmistakable and he is witty and smart with the usage of words and language. He is warm, lively, enthusiastic and all these personal qualities will make him attract a band of followers and admirers. He is also a social occasion’s delight and revels in entertaining and having a high vibration environment around of equally enthusiastic persons. Energy surrounds him like a second skin and he exudes a charisma that is hard to be resistant to. It may occasionally be accompanied by a nasty temper and an impulsive nature but that is a transitory aspect and which is generally overlooked considering his other add-ons. When the wands suit comes up in relationships, a common reassurance is of fidelity and loyalty. The court cards of the wand element are charismatic and may have an occasional roving eye but they are very clear on their personal boundary regarding love and passion. They love with a ferocity and the king is a proud spouse, father and homemaker. He highlights the achievements and qualities of his family members and is very devoted to his home life."},{"t":"p","x":"If this man proposes love, you should be careful.He is a sensuous lover and may come across as seductive at times but will not cross the boundary. He likes to control the pace of the relationship and may intermittently be warm and emotionally distant."},{"t":"p","x":"Legal bindings and marriage contracts are important for him as his sense of honour is well defined. He respects all his contractual relationships, whether in professional or personal domain. His heart will be enthused by the concept of monogamy. He may also be pursuing a spiritual practice and likes the sense of self control and peace it imparts to his racing metabolism."},{"t":"p","x":"This card is a true leader and a king in the true sense of the world. His dynamism and energy coupled with his sense of loyalty and people skills make him an unparalleled star of the Tarot deck."}],"id":"king-of-wands","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Over ambitious, demanding and only driven by need to conquer people and objects. He uses all resources at hand for controlling others to serve his own interests"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Wands14.png"},{"name":"Ace of Cups","num":1,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Ace","start":177,"end":180,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Root Power of Water (All Water Signs Combined) - Cancer, Scorpio, Pisces","Favourable Color":"Blue Yellow White","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Ace of cups is almost poetic in its beauty and the divine depths it carries. Its the hand of God upon your heart and all its emotional richness. The most powerful vibe card for new and divinely guided love and fruits of creativity. Imagery : In the Ace of Cups card, there is a hand emanating from the clouds holding out a cup, as if in a offer to the querent to take a drink. This cup is overflowing with sparkling Liquid which symbolizes pure and pristine emotion. The cup has five streams of water overflowing from the brim. These five streams represent the power of intuition and Inner voice and hint at the depth of new and innovative ideas that lie within us. The streams are flowing both ways indicating that while one draws from the Universal abundance as a spiritual blessing, one will become more in connection with Divine if the flow of emotions is kept flowing. The spiritual and emotional fulfillment shall be endless."},{"t":"p","x":"Ace of Cups is a glorious card, one of the most positive in the entire tarot. It denotes the start of an emotionally fulfilling love journey, or a new spiritual initiation, or a new creative enterprise or anything else that is closely connected to your heart and makes you feel emotionally satiated."},{"t":"p","x":"It can also indicate conception and a new birth in the family which will initiate a phase of joyful times for those connected to the event. The surrounding cards acquire importance when the question is about fertility. A supporting indicator like The Empress or The Sun will strengthen the possibility of the fertility blooming."},{"t":"p","x":"The illustration of this card shows that the cup is brimming over with overwhelming feelings of gratification and pure love. You might be feeling so suffused with the bounties of the Universe leading your life to higher levels that you will feel drawn to offer gratitude. Religious or spiritual travel and rituals are advised when this card is prevalent in your life. Professionally you could become involved in an activity where your inherent talents are utilized. These talents may have remain unearthed till date and the present opportunity to display them from the secret alcoves of your heart will being you immense goodwill and you will be delighted and pleased at your self worth. You might be rewarded for your creative approach to your work."},{"t":"p","x":"Alternatively if the situations have been difficult for you lately, the Ace of Cups will provide wonderful opportunity to reconcile and restore peace and harmony. A rift in any working or social relationship may now be healed when you take the initiative to say sorry or express how you wish the rift to be mended. The reciprocity from the opposite side will be earnest and quick."},{"t":"p","x":"Friendship also receives a fillip when the ace of cups is around. Old friendships which once filled you with happiness and laughter will surface again your life. An old love may be rekindled with fresh understanding and appreciation for each other. Relationships, old or new, now is the time when the love will flow freely. It will emanate from a deeper, unfathomable depth in your heart and will know no limits."},{"t":"p","x":"Ace of Cups is the feeling of being alive with every pore, being in a sentient space and in gratitude for all the sensations to the Almighty who you will sense within You, and not Outside."}],"id":"ace-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Creative block; loss of what your heart holds dear to it. Time of emotional loss, instability or pain, need or desire to give up a pleasure like alcohol or gastronomia or an extravagant hobby, keenness to make new friends will be thwarted"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups01.png"},{"name":"Two of Cups","num":2,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Two","start":180,"end":183,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Venus in Cancer","Favourable Color":"Blue Red Green","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Two of cups epitomizes the philosophy of love. Love is a powerful creative for the world as well as for the individuals. Love gives us the inspiration to make something of our life. Imagery : In this card, a man and a woman are exchanging their cups in a ceremony. there is a symbol of Hermes’ Caduceus in between which relates to negotiation, protection and duality. The man and the woman are differently dressed showing that contrasting energies which are convinced that when they collaborate, will produce complementary results, decide to come together and share their unique resources, personality and talents."},{"t":"p","x":"The angel grants them blessings indicating that this collaboration will bring a third dimension of creativity. This is an emotional partnership. It can indicate a love relationship becoming very strong and committed. It can also indicate that a betrothal will now be ceremonially strengthened to become a lifelong commitment which will be prosperous and fruitful for both the parties. In a work collaboration, parties will show willingness to come together and forge new alliances. Besides the professional gains, they will become emotionally close and give of themselves freely to forge this union into permanence. There is a genuine, internal desire to bond when this card comes up in a reading."},{"t":"p","x":"The 2 of cups is a traditional interaction of a contract or agreement, of two hearts beating as one, two souls united for a common purpose. Two of cups is a very encouraging card when the relationship is going through a time of conflict or struggle. It indicates that the partners are mature enough to put individual ego and individual differences behind them and to concentrate on what brings them together."},{"t":"p","x":"Although this card traditionally links to emotional and spiritual matters, the contract indication could encompass a wide range of issues like a new home. A new travel plan, a new tenancy agreement, a financial arrangement.What is important is the level of emotion behind it. There is an awareness and willingness in everyone to make this happen harmoniously and in a cheerful environment."},{"t":"p","x":"Like any Number 2 card in the minor arcana, there is no guarantee that the union that has come abut with such good intentions will be long lasting. 2s still show the beginning of the energy of the suit and require sustained effort and stamina to complete the journey till the end. It advises against the attitude of being compalescent."},{"t":"p","x":"The beginnings have been optimistic. Its a partnership and all the parties will need to put in individual efforts. No one can take a back seat and allow others to do the work. When this clarity is present, then it can lead to productive and mutually satisfying results."},{"t":"p","x":"Do not expect the relationship to be without stumbling blocks. The intentions are pure but the ego clashes could put major roadblocks. Do not be idealistic or too trusting of the other person. When you accept the grayness of the human character that you are interacting with and collaborating with then the results will be realistic and long lasting."}],"id":"two-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Emotional misunderstanding, rejection of proposal to love or marriage, rebuff in friendship or other relationships, being friend-zoned, imbalance in yin-yang balance within, emotional manipulation to connect with someone"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups02.png"},{"name":"Three of Cups","num":3,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Three","start":183,"end":185,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Mercury in Cancer","Favourable Color":"Red Orange Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The three of cups felicitates achievements and coming together of creative, beautiful people to celebrate and raise a toast to the bounty they are blessed with. The three of cups is a hugely happy card but with suggestions of danger lurking in the waters of feeling."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : This card caries the image of three women lifting their cups up into the air in a celebration of some sort. Good times are in the air, for the three ladies have wreaths made of flowers in their hair. Wreaths are often associated with success and victory, so their happiness is well deserved. The ladies are also seen standing on top of a field of flowers and fruit, further adding to the abundant feelings in this card. This is an intensely joyful card of the tarot spelling moments of unbridled joy and camaraderie. The fruits of the joint labour are adorning the grounds and there is an air of celebration, freedom and pure\"letting down of all guards” and being in the moment. Its called the Sunshine card of this suit as it denotes stepping into warm and caressing sunshine after a long period of solitariness or mundane hard work. You could be celebrating an achievement or just the joy of friendship and companionship. Idea is to be together with a certain set of people and feel free and without any grouses."},{"t":"p","x":"The 3 of cups can indicate any kind of get-together or party; housewarming, marriage, engagement ceremony, award ceremony, birth of a baby, welcoming a new family member home, launch of a new product or creative enterprise. It is not necessarily a lavish occasion, it can be a quiet celebration with good food, drinks and a lot of laughter."},{"t":"p","x":"This is also a time of having intense experiences. You might react very intensely to certain situation. It may be unlike your normally moderate behaviour. This card always carries the lurking undercurrents of emotions becoming so intense that they may become unmanageable."},{"t":"p","x":"You may be uncharacteristically joyous or you may burst into sudden tears. The balance of emotional content is an important lesson in the three of cups. Emotionally an unstable time, you need to check the swell of emotions inside you. Find well balanced, constructive ways to outlet your emotional chakra. At times the presence of a third party, often unwelcome is also indicated by this card. This person could be in physical and tangible form coming between union of two persons or it could even loom in the form of an intense memory. Additional meanings of this card are seeking out those friends who you have not met for a long time; making the first move if you feel the need to make a peace pact with someone, solace and tranquility, recovery after illness, networking required for success, socialising for advancing up the professional ladder, attending family gatherings for maintaining your goodwill."}],"id":"three-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Feeling lonely as being alienated in friendship, creative collaborations falling apart, ego-games in professional field, excessive partying, alcohol dependence, friendship of just good times but no real base to it, extra marital affair"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups03.png"},{"name":"Four of Cups","num":4,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Four","start":185,"end":187,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Moon in Cancer","Favourable Color":"Blue Green Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Gray card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Four of cups is a gray card. Most often, this shows a sense of being jaded and emotionally in a cocoon. There has been lot of frenetic activity in the recent past and when that suddenly halts and a sense of calm prevails, the adrenaline in the system subsides and you are left with a feeling of weariness where the physical world does not mean or penetrate into the senses. This calls for a much needed and deliberate time out so that your senses become decluttered and you are once more in sound nervous health."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : shows a young man sitting against a tree trunk in a lush garden with three upturned cups in front of him and a hand extending another cup from the skies and he is ignoring the offer."},{"t":"p","x":"In this card is also a deliberate sense of boredom. The man in this image already has more than he has desired. The upturned cups indicate his affluent and abundant life. All his wishes and desires have already been met with. He really has not any goal or burning vacant spots in his heart left. There is thus a sense of thanklessness and just a discontent in his body language. He is seeking more meaning in life but does not know where to look. Life has ceased to hold any challenges and the feeling of\"been there, done that” envelopes you. In such an instance, a wise counsellor or a serendipitous moment needs to make him express his Gratitude for all he has been blessed with and look for different avenues to share his blessings with. A moment to acknowledge the less fortunate than him and to extend a helping hand."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can also describe the tedium that accompanies the uneventful period in your life when nothing fruitful is happening in your life in spite of efforts. There can also be disillusionment when someone lets you down or has betrayed you in some way. You may go into a shell and refuse to interact with people and situations because you are protecting yourself from further scars."},{"t":"p","x":"The advice inherent in 4 of cups is that though this is a period of apathy and sadness, it must not linger so long that the fresh opportunity knocking at your door slips away. Time and Tide wait for no man and so it essential that you remain aware of what is happening around you. Do not become so wrapped up in your feelings of disillusionment that you cannot see what novelty is present in your environment. It could be something that could refresh and rejuvenate you and make you fall in love with life again."}],"id":"four-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Overburdening by stress or emotional demands, recovery from apathy or depression, getting over a negative period and socializing again, understanding importance of social connections, gratitude and thanksgiving for abundance in life, advise to take a break in nature or a retreat in silence"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Cups04.png"},{"name":"Five of Cups","num":5,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Five","start":187,"end":189,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Mars in Scorpio","Favourable Color":"Black Gray Blue Green","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Dark card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"There are certain cards in the tarot that instantly conjure up a dark and negative feeling. The five of cups is one such dark card. It has its silver lining like any tarot card brinking on darkness does, but the overwhelming vibe is of gloom. Imagery : The card has the image of a man who is standing with his face concealed and is cloaked in all black from head to toe. The down-turned hidden face shows his resistance to be seen or be approached."},{"t":"p","x":"The three cups in front of him are overturned. Some decks show an iota of blood spilling out of the cups. Two upturned cups are behind him but out of his line of vision. There is also a fast flowing river in front of him, a bridge in the distance and a solid looking house(even a fortification) which awaits his return across the border. This card is an indication of great despair and sadness. The person has gone through a veritable loss of great magnitude and is weighed down by sorrow."},{"t":"p","x":"The loss has been devastating and he is in deep mourning. The loss could be recent or it could be regret of a past event which has only hit his present life with full force leading him to realise how meaningless his current life is. He wishes he could go back in time to make a choice differently, a choice that was so significant that it decided the entire course of his life. He feels very impoverished at the moment and this feeling of loneliness and anxiety is acutely emotional in nature. If you are trying to rationalise the end of a relationship you will feel better when you reflect on what you learned as a result. Its a time to introspect how you could have managed the situation in a better way. There are always lessons to be learned when the 5 of cups turns up in reading. If accompanied by a regenerative card like the Death or the Sun, you will soon re-enter the relationship with higher dimensions of understanding with each other. It can also signal of a new and more dynamic relationship for you, one that will sustain you towards more self love and brilliance."},{"t":"p","x":"The central message in this card is that although something has been lost, something else has been saved or retained. The situation is not as dark as it seems. Emotional equilibrium needs to be established. Time heals all wounds and the flowing river is indicative of the passage of time being a Universal Law of Nature. The earthing needed to get over the despair is shown by the bridge."},{"t":"p","x":"With the help of emotional supporters, you must try to get back to civilization and your responsibilities which still await for your attention. The upright standing cups are the areas of your life that seek your nurturing. It asks you to retain what is left of the loss and move on in life. Life is a constantly flowing river and one cannot remain stagnated emotionally for an infinite time. You must gather the golden memories of the loss or learn from the lesson imparted but move on you must."}],"id":"five-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Ready to move on after a major loss, sorrowful period coming to an end, realizing power of self and making new plans, positive new developments in personal life, loneliness ending, new family, new property, new avenues of livelihood, turning to spirituality"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Cups05.png"},{"name":"Six of Cups","num":6,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Six","start":189,"end":192,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Sun in Scorpio","Favourable Color":"Blue Yellow Red Blue","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The six of cups is a very positive and warm hearted card full of golden memories and authentic promises for the future. A card of bondings and companionship."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : there are 6 cups filled with white flowers. \\Four of them are beautifully lined up in the foreground. Two children are depicted in the background, one of them passing the cup of flowers to the other. The sixth cup blooming with flowers adorns a lovely stately looking house. A soldier like figure is walking away from the scene, carrying back the sword with him."},{"t":"p","x":"This card highlights the power of the past."},{"t":"p","x":"The 6 of cups is a card of memories. It revives those times when you were happy ; it shows that you can relearn happiness. It can appear in the reading when a strong memory from the past or a person from the past has made an important reentry in your life. This is a positive development as being with this presence or memory takes you back to times when you were happy and carefree. Something about that time or circumstances has brought out the best from you. That spark of excellence is really pleasant to relive as it will fill your present with new inspiration and a lightheartedness. The gloom or anxiety of the present times will just melt away."},{"t":"p","x":"It may also describe a very emotional natured person who prefers to live in the hazy past and imagined times of the times gone by rather than face the challenges of the present. There may be an eagerness to recreate the history in the present and escape the confines / limitations that the present offers. Its often a rose tinted way of looking at life and is divorced from reality."},{"t":"p","x":"As they say, its refreshing to travel down the memory lane at times but not to linger there. The past has a sneaky way of capturing you, unguarded, into a time warp and does not allow you to make healthy relationships in the present context."},{"t":"p","x":"This card’s appearance may indicate reunion with old family members, meeting an ancestor, ancestral house, visit to home, school or educational institution meet up, visiting the family shrine or even the places associated with your childhood or places where you spent spontaneous times. Is stressful times abound, its time to travel the time machine and open up an old photo album, watch an old holiday video or make an appointment with an old friend. Nostalgia and recollections of the past times are the key themes here and one must make deliberate efforts to go down that lane. When this card comes up, its a time to let your heart rule your head. Its a time to spread happiness and kindness all around. So be easy with people and situations around you and treat them with a soft attitude of understanding."},{"t":"p","x":"Sometimes an old relationship may be rekindled in order that you might gain from the experience in terms of personal growth. In case a surrounding card is the Star or Ace of Cups, then an old flame or good friend may return significantly in your life. By itself this card does not say whether the partnership will be revived or you will again go your separate ways. But when supported by cards as above, does indicate that the partners have grown on a soul level through the experiences on their individual life journeys. They now cross paths to teach each other some new lessons and perhaps initiate a beautiful relationship oriented towards higher goals."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can also describe something old, like an antique that turns out to be valuable. It can indicate you rediscovering an old hobby or talent and find an opportunity to hone it in present context. Ancestral property and gains may also be indicated by this card."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears, its time to connect with the past and be discerning enough to know what component of the past can help you deal with the present in a better way and in fact lay the foundation for a brighter future."}],"id":"six-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Clinging to the past and ignoring the present, Learning and derive solace from past experiences but not lingering there, realizing the power to create the present moment, disrespect to elders, not learning from past mistakes"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups06.png"},{"name":"Seven of Cups","num":7,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Seven","start":192,"end":194,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Venus in Scorpio","Favourable Color":"Blue Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Gray card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"This is a Gray card of the Cups suit and indicates mental confusions, an attitude of non decisiveness, falling into the trap of temptations that detract you from progressing in life and at times to the vices of substance abuse."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The card shows seven cups floating in the air while a man in darkness stands in front of them and seems to be in a situation of choosing one or several of the options available. From afar the cups look tempting and shiny and holding great promise but a closer inspection will yield forth the truth that they may contain unpleasant and even dangerous objects. This card majorly talks of being sidetracked by the glitter that life offers us. However all that glitters is not Gold and one must sue careful powers of discernment and patience to study the various options and select the one which will actually lead us to our well being. The others are just red herrings to test our mental powers and power of selectivity."},{"t":"p","x":"The seven of cups warns us against wishful thinking, indulging in whims or concentrating on daydreams that will never amount to anything."},{"t":"p","x":"You should be very tough headed when making an important decision of life. The seven of cups is a card of emotions being susceptible to pursue that which looks easy or attractive. However just as in the picture there might be lurking dangers as denoted by the snake."},{"t":"p","x":"As a card that appears for the future time, its a card full of potential and choice for you. Choice is a big power that the human mind is bestowed with. Its a blessing by the Universe to be able to exercise Free Will and use your aptitude, judgement and experience to be able to make a choice at an important juncture in life."},{"t":"p","x":"The only caution with this card is to use this gift of choice carefully. One of these opportunities will be very favourable for you and will lead to success and contentment."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can sometimes a person too spoilt for choice. He may be surrounded an excess of positive support, even pampering. In such a case or when his heart is very malleable to peer pressure, he may get attracted into bad d company and be prone to indulging in alcoholism, drug use, gambling or easy relations with the opposite sex."}],"id":"seven-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Being too imaginative to the point of delusional, mental disorders, resisting pleasures of life, self sacrificing attitude, celibacy and abstinence, giving up planning and moving to action stage, taking help of an advisor to choose the best option available"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Cups07.png"},{"name":"Eight of Cups","num":8,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Eight","start":194,"end":197,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Saturn in Pisces","Favourable Color":"Blue Red Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Gray card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The eight of cups brings in the message for walking away from the excesses of the world; a time of retreat and solitude and search for peace of mind and a higher purpose in life. Imagery :A singular person, with his back to us is waling towards a mysterious cave. Eight cups all upright and apparently brimming with their resources line up the foreground but the person is in total disregard of them. His focus is elsewhere. The Moon is peculiar, as in its denoted both as Full Moon as well as New Moon. Full moons are a classic symbol of endings and New Moon of beginnings. This is indicating that one cycle has to end before a fresh beginning may be made. When the eight of cups comes in a reading, you are saturated with the material abundance and all the rigours that have gone into accumulating and then multiplying it."},{"t":"p","x":"Life has become a never ending conveyor belt of demand and supply, You feel burned out and at the mercy of the world asking for your emotional and mental inputs. You feel an innate desire to retreat to a place where the clocks ticks slower for you and you can be in solitude to replenish your creative energies."},{"t":"p","x":"This card literally points to taking time out for a retreat or a meditation camp or a time period communing with nature like a hiking trip or a nature sabbatical. It is time to clear your own system by filling it with Universal energy such that your original aura is restored, unmarred by the corruption of the needy persons and situations around you."},{"t":"p","x":"There is more hope embedded in this card than apparent initially. The soul is thirsting for more knowledge about the Universal Truth when this card and its tendency appears in a person’s life. You realize that the material manifestations are a mere myth."},{"t":"p","x":"The all pervading Consciousness that exists within each of us will need careful nurturing and a blankness to be felt and experienced. 8 of cups is a classic card for such deep level yearnings and the resultant Ecstasy. The New Moon is the empty but promising vessel of the heart while the Full Moon indicates the joy that will fill it once the alignment with the Divine is made."},{"t":"p","x":"In relationship and emotional issues, this card is not very positive. It generally indicates that the alliance has run out its course and one of the parties does not want to cling on and wants to retreat from the relationship. Its also heartening in a way because there is the maturity to realize when the relationship has become more of a burden than a blessing. It takes courage to enable able to walk away from a relationship yet its a choice that will give immense peace in the long run."},{"t":"p","x":"If the situation is that of a marriage and children or other family members’ responsibilities are involved, then the retreat may not always be so evident. The partners will develop an indifference between them and be mentally divorced from each other, even though they may be living under the same roof. Mental isolation is also an important attribute of this card. In general, this card carries bleak news. There may be failures and disappointments when this card comes for success or achievement related question. The eight of cups carries a sense of inevitability. There might be the end of cherished hopes and dreams. However instead of self guilt, one needs to detach from the negative situation and retreat into contemplation and analyse the causes of the disappointment and also realize how the unrequited desire could be part of God’s larger divine plan for your well-being."}],"id":"eight-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Holding on to a rotting relationship or an idea, afraid to give up comfort zone, selfishness and possessiveness, avoiding a confrontation, denying your spiritual side, overindulgence in luxuries and power, escaping necessary commitments, pretentious spiritualism"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Cups08.png"},{"name":"Nine of Cups","num":9,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Nine","start":197,"end":200,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Jupiter in Pisces","Favourable Color":"Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"h","x":"Chakra"},{"t":"p","x":"This is an incredibly positive card of the Tarot, Also termed the\"Wish Fulfillment” Card as it carries news of your dreams and desires coming true."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : A prosperous and middle-aged man is sitting on a wooden bench while his arms are crossed, and his face is showing quite a level of contentment. He is dressed elegantly and has the look of the true satisfaction. The head-dress on his head is red, and is a depiction of fertile mind capable of manifesting. Nine golden cups, in the background on a U shaped table are structured and arranged in an orderly manner. The Nine of Cups symbolizes a representation of fulfillment and success, both spiritually and materially. The man shows that expression of success after achieving his innermost desire. There is no negative undertone in this card. Its a card of triumph, of complete success, almost of satiety. Everything you have hoped for, planned for is about to come true. In fact this card is about MANIFESTATIONS of your visualization. The events will unfold almost exactly or in a better way than you have been visualizing. If there are unfavourable supporting cards in the spread, the positivity may be delayed but it can never dilute the brilliance of this card’s success. This is your hour. Much like the figure in the image, the Universe is favouring you. You are being showered with success and abundance from all around and your happiness will be ultimate. It talks of favourable results from professional, personal, financial and even spiritual life."},{"t":"p","x":"As its one of the higher cards in the cups suit, the wish fulfillment relates to the heart chakra in a substantial manner. What gives your heart the ultimate joy? What gives it surmounting satisfaction? These questions are an integral part of both the enjoyment as well as analysis of this Tarot card."},{"t":"p","x":"It tells us to clearly go into the process of knowing what gives us happiness and also\"take action on making your dreams coming true”. It talks not just of destined success but advises us encouragingly that the more karma we put into making our dreams our reality, the larger will be the returns and the more vibrant the satisfaction we will derive out of it. Its a card of constant action and never of inaction. It indicates that you should always be prepared to take full advantage of the favourable situation, much like the Wheel of Fortune Major Arcana. Time wheel is spinning in your favour and you should be on high energy mode to take suitable action to turn your wish into reality."},{"t":"p","x":"Its also a warning card to not let success get to your head. Do not be so immersed in the enjoyment phase that you become ignorant of the undercurrents of the environment. When this card appears in a reading, the person is generally enjoying the fruits of his labour. He is relaxed and in a generous mood. Socialising & partying, lassitude and simply being in emotional cocoon will be his general orientation. Such opportunity can be taken advantage of by an adversary who are waiting in tow for the guards to be down."},{"t":"p","x":"Thus its a warning to not be complacent about the success but also to safeguard it judiciously."},{"t":"p","x":"There is also a chance that you so smug in your prosperity that you might ignore the plight of those who come to you for help or succour. This card may imbue you with a sense of superiority and unlimited good luck. Beware ! It may not last forever so continue giving back to the society so that by the Law of Attraction more of abundance might keep getting attracted back to you."},{"t":"p","x":"All in all, this card indicates happy endings. If you have recently been struggling with low finances or a troublesome relationship or a general adverse fortune, now the times will turn dramatically for you. Provided your efforts have been going on in the direction of your dreams, Dame Fortune will soon bring a smile of contentment on your face."}],"id":"nine-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Smugness and arrogance, superficiality and hypocrisy, being stingy with abundance, non\u0002helpful attitude, being so self satisfied that cannot notice feelings of others’, using money to get your ways unethically and illegally, feeling emotionally empty and still seeking more to acquire"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups09.png"},{"name":"Ten of Cups","num":10,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Ten","start":200,"end":203,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Mars in Pisces","Favourable Color":"Blue Green","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Ten of Cups is perhaps the most joyful and optimistic cards of the Tarot deck. It ushers in a sense of contentment and of completion. Your life looks perfect at the moment, to you. All that you ever wanted, is within your reach. Imagery : A couple is looking out at the lush landscape while a pair of children play happily nearby. A rainbow envelopes their happiness providing a colorful and reassuring support of the Divine over their blessed life."},{"t":"p","x":"The Rainbow is like the proverbial. gold at the end of the rainbow. All the efforts have finally been paid off. You have achieved something that is giving you immense pleasure and a sense of completion. The family life is very peaceful and full of cooperation when this card makes an appearance. People are extremely satisfied with each other and offer their gratitude for the privileges they are receiving. This mutual respect for each other is contagious and makes the entire environment very positive and calming, even for outsiders. When this card comes for a relationship or an impending marriage issue, the prophecy is of extra compatibility where there will be negligible conflict."},{"t":"p","x":"You should rejoice and take stock of your success, and feel your confidence surging at your achievements over the long emotional journey. The tens of any suit represent the whole of the situation, the environment of the situation. The ten of cups shows that our emotional enjoyment is being extended out into the rest of our life. It now encompasses our work life, our friendships and perhaps even our finances are associated to our happiness. This is a good time to acknowledge just ow well respected and well loved we are."},{"t":"p","x":"Sometimes this card appears when you are trying to move out of a difficult phase into one that will much easier on your nerves and emotions. If this card appears as a card after a dark card like Ten of Swords or Three of Swords or The Tower, its a very welcome salve for the wounds on the psyche. You are in serious need of some respite from being battle weary and this card will bring soothing times to the battle weary. It can also indicate moving into a larger or grander home or buying luxuries that will upgrade you socially. This card can indicate expensive purchases like designer clothes or connoisseur jewellery or taking an expensive exotic trip. Unlike the Nine of cups which also spells contentment and achievement of what the person holds dear to his heart, this card is a notch more positive."},{"t":"p","x":"While the Nines bring in success, it may be short-lived and furthermore you will have to safeguard it zealously lest it be taken away from you. Ten of cups spells long lasting happiness and abundance, which you can enjoy with a relaxed heart and mind."},{"t":"p","x":"The card is a beacon of hope. It brings in knowledge that your life is progressing in a way that it is meant to. You are aligned with your higher goals. Your sense of self worth is high and you are in your Golden Period being extra productive at whatever you engage in. You are at home with yourself and have much to be grateful for"}],"id":"ten-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Non fulfillment of wishes, feeling emotionally empty and cheated, loss of family life, childlessness, children ignoring parents/elders, no interest in material possessions, unrealistic ideas about a perfect world, marital troubles and divorce"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups10.png"},{"name":"Page of Cups","num":11,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Page","start":203,"end":205,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Personification Of Water (Element Only)","Favourable Color":"Blue Pink","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"This is the beginning of a new phase in your life that involves your emotions in a major way. It could be the initiation of a new relationship or a partnership or a professional venture that is also close to your heart and not merely pursued for ambitious or monetary reasons."},{"t":"p","x":"Whats important to note here is that the status of this situation is very fragile at the moment. The Page indicates an early gestational period of a relationship or creative venture. It will require protection from harsh factors and a bit of protective nurturing. A budding romance with this card continues to develop well into a meaningful relationship. It will be enjoyable for you and though it may never become very intense or convert into a legal commitment, it will always remain a friendship you will cherish due to genuine affection for each other. Page of cups also refers to a creative or spiritual opportunity. For example you could initiate a course of study that tells you about the global patterns or various languages of the world or helps you gain multicultural knowledge about a particular subject like art appreciation course of art styles across countries of the world."},{"t":"p","x":"The Page is a message bearer and what kind of message it will bring to you depends on the nature of the suit. The Page of cups will bring to you some news about a new relationship or a message from someone you already know. It will be a gentle and encouraging energy the Page will carry, unless surrounded by a volatile card that can darken the message. As a person, the Imagery of the Page of Cups is a young fellow, possibly an adolescent or a young adult. This person will be creative and sensitive. He will be fickle in his interests and his attachments to persons and issues of interest may keep changing frequently. He is ruled by the waves of the heart and may be a poet, a painter or a composer."},{"t":"p","x":"The wave imbued river in the background indicates his fluctuating emotions. He is prone to rapid changes in moods. The fish he is looking at so intently springs from his subconscious so the appearance of this card indicates messages in dreams or during deep meditation or the angels trying to make contact with you through one of the Four Clair senses. He will be helpful and innocent at heart. He may also be a gentle spiritual presence in your life, a wee bit ethereal and wrapped up in his own world. When the page of cups appears, its not necessary the person is already in your life. He is a subtle presence and you may not have even recognised him till date.Sometimes this card describes a person who will never play a major or visible role in your life. He will simply support you at a time and help you reach your goal."}],"id":"page-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Fear of entering relationships, naive and immature person, wishy washy in decision making, dreamy and impressionable person, no clear cut goals and passions, disconnected from Intuition, disappointing news in love and matters of interest, non-commital in heart related matters"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups11.png"},{"name":"Knight of Cups","num":12,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Knight","start":205,"end":207,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Aquarius / Pisces","Favourable Color":"Blue Gray","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Knight of Cups is a person who is active and dynamic. His heart rules over his head and all his thoughts and actions are emotionally driven. However as a person he is helpful with innate goodness and generosity of heart."},{"t":"p","x":"This card talks of being wary of letting emotions rule your decisions. It warns to be pragmatic and analytical before making emotional commitments. There may be risks in trusting wrong people and one should not be so gullible so as to be emotionally manipulated. The Knight however is emotionally vulnerable and at times gets caught in the emotional trap set by people not wanting his well being."},{"t":"p","x":"In the Imagery, the Knight is important because he gives us the message of taking action in the area where our love lies. The Knight is astride a horse and carrying the cup of love or creativity as the case may be. He has set out to make his dream a reality. Follow your dream, says the Knight of Cups. Your creativity is at an all time high and you could be really successful at making great contacts with people who can help you succeed and appreciate your talents. Its not a time to be coy or shy but rather be very transparent about your creative talents as well as aspirations. Its the perfect time to make a business out of your creative hobby."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes up, there could be a period of intense emotional growth for you. It could even be a powerful spiritual experience that will raise your vibration irrevocably. The Knight of cups could herald an enjoyable time for you where you will open yourself up emotionally and embrace new feelings and sensations. It will provide more meaning to your life and make you feel more self worthy."},{"t":"p","x":"Additional meanings of this card are relocation to a calmer place, travel across waters or to a peaceful retreat, a spiritual camp or meditative experience. The white horse in this image moves gently and pleasantly so the pace is languid and self exploratory. The whiteness of the horse indicates the flavour of the image to be full of light and love."}],"id":"knight-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Creative energy has been blocked mostly due to emotional reasons and feeling of frustration;"},{"t":"p","x":"person caught in own world and disconnected from reality, fantasy or substance abuse, false promises of love"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups12.png"},{"name":"Queen of Cups","num":13,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"Queen","start":207,"end":210,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Gemini / Cancer","Favourable Color":"Blue Purple","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The mistress of the misty and elusive world of emotions, the Queen of cups is known for her idealistic and imaginative nature and her dexterity in understanding the complex world of feelings and creativity."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The Queen of Cups is an extremely emotional figure who sits astride a white throne, draped in pristine white cloak and gazes wistfully and intently at the chalice of emotions she holds,. This chalice is bigger and more ornamental than all others in the suit of cups indicating her high stature and that she is a master of emotions.He imagery evokes a sense of other worldliness and her being self absorbed as she dips and surfaces in the enigmatic pools of the world of the subconscious."},{"t":"p","x":"As a situation card, the queen of cups denotes a period where you are on a creative high. You will be inspired to create beauty and aesthetics out of your wells of imagination. You will feel mellow and soft, receptive to the emotional vibes and conversations around you."},{"t":"p","x":"Its also a time of extreme patience. The emotional intensity of people around you may be high; there might be histrionics or there might be aggression in the air. The Queen simply waits patiently. Patience is the most difficult art to practise-it requires immense self control and the Queen of Cups has mastered this art. Of waiting. Of the natural rhythms taking over. Gradually all tumult dies down. Whether its in the environment or within your own mind."},{"t":"p","x":"So when the Queen comes, the solution can be of non-action. You cannot stop your mind from chasing thoughts; the Mind will not listen because it is genetically programmed to be active. When you stop the action, when you do Absolutely nothing, the Mind slows down. This eases the emotions and gradually the emotional balance is restored. The Queen wants emotional balance and teaches you how to achieve that."},{"t":"p","x":"Its a time also to be careful about the emotional health of the company you keep. You are like a sponge picking up on their emotional ebbs and flows. You must avoid spending long periods of time with those who are angry, negative or who drain your energy."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person she is the ruler of the emotional and imaginative realm. Her throne is at the border of the vast ocean. The vastness and infinite depth of the ocean are akin to the depths and mysteries of the human heart. The deepest part of the human emotion is the subconscious. The waves and wisdom of the subconscious are still an enigma for most. This queen has the intuitive gift of ploughing deep into the subconscious and providing guidance and support."},{"t":"p","x":"The advice this queen offers is startlingly perceptive in its level of insight. It carries a very uncanny level of Truth. Generally this queen is sensitive of others’ feelings but when she is articulating a channeled message based on her divine connection with the Almighty, she can be direct and piercing."},{"t":"p","x":"She needs to cushion her words in a less direct way to avoid offending those who seek her for her wise counsel. This queen has a direct connection with the angelic realm. It is symbolized by the handles of the cup she is holding which are shaped like angel wings. Images of cherubs and angelic figures also adorn her throne and envelop her as the Earth Mother. She is a gifted psychic and clairvoyant and maybe an experience expert at tarot and angel card readings. She is a wonderful maternal figure and the classic earth mother. She cares about her own home, her extended family, her circle of friends and emotional links and also the environment. She may be the pivot around which environmental campaigns are functioning and she teaches all the inter connectivity of the Five elements and how to restore balance in the eco-system."},{"t":"p","x":"She is a also an excellent cook and her favourite fields of excellence are hospitality, nursing, healing, medicine, psychotherapy, counselling, training and education related disciplines."},{"t":"p","x":"She manifests our Yin or the feminine element of the complete human energy system. Her qualities of femininity, receptivity, calmness, emotional understanding, nurturing and empathy are called upon to be harnessed when her presence comes up in your reading."}],"id":"queen-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Oversensitive, no control of emotions and feeling of being emotionally overwhelmed, lives each emotion to excess, Self sacrificing, dreamy and escapist;"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups13.png"},{"name":"King of Cups","num":14,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Cups","rank":"King","start":210,"end":214,"meta":{"Element":"Water","Planets":"Moon, Mars, Jupiter","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Libra / Scorpio","Favourable Color":"Blue Red Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Sacral/Swadishthana Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The King of Cups is the most powerful card in the cups suit and depicts maturity, generosity, wisdom, and emotional balance."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : An aged king sits with a melancholy expression on his throne with an amulet around his neck in the shape of a fish which represents his emotional depths and the spirit of creativity. Behind the king is a fish jumping out of the ocean representing emotional impulses and on the right is a ship sailing on high tide representing emotional management in the material world. This king epitomizes control over emotions to charted the changing tides of the material, practical world. As a situation the King of Cups is a direct reference to you having to face an emotionally challenging situation. There could be a heartbreak or an issue of inter-personal conflict. A situation will arise where you will need to exercise your emotional maturity. This will call upon you to suppress your innate emotional impulse, analyse the situation objectively and take a calm and balanced decision. The king of cups is a very influential figure in the Tarot court as also the real life when his energies are called upon."},{"t":"p","x":"Self control over own emotional space is the biggest lesson that this card brings upon us. The human mind is frail and whimsical and falls continuous prey to the vagaries of the emotions that surge within. You must learn to be\"mindful” of own emotions. Begin by developing a greater self-awareness and a deeper knowledge of yourself."},{"t":"p","x":"When faced with a challenge that elicits a spontaneous reaction from you, pause and try to maneuver it to a moderate level. Avoid any extreme reaction. Respond to an emotional situation; do not react to it. So any sudden demonstration of anger or sadness or happiness must be moderated and then expressed. This makes you powerful and effective in dealing life situations. You are still sensitive but you use your mind to filter the excesses of the emotion."},{"t":"p","x":"Remember, says this card, excess of any emotion is toxic and will lead to emotional problems subsequently so learn to master your own emotions first. Try to understand the situation, the person before you in a state of awareness and then calibrate your emotional response to best flow with the situation at hand."},{"t":"p","x":"Tempering the intensity of your emotions will give you an astounding command over the challenges in your life, even the unexpected ones. So do not fly off the handle at an unpleasant scenario nor go happily overboard when events are in your favour. Maintain your emotional equilibrium and you will be more hi-functioning and successful in the material world. You may need to act in an advisory capacity and without being emotionally biased, act friendly and helpful. Having self awareness will help you to judge the problem objectively form various angles, without getting emotionally dragged into it. The counsel you can impart then, is fair and supportive."},{"t":"p","x":"Cups is also connected with spirituality and religion so the King of Cups may represent a situation where you go in for such studies or make advanced research into these subjects. You may even be offered a role of a religious or spiritual adviser or you may someone highly influential from these disciplines. You may also be asked to head a negotiation or arbitration problem. This could be in the outside world or even at the domestic level. You need to exercise your attributes of tact, diplomacy and being objective in such a demanding environment. Remain mature while dealing with negative energy. Shield yourself not to get affected by energy suckers and focus on the constructive role you need to play in the emotionally volatile situation."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person, the King of Cups is an emotionally mature person. He has one through multitude of sufferings in his own life, done his inner transformation work and emerged a richer, stronger person in terms of being able to manage his emotional impulses. Nothing takes hi by surprise and he links the emotionally needy humans as just another element of the cosmic cycle undergoing their karmic circus. He may decide to document his understanding of human emotional experiences and may be an effective management guru or a writer of life-issues or a mentor or a spiritual influencer. He will come across as an empathetic and wide person but noticeably he will also have an enigmatic air to him that may make him unapproachable. He shields himself from energy vibes and that gives him his strength of being able to analyse emotions in a dispassionate manner and offering constructive solutions to the world."},{"t":"p","x":"He is generally a successful person in his field with a strong love for Reading on intellectual and psychological issues and engaging in creative pursuits like art, music, theatre, writing or photography. He is insanely attracted to emotional issues but operates on a higher level of understanding of the emotional world and that imparts him his royal status."}],"id":"king-of-cups","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Shows immaturity, inexperience and insincerity."},{"t":"p","x":"Shallow & has not understood the depth of life, Untrustworthy & fickle minded"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Cups14.png"},{"name":"Ace of Swords","num":1,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Ace","start":214,"end":216,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Root Of Powers Of Air (All Air Signs Combined)- Gemini, Libra, Aquarius","Favourable Color":"White Blue Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Ace of swords is a card of triumph. To an extreme degree the Triumph has come from a show of force. The Force can be a physical force, the force of willpower or force of position or circumstances. The crown with vines at the top shows unmitigated ambition and the intellectual acumen needed to hit the bull’s eye."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : An upright sword, held aloft by a strong hand. Its piercing through a crown laden with vines and foliage. When this card appears you have recently won a high position through your own efforts and calibre and you will be feeling both the Euphoria and the power of your conquest. This card can also show the birth of a child or an idea or a new endeavour. What is important to note when this card appears in the reading is that you have been invested with tremendous power from the universe to make a difference in any area that you choose to make it in. It is up to your individual discretion whether you want to love with passion or hate with intensity but extreme feelings will soar inside you. This intensity will also influence very noticeably other persons surrounding you. You are riding high on the crest of the power wave, The upright sword which is a part of the imagery of this card is sharp, unidirectional and very focused. Your intellect is razor sharp at the moment. There is a subject or an issue that you have been thinking about, almost obsessing over it and it has a powerful effect on you."},{"t":"p","x":"This is also a Karmic card because the changes that will come after executing this decisiveness will influence your destiny for times to come. When the Ace of swords appears in a reading it also time to take a tough decision about something. Your attitude must transform to being objective and dispassionate. There is no room for emotional weakness or emotional considerations when this card comes up. Surrounded by emotional cards could have an adverse meaning. It could show that you are being too ruthless about an issue and need to tone down your sharpness and your decision is going to affect other persons so a hint of consideration for others should be amalgamated."},{"t":"p","x":"If the situation is regarding falling in love or assessing a new attachment, this card is very prophetic because it indicates karmic connection and that you will be connected with each other across lifetime.You may not be in permanent relationship but will leave a mental impression so sharp that you will either influence their ideas for a lifetime or even meet at opportune times across the years. The Ace of swords carries tremendous latent power and it is up to the human intelligence to use it for the benefit of others and not to create any danger or losses for others. your thought process should be clear but constructive."}],"id":"ace-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Evading the truth, acting out of emotion rather than harsh reality, mental ambiguity, missing the target due to lack of clarity, circumventing the truth and making up pretence talk"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Swords01.png"},{"name":"Two of Swords","num":2,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Two","start":216,"end":219,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Moon in Libra","Favourable Color":"Yellow Gray Blue","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Medium Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Two of swords epitomizes the image of tranquility and balance.It is however not really balance between two forces, rather it is a situation of stalemate where non decisiveness has frozen the moment in time."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : A blindfold woman is sitting on a bench and holding two swords in criss- cross fashion across his eyes. The vast water body at the back indicates the emotional attachments the person is still susceptible to. The swords are in perfect balance indicating the woman's dexterity in maintaining the position. This indicates a contest between two opposing forces where the battle lines are drawn but they are more ideological rather than physical. A difficult decision needs to be made and one of the swords will finally exert itself. When this card comes up, the decision maker is unable to reach a clear decision. He is delaying the inevitability of the decision and holding the cards close to his chest regarding the final outcome of the decision."},{"t":"p","x":"Emotional attachments and weakness may have a lot to do with this decision. The blindfolded woman is reluctant to analyse the facts of the choice in the light of reality. She is living in her own cocoon and is under the illusion that the harsh day of making a judgement will never arrive. She has the mental skills and austerity to be able to hold the contrasting ideologies in perfect balance for a considerable length of time."},{"t":"p","x":"She feels regret at letting one option go and may feel that if a decision is taken it may emotionally hurt one of the parties. She wants to be so fair that she is not taking a stand at all. This sitting on the fence position is really stagnating the situation. This card calls for standing strong for what you believe in and your ability to navigate difficult waters. The implied message is to open your eyes and not avoid the situation."},{"t":"p","x":"The person maintaining this state of non-decision is exerting a lot of energy in doing so. You are fearful of altering the balance not realizing that the so called balance is not natural and since the energies are in conflict with each other they can never blend or be in union."},{"t":"p","x":"Two of swords can also indicate excess worries in the mind. Since this person lacks objectivity of looking at facts in cold light, he might be prone to apprehensions and may be making up choice situations of What if Option A or what is Option B in the recesses of his mind."},{"t":"p","x":"If you are caught in the middle of a dispute, an unpleasant legal case or a corporate battle or a domestic conflict, this card indicates a ceasefire situation in which the parties may regroup to ponder on future possibilities."},{"t":"p","x":"This card appears when the person is going through a very difficult situation of decision making. His loyalty is a divided and he is carefully analysing the pros and cons of both the situations. This is that moment when the person sits in introspection, in Silence He is closed to external influences at the moment it is an internal moment of peace making him dive into the depths of emotional wealth and also the ocean of reason and trying to decide which option is going to serve him best for the coming time."},{"t":"p","x":"You face these mental conflicts in your daily life when you are compelled to make a choice between A and B. Both are dear to you as you have invested materially or emotionally in both of them."},{"t":"p","x":"The moment of decision has arrived when this card comes in the reading. It asks you to be responsible and accountable for your choice and to make a decision as that will enable the progress of the matter. On your decision several other destinities might rest and its time you acted with maturity and courage and being clarity to an ambiguous situation."}],"id":"two-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Making a decision using emotion rather than logic, misplaced emotions, wrongly placed trust, going against own ethic of right vs wrong, taking sides and not being balanced in judgement"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Swords02.png"},{"name":"Three of Swords","num":3,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Three","start":219,"end":222,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Saturn in Libra","Favourable Color":"Gray Red","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Dark Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The three of swords is the card reflecting agony, inner turmoils and necessary painful choices. Its a card of emotional transformation that is churned by personal suffering and eventual realizations. The essence of 3 of swords is not heartbreak as such, but how we deal with it. Swords are about thought and intellect, not emotions. Perhaps you are meant to help others see their sorrows in a new light and truly understand what is causing the pain. That way they can let go of the pain and start healing."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : Three sharp swords are piercing the Heart. The penetration is very acute as the ends of the swords are visible on the reverse of the hearts. Gray clouds surround the bleeding heart and a general air of mourning surrounds this image."},{"t":"p","x":"The nature of the swords suit is very rampant here. It suggests worries and adversity that have hit you to the core of your emotional space."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes up in a reading, the situation will definitely bring painful losses and realisation. Your emotional illusions may be stabbed brutally as you are left shocked and almost lose your balance with the unexpected pain that might impact you."},{"t":"p","x":"There may be a form of treachery that is involved here. The three of swords indicates the eternal triangle where due to direct or concealed incursion of a their party, the balance of the binary union is lost. There are unethical practices and its a time of secrets coming to light, shocking revelations and sneaky behaviors."},{"t":"p","x":"The positive aspect of this card is that when the binary relationship is not strong then the cracks are becoming wider by the entry of the third party. The crack that was always there but which perhaps the two parties were overlooking or just turning a blind eye to. The fundamentals of the relationship were already fractured."},{"t":"p","x":"The 3 of cups will make the chasm more glaring. There will be pain and surprises but also an air of inevitability as the truth pours out of weak loyalties that swayed so easily. Sometimes this card refers to medical procedures like a heart surgery or an invasive surgery of another organ that may cause anxiety and fear."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes up there is also an excess of emotions displayed. There may be an outbreak of tears or hysteria. There may be a verbally colorful and violent spray of words as an emotional outburst. Emotions will be volatile and unstable. This card also indicates separations. A long lasting marriage may come to an end leaving you emotionally disoriented and in trauma. There might be an actual death of a close one, leaving you with a sense of acute loneliness.Even if you are still in a relationship you may be subject to emotional neglect and demeaning. No one is willing is listen to your side of the story and you feel an emptiness deep inside your heart. All such cases of deep sadness are coming up for counselling and healing when the three of swords makes an appearance. Its a powerful and potent card and must be given due importance in the spread. It may lead you to root of a existing problem that may lie in the past and encourage you to gently unravel the painful history of a problem."},{"t":"p","x":"Psychological excavations become important with this card coming up. You may be unable to open up and share past pains and this repression could be creating fresh psych\u0002somatic disorders inside you. This card when already experienced, creates fear inside a person regarding trust and letting go emotionally. This may be a challenge when forming new relationships, whether for work or personal satisfaction."},{"t":"p","x":"It will call for emotional readjustments to bring the emotional quotient to a balanced state. The advice is to accept the pain when it comes. Embracing the pain and riding it in all its severe glory will give you deep strength and the self belief that if you could cross this turbulent time, you are a strong, divinely guided person."}],"id":"three-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"A recent loss or a heartbreak and you are still not fully recovered, slow progress, time to let go of the past and embrace joy of the future, positive card for health situation, being surrounded by a strong support group, internal growth due to pain suffered"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords03.png"},{"name":"Four of Swords","num":4,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Four","start":222,"end":225,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Jupiter in Libra","Favourable Color":"Gray Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Four of swords is a message of rest and rejuvenation. It points to a time when the physical or mental fatigue is acute and one needs time out for solace and regeneration. Its a temporary phase for gearing up for future challenges."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The figure on the Four of Swords is resting in peace on his tomb or an austere bed. His hands are in prayer, and his face is relaxed and tranquil. The Stained glass windows explicitly show this to be the Church, where the weary from the world affairs may rest in peace, either eternally or when alive for a while to restore their composure. Its a very peaceful image."},{"t":"p","x":"Three swords hang on the wall, and one lies under the figure, showing that it--or, what it represents--is more important or personal than the others. Like all fours, the Four of Swords represents foundation. The soldier even while at rest is alert, as the sword at his bedside shows. Rest but be alert. The number Four in Tarot represents stabilityand the beginning of structure in the development from the Ace. Even amidst difficult circumstances, you have now achieved a small cocoon where you can pause and regather your energies. Your conflicting ideas, your aggression, your alpha energy are held in check and in balance for a brief moment. Its a time of no-action and simply to be motionless."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes in the reading, its a deliberate message to leave the battlefield of life and retire to a corner while you cater to your own physical and emotional needs. You might have reached the end of your resources for now and your body, mind and nerves are asking for respite and nourishment."},{"t":"p","x":"The image in the card is of the Church where no swords were allowed and the warriors upon entering had to blunt the edge of the sword before entering."},{"t":"p","x":"The illustration here on the card is very telling of this traditional practice. Swords indicate our Intellect, our mental activities such as thoughts, analysis, worries, plannings. It also rules strife and discord and problems. For the time being, all of these are at rest and in a suspension mode."},{"t":"p","x":"Instead of being charged up or active, you need tobe passive and at rest at the moment. If you have been engaged in a frenetic physical or mental activity of late, you need to pace down and let your natural impulses take over. The body cycles need to come back to equilibrium and a state of naturalness. This card often come up when a person is undergoing a burnout. You might have been engaged in exhausting mental work or negotiations or a personally stressful situation. Your mental abilities seem to have become blunted and even deciding on common mundane issues has become burdensome. This burning out requires immediate reprieve in the form of rest. Become emotionally and mentally isolated and keep the communication to a minimum. All communication requires energy which you really are not in a position to spare for the moment. So accept this and go into voluntary sabbatical for a while."},{"t":"p","x":"If a situation has been calling to you to make a difficult decision which might lead to ego flare ups, then too this card can be helpful. Step back from the minefield. Pause and reflect and contemplate. Pick your arguments and the approach that will be most effective and then take action after a while. You could become interested in meditation and enrol for a course in structured meditation practice or if more actively inspired to join a new fitness or yoga program. These are all earthing activities that bring into union the mind and body along with the 5 elements (Pancha-Mahabhoot) in your energy field."}],"id":"four-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Aggressive attitude, highly competitive, argumentative, not willing to give up or concede defeat, workaholic, relentless search for truth at the cost of personal safety, fond of physical sports and valour games, need to retreat and perhaps meditate and reflect"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Swords04.png"},{"name":"Five of Swords","num":5,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Five","start":225,"end":228,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Venus in Aquarius","Favourable Color":"Blue Gray Red","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Challenging card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"This is a reality check card of the tarot and actually epitomizes that life is gray. Victory and defeat both form the circle of life and one must accept with grace both the sides of the coin. Imagery : A victorious man with a smirk on his face, a defeated man walking away, figures in the distance mourning, a battlefield near a lake."},{"t":"p","x":"As a predictive card, from the loser’s point of view it denotes loss and misfortune. It foretells defeat of your plan or an unhappy situation. The defeat may not be absolute but will be more than what you had expected. If you had expected a victory, its a clear negation of your expectations. Surrounding cards may mitigate the loss but when this card comes up, you should be very careful of a pitfall or a major setback. Its a warning card in true sense of the term. Additional connotations could be possible hidden dangers, discouragement and defeat, tragic circumstances, mourning, destruction and dishonour."},{"t":"p","x":"This is not an easy card to decipher and its interpretation will depend whether the one asking the question is the winner or the loser. Even if the querist is putting his narrative as the loser, it would be pertinent to examine by the tarot reader if he ever has played the role of the deceitful winner in the past and what he is experiencing now may be merely a payback by the Universe."},{"t":"p","x":"In most interpretations you or the querist are at the receiving end by underhand means employed by your opponent."},{"t":"p","x":"This setback is unexpected because you trusted the ethics of your opponent, in some cases he may be a close friend, colleague or life partner."},{"t":"p","x":"The victory has come about by unethical and deceptive means. Victory means the world to the person who has gained an upper hand here and is rather smug and arrogant at the petty victory he has earned by using mental games and manipulative means."},{"t":"p","x":"He has won the game by disarming the opponent. When the opponent’s defences were down, he was caught by surprise and thus had to lay down his weapons. Its not a fair victory and the lesson inherent in this card is that deceitful people may be all around you. If you are in a relationship or a competitive situation where you feel you were pushed into a disadvantage and then defeated then do not be disheartened."},{"t":"p","x":"Its the way smart people function in this manipulative world and one must learn the ways of the world fast. Its a card of great learning and inner transformations."},{"t":"p","x":"The sneaky means were employed because the opponent feared you are smarter or more capable and given a fair chance would have definitely won. Its actually a medal of your calibre that the opponent had to use mental trickery to make you weaker. Take confidence from this fact, re group yourself, strategise and then strike back to even the game. You may even decide to leave this battlefield especially if this card pops up in a relationship or a friendship."},{"t":"p","x":"If an emotional partner subjects you to emotional abuse or to put you down in an embarrassing position, you must seriously consider whether you want to put in your efforts into this emotionally abusive setup. This person is clearly a bully and derives his one upmanship by demeaning the other. This would be an inherent trait in him, not likely to change easily. Decide if you want to stay and counter this passive\u0002aggression or simply choose to walk away and forge a new and fruitful relationship with someone who is comfortable with your excellence."},{"t":"p","x":"The five of swords is a card full of deep wisdom. It persuades us to reconcile ourselves with the disagreeable events that have taken place and to move on from there. The incidents that are analyzed during the 5 of swords may act as a catalyst to help you make healthier choices about where you want to mentally invest in the future."}],"id":"five-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Power struggles, false ego, false sense of intellectual or physical superiority, creating conflict in work due to non harmonious behaviour, loss of love due to petty ego games with partner, cheating in marriage or business collaboration"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords05.png"},{"name":"Six of Swords","num":6,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Six","start":228,"end":231,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Mercury in Aquarius","Favourable Color":"Blue Gray Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"After the upheaval of the five of swords, this card indicates the need to move away from mental stress. Its card of movement towards peace and tranquility and a time of mental restoration. Its a card of planting positive thoughts in our mind. What we plant in our subconscious mind and nourish with waters of emotion, will one day become a reality."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The man is rowing a boat towards a distant island full of succour. The movement is from turbulent waters towards calmer ones. The swords are down-turned and he has fellow passengers who may be his supporters or his dependents. This card indicates movement away from an unpleasant experience into calmer waters. It may not be deliberate at that time since the emotional severity is still battering you and you are moving away from the stress as a reflex reaction. However sometimes a movement away is important to preserve your sanity and at times your safety. You may be physically moving away from a destructive episode, such as an abusive relationship or friends who enable abusive behaviour. As per the image, the water to the right of the boat looks choppy but to the left it is placid. The oarsman might be you/querist or it could even be a saviour who appears as an angel to fish you out of a crisis and take you to calmer shores. Six of swords can mean a physical movement involving change of locations. It can in modern times indicate a relocation of the place of work or even a relocation to another country if the progress opportunities are better there."},{"t":"p","x":"At times, the retreat may be psychological and not involve a physical movement. You may be retreating into an inner space to gain an objective perspective over a troublesome situation. The wide expanse of waters indicate your subconscious and at times when the troubles are within the mind and can only be dealt by self analysis, this is an excellent card of guidance."},{"t":"p","x":"This movement may not be voluntary as is evident from the figures huddles inside the cloak and sailing away in the relative anonymity of darkness. However in the longer run it will bring peace to the ones who were courageous enough to move to calmer environment. Change is always difficult but the feeling of relief that will overcome you once the waters have been traversed will be infinite."},{"t":"p","x":"6 of swords can also also point you out in the direction of taking a holiday.You might be deluding yourself that you cannot break away from the exhausting work surrounding you. This card strongly advises you to take a break where you are completely disconnected from your routine demanding life."},{"t":"p","x":"It will give you better perspective over your existing gifts in life as well as help to orient your future plans in a more balanced manner. Sometimes in the frenzy of mental work we may forget to keep balance in various aspects of our life. In our mad race, the emotional and health aspects may get neglected. This card will sound like a beagel to tell you that the imbalance so being created may lead to great problem in the future so it is best now to break away from the tedium and restore the fabric of your life."},{"t":"p","x":"Mental peace is the greatest treasure in the world, you will realize. Only when the Mind is free to think and analyse, can real happiness be born and in fact recreated."}],"id":"six-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Making of new discoveries and decisions, being careful about what you speak as well as how you speak, taking strong back ups of information and documents, confronting some necessary issues so that relationship can move forward, staying in the field and fighting your battles, feeling alone"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Swords06.png"},{"name":"Seven of Swords","num":7,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Seven","start":231,"end":234,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Moon in Gemini","Favourable Color":"Yellow Red","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Dark card with a smart lining","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The seven of swords is a dangerous card as it warns you of the deceptiveness around. It advises you to be cautious and avoid temptation, rash decision and over-trusting. Imagery : A sneaky looking person is stealthily running away from the circus tent where apparently he works with 5 of the 7 swords tightly clasped to his chest. He looks back over his left shoulder to check is anyone has spotted him in the act of the theft."},{"t":"p","x":"This is literally the card of theft and espionage. If the question is regarding duplicity or deception in any form, this card is a strong Yes. The degree of deception shall be decided by the surrounding cards. If they aggravate the act then there is physical theft or loss of intellectual property (mostly occurs as the swords rules over the mental faculty)."},{"t":"p","x":"If the supporting cards are relatively innocuous then the deception or the desire of deception may just be cooking in the mind and showing a manipulative mind at work."},{"t":"p","x":"Interestingly this card does not show duplicity but rather the act of evading the truth or telling the truth only partially. Seven of swords occurs when the person is dodging an emotional or verbal confrontation and is stealing time away. This could be due to lack of preparedness or just an aversion to being accountable during the confrontation/clarification exercise."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears in the reading, you should be cautious and really tread very carefully. There is a hint of subterfuge here and smart mind(s) may be playing tricks on you. Like the major arcana card of the Moon, the environment is murky and ambiguous and you must use your own intuition and heightened awareness to confide or not to confide. You might be dealing with a narcissistic person who only thinks of own ego gratification and self glory. He may take away from what is due to you and has been the result of your sustained hard work. Beware of work related discredits and non acknowledgement."},{"t":"p","x":"There are times when it is necessary to be evasive or partially omit the truth. Even though you may not believe personally in that ethic, however such an occasion has now arisen. You will have a situation where nothing will be gained by telling the entire truth; it would be better to give them an edited version of the truth.Sometimes you may decide to hold some cards close to your chest as telling the entire truth might bring dis-reputation or create more conflict or misunderstandings. In such instances where omission will help to salvage a situation or prevent it from worsening, the seven of swords approach may be adopted but remember that Truth does find its own way out and will do so sooner or later so handle the situation with maturity. Evading the truth is also sometimes a manner of self defence. If you know that is the reason try to form a cordial bond with the person concerned so he may become more comfortable with you and gradually open up about the other facts too."},{"t":"p","x":"In legal cases, this card can work against you as high level of dishonesty may be at play against you. The opponent could use dark methods to transfer the blame from oneself to you. All forms of theft are indicated by this card. Take extra care of your belongings. Be almost obsessively careful about the security of your documentation."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person the seven of swords is a genius person who is very high on ideas and may be a research or scientific genius. Its shows cleverness and the mental dexterity to over-smart the other party and to come out unscathed of a troublesome situation. He is a person who like a double edged sword will get to the root of the matter and makes an excellent detective, Intelligent agent and surgeon."}],"id":"seven-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Choosing ethics over deception, choosing to do what feels right to your Conscience, Ready to face punishment or repercussions of a folly previously committed, apology and regret, turning over a new leaf, restoring the rights of someone you may have cheated, turning to moralistic way of living"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords07.png"},{"name":"Eight of Swords","num":8,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Eight","start":234,"end":237,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Jupiter in Gemini","Favourable Color":"Gray Blue Red","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Dark card that can Empower","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Eight of swords is about freedom from ideological imprisonments and the feeling of being trapped and unable to move in a constructive direction. Swords represent thoughts and one becomes a victim of thoughts-of others and more cripplingly of self limitation."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The woman is standing helpless, blindfold on eyes, hands tied behind her. Her robe is red and 8 swords are piecing the ground on either side, as if cordoning her off. Eight of swords is a card of emotional turmoil. when the excesses of the material world have become very difficult to comprehend and the soul is screaming for some solitude and emptiness, this card becomes significant."},{"t":"p","x":"The external demands; the external sounds ; external noises has started barraging your brain to an extent that you cannot think Straight."},{"t":"p","x":"this is the time when the person needs active support and a helping hand to come out of the inner hell. This is the point when many suffering from the eight of swords syndrome for a prolonged period fall prey to depression or decide to end their life through suicide."},{"t":"p","x":"This is a very strongly negative card in the tarot and must be taken seriously. If needed, expert medical care must be provided to the person whose spread is being analyzed. Self survival is the most Primal Instinct of all human beings. The need to be alone in order to sort out the feelings and thoughts is strong when this card is impacting."},{"t":"p","x":"There are voices in the head that are weakening you. They could be the voices of years or even generations of mental conditioning which highlight your perceived weaknesses and why you should not be breaking away and making your own path. They lead to self defeating attitudes and behaviors and all this suppression creates tragic conditions, at times. Most of these sounds are only clamouring for your attention. They have no real meaning or relevance for your future life. This card can also be self defensive. In that case it should be only till the time the shock is over and you have rediscovered your latent courage. At times you may have been hurt so badly in the past that you may choose to cut yourself off emotionally so that there is no risk of history repeating itself. However this will make you many new joys that life may have lined up for you. Always remember if someone did not turn out as you expected, a greater good is meant for you. Its only a matter for divine timing to deliver it to you."},{"t":"p","x":"The eight swords surrounding you are nothing but attention demanding voices who are sucking on your mental energies. You are encouraged to take off the blindfold and look in front of you. The water in front is your gentle intuition and the paved road is the supporting path that will take you to your future. Pick up one of the swords and cut through the inhibitions of stereotypes and societal norms that hold you back from exercising your individuality."},{"t":"p","x":"You are stuck in a trap of your own making. When you stop heeding the voices, they will dwindle and go away. What we give energy to; simply grows. The moment your energy shifts to your own improvement, all the defeating factors will start losing their strength."},{"t":"p","x":"You will find you were blocking your own path once you start assessing your own strengths in bright light. This is the card of Self Empowerment and finding your true identity."}],"id":"eight-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Voicing your opinion freely, release of unwanted fears and anxiety, being in a space of mental clarity and enthusiasm, finding a solution to a problem, high sense of self belief and the energy to carry plans forward, courage and personal power"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords08.png"},{"name":"Nine of Swords","num":9,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Nine","start":237,"end":239,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Mars in Gemini","Favourable Color":"Black Blue","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Dark card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Nine of Swords is one of the darkest cards of the Tarot deck and signifies a phase of deep worry and anxiety. This mental darkness is symbolised by nine swords hanging above the figure’s head indicating the deep state of mental distress. Imagery : A man sits up in bed in darkness of night. The bed and quilt are ornate. He has his face covered with his hands and is fraught with tension."},{"t":"p","x":"Interestingly, The swords are equal in length pointing to the fact of an obsessive thought is repeating itself in the mind space and leading the person to keep awake even at nights. Some people call this the\" Nightmare Card” as it may indicate those worries or thoughts that do not allow us to have any rest and keep thrashing around in the head."},{"t":"p","x":"It can also indicate having excessive thoughts about a person or an event and going over in the mind about possible eventualities. When this card comes up, beware of extreme negative thinking. This could be generated by real events / situations, and at times by obsessing over a thought or a possibility to an excessive degree. The imagination has to be separated gently from the real problem and then the future course of action sought."},{"t":"p","x":"Nine of swords is a card for loud noises and arguments and voices in the head. This card also describes the abject grief and desolation that follows a bereavement or a major irrevocable loss of some kind. A cherished relationship might have ended, a loved one may have died, a bankruptcy may be about to occur, a serious illness could have been diagnosed."},{"t":"p","x":"Nine of swords can also at times be a result of an exaggerated imagination. You might believe that the worst will happen and you will be left without an anchor. Your imagination may be churning in over drive creating terrifying scenarios that have little or no roots in reality. Also indicates loneliness and a feeling of helplessness. The surrounding cards are important when coupled with nine of swords, as their elemental nature could direct to the cause of the worry. Coupled with Major Arcanas like the Tower or the Moon, could show mental disorders. As feelings, nine of swords also signifies guilt, fears and shame. This person needs support, wise counselling and analysing the cause of the stress. Shows person who is stagnating in own loop of negative thoughts and feeling of low self worth, under\u0002confidence and inability to handle life situations. When this card comes, we must learn the lesson that life will be suffused with struggles and opposing forces. With extreme patience and balance of composure, one must look at brighter lining in our life, seek professional or trusted counselling, and work diligently towards shedding the darkness surrounding us."}],"id":"nine-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Very pessimistic thoughts, self destructive behaviour, need for professional therapy, mental disorders, health deterioration, phobias and fears, hallucinations, suicidal tendancies, time for spiritual solace"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords09.png"},{"name":"Ten of Swords","num":10,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Ten","start":239,"end":242,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Sun in Gemini","Favourable Color":"Black Brown Red","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Dark Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Ten of swords is a prophetic card and portends sorrow, despair and deep trouble about to come soon. It signifies an end or a closure. With almost nil chance of recovery. Definite End of a cycle."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery :A warrior like figure lies face down on the ground. Ten swords pierce his back. There is darkness in the background. This is a horrifying card visually. Here the image itself speaks a thousand words as the brave warrior lies absolutely still and prostate on the hard earth and ten swords protrude from his back. The wounds have been inflicted by someone else, as is evident by the positioning of the swords."},{"t":"p","x":"The failure will not be easily overcome. This is not a fortune to be avoided or changed, only to be endured.Its a card of tragic and darkly dramatic endings. The situations have left you completely vanquished and demoralized. As though you have been slain and the last drop of your blood has been drawn out. You are now nothing but a skeleton, a caricature of the living dead. If you ever had the feeling of walking like a zombie with no energy left within you, so difficult have been the circumstances, this card may well describe your condition."},{"t":"p","x":"Mostly this condition is due to acute betrayal where you feel you have been stabbed in the back, Sometimes fortune does not seem to be your companion even for a bit and you will meet failure after failure or rejection after rejection. This incremental loss leads to the stamina being depleted, the morale crumbling and you may have a nervous collapse. The 10 of swords is a card of endings; and it indicates that a particular chapter of a relationship is over. Its not always the end of the relationship but rather the dimension and form it had been currently in. Though this card is bleak, yet at times a sharp turning point is needed. This is that sharp point of re\u0002thinking, re-strategising and re-adjustments that you need to make with a sense of surrender and acceptance."},{"t":"p","x":"You have hit rock bottom, the nadir of the issue you are so in despair about. After hitting this point the wheel of life can only take you up towards better experiences."},{"t":"p","x":"The dark sky at the back of the sky heralds the dawn which is symbolic of a fresh morning always awaiting the darkest of dark night."},{"t":"p","x":"This blow in the back, metaphorically seems that the threat came from the other side and caught up with you without adequate preparation. However this is not always the case in the battle field of life. Very rarely do crisis come without a warning. There is always a warning gong but we may be too self absorbed to notice it."},{"t":"p","x":"When this card comes its also a time of self introspection and looking back at the flow of events that have brought you to this juncture. Have you been ignoring the warning signs that something is wrong in the hope that self corrective measures will themselves come into practice. Did you act out of fear of being alone and went along in a toxic relationship. Did you keep hoping for a windfall in the business and made indiscriminate investments."},{"t":"p","x":"You must remember every reaction you are facing has been created by action also perpetuated you at an earlier date. Look for the root cause of the crisis that now befalls you. It had to be a faulty thought or action on your part at some point in assessable past."},{"t":"p","x":"The ten of swords is a secretly hopeful card ; it reveals that the worst has befallen us already, there is an inherent relief that you have survived the final calamity related to the question and that you still have the power for new beginnings and radical changes in your life. The process may be arduous and slow but the sapling will surely become stronger with time, provided the lessons have been learned."}],"id":"ten-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Positive message of hope and renewal after a distressing period, luck and opportunities smiling again, time of relaxation and enjoyment, a major project getting finished with great returns, recreation and leisure, need to let go of painful past experience"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords10.png"},{"name":"Page of Swords","num":11,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Page","start":242,"end":244,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Personification of Air (Element Only)","Favourable Color":"Blue Gray","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Gray and Volatile Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Page of swords can describe a situation or personal attributes. It carries the seed of an intellectual thought or a person whose dynamic is life is based on thoughts, intellect and communication."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The Image shows a young man who is cutting through some dark clouds and is standing in an action position of sword held aloft. The Page of Swords will bear some news or message for you. When this card comes, it will be a definite communication you will receive."},{"t":"p","x":"Swords in page form represent all forms of intellect and communication. Some news regarding your ideas or your mental acumen will soon reach you. You need to be alert to activities related to communication of all types, professional offers, self expression offers and any educational initiatives concerning you."},{"t":"p","x":"This card also denotes a legal battle, mostly a tussle where there may be a conflict of ideas. It could also be a contract or agreement that needs to be signed.If there are more swords in the spread, it would be wise to seek the counsel of an expert before committing to anything on paper. In any case, when the Page of Swords turns up, you must be meticulous in understanding the fine language of any document or legal paper."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person the page of swords is a fierce fighter with words. Carrying excellent repertoire of words in his armoury, he uses words to win arguments, cut through obstacles and meet all resistance to ideas with aplomb. He may also be a master of sarcasm and very direct talk. He is not a person you would want to get into a word tussle with."},{"t":"p","x":"He is energetic and bursting with ideas. Impulsiveness and being brash with communication style is also part of his temperament."},{"t":"p","x":"He loves to be in touch with persons he has interacted with at some stage in life. Communication is the key to keep his mind running and he may use the social media extensively to propagate his ideas and opinions. He also would like to be in touch with you via mails or calls even though distantly located, geographically. He believes that meeting of minds knows no boundaries and that thoughts are meant to be shared and developed upon."},{"t":"p","x":"The downside is that he can be brusque with his words as like any page, there is a quickness and immaturity in his demeanour. However his intentions are pure and he will leave a lasting impact on your life due to his sharp intelligence or command over ideas or language."}],"id":"page-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Misunderstandings and wrongly expressed emotions, missed messages, nervous stuttering and stage fright, liar and deceptive person, impulsive speaking and hurtful words, gossiping to gain friends, mind is sharp and unpredictable, Master of words"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Swords11.png"},{"name":"Knight of Swords","num":12,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Knight","start":244,"end":246,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Taurus / Gemini","Favourable Color":"Blue Red Gray","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Troublesome and Volatile Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Knight of Swords is a man in a hurry. He rides a ferocious speeding horse, the sword cutting trough all obstacles in the path. He wears a full suit of armour and is unflinching his pursuit of goals."},{"t":"p","x":"As a situation something is about to happen very quickly when this knight appears. Much like the 8 of wands which shows speedy communication, this card indicates that plans will be put into action at a rather rapid pace and you will not have a moment’s chance to reconsider."},{"t":"p","x":"You will be surprised yourself at the frenzy all around you as you will have no chance to analyse what is happening around you. A situation will sweep you off your feet and it will most likely be linked to meeting someone influential or a strange melange of ideas with someone or having an experience that leaves you with pumped adrenaline."},{"t":"p","x":"Its also a card which will compel you into a direction where deep focus and fixity of purpose is required. This knight achieves targets single mindedly with little regard for permissions and protocol. Get prepared for a time of action, forceful decisions and asserting your individual opinions. It will also be a time when you make public speeches or project your talents and ideas to a larger audience with confidence and aplomb. You will get recognized for your originality. As a person this knight is akin to a warrior or a revolutionary soldier. This person is restless, impatient and has no time for dilemmas and delays. He rushes headlong into ventures without much judicious thought and may face setbacks and failures due to his hasty nature. Also can be a bully at times if the others are not thinking or acting at his ferocious pace. He may be mocking of the average or less than average performer."},{"t":"p","x":"He may be a student or practitioner of communication, advertising, Public relations, mass media, University lecturer, adventure sportsman among other interests."},{"t":"p","x":"You will feel strong when this person is siding with you but may become intimated when you have him as an opponent. With careful handling he is a definite asset. His high energy and obsessive target orientation should be constructively utilized for his strengths to be realized."}],"id":"knight-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Patience is required as the situation will move more slowly than you wand. Hold your Horses!"},{"t":"p","x":"Feeling regret over spoken word or deed, engaging in worthless debates/arguments, internet trolls"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Swords12.png"},{"name":"Queen of Swords","num":13,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"Queen","start":246,"end":249,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Virgo / Libra","Favourable Color":"Blue Red Gray","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Intellectual Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Queen of swords is an aristocratic and stern lady sitting on her plush throne. She has her back to the past and is looking into the future. Her place is among the clouds as she represents the air element; she has risen in intellect from the mundane. In one hand she holds a sword pointing to the sky and her left hand is extended as if offering something. The Queen of swords gives us the gift of judgement and discernment to manage our life better and also gives us the open mindedness to be receptive to ideas and knowledge from others. The butterflies on her throne symbolise transformation and the bird above her head speaks of her high ideals and superior intelligence level."},{"t":"p","x":"As a situation when the Queen of Swords makes an appearance in your spread, its time to let emotions be on the back burner and sharpen your analytical skills. An activity or responsibility of great weightage and scholarly aptitude is awaiting your expert touch. The situation may ask for an attitude of emotional detachment and where decisions have to be taken after much research and meticulous examination of facts. The Queen of swords indicates a time of loneliness and self-reliance. There will be a dearth of companionship and warm friendship in your life when this card comes up. You may have to keep yourself occupied with academic or mind oriented activities. Regular people may find you above their league and be intimidated by your clarity of thought and speech."},{"t":"p","x":"It could even indicate a need in your life for becoming less emotional and more rational. To use your intellectual capacity to reach your goals and expand your knowledge horizons. Emotional demands would only act as an unnecessary distraction. There are times in life when one needs to be focused on self."},{"t":"p","x":"You are on your way to greater heights but still have some goals to accomplish. You envision yourself as a provider of wisdom, strength, and knowledge to those around you, but you still have some inner work to complete first and the QOS urges you to continue."},{"t":"p","x":"You have already acquired many skills and talents that can help you assist others, but to truly flourish you will need to keep learning. Take a new course, experiment with a new passion, journal your ideas. The more you learn and expand, the better you will be able to expand others."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person this Queen can be enigmatic and self contained. She is often inscrutable who try to read the workings of her mind. She can be a fantasy figure in someone’s life who is desirable but unattainable. She is an aloof persona and avoids forming relationships in real life as that could make her vulnerable to emotional pain."},{"t":"p","x":"She is a woman with great fortitude and resilience, who can prune the unnecessary clutter and emotion in any situation and come to a decision that is fair and knowledgeable. She generally occupies a position of authority where many are affected by her mental skills."}],"id":"queen-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Sharp tongue, love for gossip and grapevine. This person loves intrigue and hatching conspiracies."},{"t":"p","x":"Bears grudges and likes revenge. Broods on the past and is self-opinionated and small minded."}],"tone":"positive","img":"Swords13.png"},{"name":"King of Swords","num":14,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Swords","rank":"King","start":249,"end":252,"meta":{"Element":"Air","Planets":"Mercury, Venus, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Capricorn/Aquarius","Favourable Color":"Blue Purple Gray Red","Chakra Associated":"Heart/Anahata Chakra"},"rating":"Intellectual Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The King of Swords is a very powerful figure, materially as well as metaphorically. about to unfold. He is a mature, pragmatic and inscrutable person who would be the final deciding factor in a situation which requires solution. He wears a ring on his middle left finger symbolizing his judicious powers akin to planet Saturn. His blue tunic symbolizes knowledge and understanding and his purple cape proclaims his power and ambition to reach the top of his field. The clouds around indicate mental challenges The two birds flying above the clouds are representing Huggin and Munnin, a pair of celestial ravens who always accompany Odin, The king of Gods. Huggin represents the thought and Munin represents the memory. Thought and Memory compositely constitute the Human Mind and impart it its uniqueness and elevation among all living creatures. In the poetic Edda, Odin says: Hugin and Munin fly each day over the spacious earth. I fear for Hugin, that he come not back, yet more anxious am I for Munin."},{"t":"p","x":"The double edged sword symbolizes the ability of this king to analyse a situation from both sides, butterflies stand for transformation and the two crescent moons symbolise balance between male and female energies."},{"t":"p","x":"This king denotes success and ambition in the highest sense. You will reach the top position in your domain with your single minded dedication to work. When this card appears, there is a fixation for acquiring material assets as a means of security and using your extraordinary mathematical, scientific or technical skills to create an empire for yourself. Great fame and respectability follows and there will always be a group of dedicated persons reporting to you and making this empire function smoothly."},{"t":"p","x":"King of Swords in a situation calls for calmly analysing all the aspects of a problem. Emotional partiality and emotional desires should be kept aside and what is best for long term sustenance should be opted for. The intellect rules the world and any act that elevates the Mind should be pursued at all costs. Emotions merely detract from the goal and the entrappings of emotional relationships are best avoided. Friendships with like minded and pragmatic persons may be on the cards when this card arrives. Behind this alliance would also be strategic planning for a collaboration in the possible future. Success has to planned meticulously. It is no accident but a result of carefully calculated thoughts and actions, this card teaches."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person, this card highlights the attributes of this mega achiever. He is witty, articulate and a very smart person. Its difficult to defeat him in arguments as he has a tremendous command over facts and figures and a remarkable memory. He may be a great debater or a writer with multi disciplinary knowledge."},{"t":"p","x":"He needs continuous mental stimulation to keep him engaged and he finds it hard to spend time with people who are overly emotional or sensitive. The compatibility frequency is absolutely different."},{"t":"p","x":"This man is often argumentative. He will go to any lengths to win a verbal argument in the name of debate with the opponent. His words are sharp and penetrating. He bears no regard for the feelings of the other and his single focus is on winning the exchange. For this he can do great research to support his case. He makes excellent investigative journalist, detective, writer or a public speaker."},{"t":"p","x":"Due to the richness of his ideas and facts as also his holistic perspective, he is often valued as a consultant and a mentor. He could also be a lawyer, a chartered accountant, doctor or a psychiatrist. He will give you an honest and expert opinion although you may not want to listen to it since it makes for uncomfortable listening."},{"t":"p","x":"He loves to get into disagreements and demonstrate his intelligence at every opportunity."},{"t":"p","x":"The person carrying the qualities of this King will a good friend but a formidable enemy.If he supports you he is a fastidious companion as he is level headed and maintain an objective view of whatever is happening. If he decides to oppose you, be prepared for a persevering argument that he will try to win at all costs. This king teaches to keep a cool head in spite of all hostilities, have a sardonic sense of humour, speak the truth even if it bites and use your mental sharpness to cut out your unique path in this world."}],"id":"king-of-swords","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Confused thinking, prejudice and biases, manipulative energies who love combat and even unhealthy competition"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Swords14.png"},{"name":"Ace of Pentacles","num":1,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Ace","start":252,"end":255,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Root Power of Earth (All Earth Signs Combined) - Taurus, Virgo, Capricorn","Favourable Color":"White Yellow Green","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Like all Aces, the Ace of Pentacles indicates potential. This ace in particular points to money and its uses. The Pentacle is a symbol of the earth element, and seen as a sign of wealth and all things material and earthy."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The single mysterious hand of opportunity appears from the clouds, holding potential in the form of a gold coin with a pentacle engraved on it. The sky is blue with few clouds, indicating no immediate storms in your path. The ground below is fertile, and the archway beckons you to enter. The coin represents the element of earth, and physical, or tangible things."},{"t":"p","x":"The Ace of Pentacle refers to the healthy beginning of a material venture that will bring prosperity or a rise in status. The image shows a flowering garden full of flowers giving off an aura of fertility, growth and affluence."},{"t":"p","x":"The Ace of Pentacles reveals that you have a chance for something new, something pertaining to the physical side of your life. New opportunities are here. They bring with them a chance for you to get closer to your goals, particularly pertaining to your career and the comforts that life has to offer. Its a very exciting card full of potential simply because it brings with it an open ended opportunity to engage in any activity that you are seeking fructification in. Its as if the UNIVERSE is asking you to visualize how you want your abundance to be manifested."},{"t":"p","x":"The traditional meaning of this card is an engagement or marriage, since these were often accompanied by dowries or extravagant gifts. In the modern times, it still means long term bonds that will stand the test of time and remain stable. It could also indicate a union where both parties are hard working on being focused on their career, will work towards better earnings and rise in fortunes."},{"t":"p","x":"As a sign of collaboration, the Ace of pentacles promises a very fruitful business partnership. Th venture will proceed smoothly and flourish with time. Also note the surrounding cards when energies of other persons are connected to the spread. While a 3 of wands here promises expansion and profits, the Moon could give rise to deceit and distrust. So also connect the meaning of a card in context with the surrounding cards."},{"t":"p","x":"This Ace is also connected with not only the material but also the sensual side of our existence. It could be the beginning of an experience that gives any of our senses, satisfaction. Attending an opera concert, creating a painting or a pom, visit to a luxury spa, a yoga regimen or even a sensual love affair are all indicated when this card comes along in a reading."},{"t":"p","x":"What gives you sensual pleasure and satiates you through your sensory system is an individual preference and must be studied accordingly with reference to the person’s query. In all cases this card will satisfy your material and sensory needs. It is indicative of rise in life and enhancement in reputation. Buying a new home, starting a new business, redecorating your living premises are all realities when this card is appearing. With the Ace of pentacles, you may also receive a windfall gain or a financial gift. You might receive a promotion at work or a wonderful appreciatory feedback and reference if you are self employed. You may also come across an item of value or buy a a valuable that appreciates over time."},{"t":"p","x":"Prosperity is on its way and it will be long lasting as it is rooted in reality and sustained hard work."},{"t":"p","x":"Make sure that you are psychologically prepared for the opportunities that are appearing. Pentacles arrive as a gift of bounty and you must be energetically ready to receive when it arrives. Maintain a calm and receptive mindset and be flexible to make changes in the conservative methods. Inculcate your spiritual prosperity to enable you to harvest the material prosperity."}],"id":"ace-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Financial blockages, Fear of investing or multiplying money, Lack of employment/ livelihood opportunities, Substance abuse and resultant bad health, Sedentary life style and lack of care of physical self, Eating processed foods rather than nourishing natural foods,Feeling high levels of anxiety and restlessness as grounding is lacking."}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles01.png"},{"name":"Two of Pentacles","num":2,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Two","start":255,"end":258,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Jupiter in Capricorn","Favourable Color":"Blue Red Brown","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Positive card with caution","body":[{"t":"p","x":"This is card of taking ups and downs of life with grace and flexibility and finding the undercurrent of joy of living even as you juggle the challenges that come in the wake of daily living. Imagery : A young man is seen dancing holding 2 pentacles in his hands and the pentacle disks are attached by an elastic that is similar to the sign of infinity. He holds one coin higher than the other, suggesting the ascendancy of that part of his life over the other. The two ships behind him are riding over choppy waters suggesting clearly that the juggling efforts will be successful."},{"t":"p","x":"The image is very pertinent in this card. The infinity symbol shows that the person can handle all the issues that will come his way with grace and dexterity. He is in a state of wonderful balance which he manages to do with his quick witted mind and careful planning."},{"t":"p","x":"This card is about the multitude of small challenges, foreseen and unforeseen that pop up in your life everyday. They have to be handled and handled well. This card in the spread shows you will need to be on your feet attending to many different aspects of your material life, requiring your attention. You will do it with joy and without getting hassled. This is also a card of finding joy in the mundaneness of life. If you lead your life with a sense of constant wonderment, each moment can be enjoyed."},{"t":"p","x":"At times managing the various demands will be tough but you must try to take each moment as it comes and learn the fine art of multi-tasking."},{"t":"p","x":"Since pentacles is about all those things in our life that imbue it with a sense of security, the two of pentacles is essentially the point where we will need to strike a delicate balance between two of these aspects. There could be two relationships in your life that are demanding simultaneous attention. You would need to decide that with the limited resource of time available with you, which of these needs to gain precedence at the moment. This is a constant case of jugglery as your resources are limited and the demands of life are many."},{"t":"p","x":"Being pentacles, the most obvious dilemma you will face with this card is to decide how you want to allocate your finances in at least two different aspects of life. There could be two expenses coming up but your financial resources are constrained. How you budget your financial resources so that the most important needs are met is a result of this card’s thinking. If you have a large loan taken out, this card could appear a lot as you try to pay that off while cutting down on usual expenses. This will require constant adjustments from your end. The message here is that such juggling will be a part of your everyday life as long as you are alive."},{"t":"p","x":"There will always be a choice to be made, whatever age you are at. Sometimes the choice may be between health and work or leisure and work or work vs the home life, career vs family and so on. These are an intrinsic part of the material life while you live a fulfilling human life."},{"t":"p","x":"One must try to deal with these nitty gritties with a stoical mind and graceful persona. Do not allow such worries to hassle you and deal with them as flexibly as you can. The infinity sign is very positive as it talks also of karmic give and take. As long as you are managing with grace, the Almighty will keep the flows coming in."},{"t":"p","x":"The two of pentacles shows that the budgeting you are having to do at the moment will be temporary. If you manage it astutely, giving precedence to the demand which needs to be attended urgently, then your life will flow towards more abundance. This card tells you to make intelligent choices and rather than multi tasking irrationally and making life complicated, you should prioritise the most important aspects of your life. It also advises you to make yourself a priority and not just cater to others’s needs and requirements. If the choice is between your physical or mental health and the responsibilities you shoulder, its time to give yourself the attention you deserve."}],"id":"two-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Inability to multi task right now, learning to prioritise and letting go of that which is not immediately rewarding, emotionally overwhelmed and unable to get work done, lack of choices in livelihood, unwilling to relocate or take transfer for work expansion, delays and glitches in business travel"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Pentacles02.png"},{"name":"Three of Pentacles","num":3,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Three","start":258,"end":261,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Mars in Capricorn","Favourable Color":"Gray Brown","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"When this card appears there are great advancements to be made. Its a hugely positive card for professional accomplishments. The lesson to be learned here is that the time for individual contribution needs to change for a broader perspective."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The image shows a young apprentice standing on an elevated surface, working on the construction of a cathedral. Two men(apparently the priest and a patron) stand in front of him as he highlights his ideas on the plans which are laid out on a parchment paper. The two men are more experienced than him yet listen to him with rapt attention due to the value of the specific expertise he carries. He is valuable to the project in spite of his hierarchical stature. The three of pentacles is the initial manifestation of your creative venture, business, or a new earthy relationship. Its the time when you are not the owner of your creation or idea anymore. It is now spreading out to the outer world. It is on fast track to expansion and will require you to be more daring and open to meeting patrons and promoting your work. Three always signifies growth after the initial germination of ones and the executive ability of twos. Its a time where you should be aware of the strengths of your project and articulate it to the external agencies. It is time to develop and expand the initial idea."},{"t":"p","x":"Your relationship with with your co-workers and collaborators will reach a higher level of intuitive understanding. You will be in harmony with each other’s working styles and an element of mutual trust and appreciation will prevail. If your work is looking to find new markets or customers this card is the most positive of the pentacles suit. It denotes the quality of your work or talent impressing the right people and the opportunity to expand and exhibit may walk right up to your doorstep. This is also a time to upgrade your job or business if you feel challenged enough. There will be encouraging response from the market for your unique talents. Even if your experience is lacking somewhat, the unique perspective and originality you bring to your work will make you rise in your field. Your job may even arrive if you have been recommended by someone rather than because you applied for it. iF you are self employed, this is an auspicious opportunity for being offered an important contract that gives you sustained returns. Boosts for your career, hobby turned profession, reputation, income are all on the cards. You need to be mentally prepared to seize these chances at making your wheel of fortune turn in your favour. Be clear and explicit in what uniqueness you can bring to a project or a new relationship. In retrospect you will realize the important stepping stone this will become in your path to ascension."},{"t":"p","x":"Another connotation for the three of pentacles is the need for team-work. You will have to learn to collaborate with the skills and assets of those around you. The period will call for greater camaraderie and teamwork from your side. You will learn the value and unique usefulness of a fruitful team and the splendid results it can create."},{"t":"p","x":"Successful projects usually require different kinds of expertise, and at this moment, the Three of Pentacles means that all the skills required are coming together. Great success awaits you if you become a part of an energizing and productive team. You should learn to receive and offer help, consult others for their perspective, and enjoy this fast track period of pursuing your ambition as it promises success and popularity and meaningful relationships."}],"id":"three-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Inter-personal conflict in team or department, team spirit is lacking, work getting criticized, appraisals getting delayed, promised promotion or pay hikes not being delivered, arrogant boss, lack of professional support, need for networking, need to promote your craft or product"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles03.png"},{"name":"Four of Pentacles","num":4,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Four","start":261,"end":264,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Sun in Capricorn","Favourable Color":"Gray Red Black Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The four of pentacles depicts achievement of financial security but also warns of being wrapped up in material affairs or of adopting an over possessive or even miserly attitude towards your resources. It is a card which carries both positive and negative perceptions."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : This card depicts a man sitting on a stool holding onto two pentacles in a defensive manner. One pentacle is balanced precariously on his head, the other held close to his chest and two are beneath either foot. He can not move for fear of loss of his pentacles."},{"t":"p","x":"This is at once a humorous and also satirical representation of the person when he has amassed a certain amount of security in the material comforts he was seeking."},{"t":"p","x":"Four of pentacles is a card of reassurance and abundance. All the efforts and collaborations of the first three cards have borne rich fruits. Your plans have worked out well and been financially rewarding."},{"t":"p","x":"You are in a stable and secure position as indicated by the FOURS in the Tarot. The buildings in the background are also depicting a good lifestyle and status for you."},{"t":"p","x":"However with security can come the desire to have more and to become miserly with what you do have. When this card comes, the person has developed an insecurity for his assets. You fear the loss of your hard earned fruits and become so fixated about their safekeeping that you are keeping guard over them day and night."},{"t":"p","x":"Its like an obsession which is never a healthy attitude to develop since it is making you immobile. You are sitting so tightly on our resources that the flow of abundance will eventually cease for you. When you do not put in the capital(material or otherwise) to expand further, then the progress will eventually halt."},{"t":"p","x":"This insecurity could stem from a past where you suffered from Lack. Not having sufficient resources in the past makes you now want to zealously defend what you have earned in order that savings for future are ensured. While savings are always a positive step, this card warns you to not become so obsessed with savings that you cannot enjoy your bounty. This\"POVERTY CONSCIOUSNESS” or\"LACK CONSCIOUSNESS” is a self fulfilling prophecy. It implies that when you think you do not have enough, that thought becomes a vibration and attracts more lack/poverty to you keeping you in a stagnant pool of meagre returns."},{"t":"p","x":"This avarice or miserliness should be translated into balanced spending and also inculcating the healthy\"ABUNDANCE CONSCIOUSNESS” where when you visualize that what you have is surplus, you will start attracting more riches to yourself. This is the cosmic law of cause and effect that has been eulogized well in Indian and Western classical texts alike. What you give freely of, you shall receive freely of, goes the Universal Law of Attraction."},{"t":"p","x":"At times, this card can indicate a sensible approach of keeping financial information to yourself. This can also show when you want to keep your plans and ideas to yourself for a while before sharing them with the external world. This buffer period helps the idea or information to mature and when the timing is correct, it may be revealed. It may also be a useful approach to keep a tab on your financial affairs if surrounding cards are indicating extravagance and mindless expenditure."},{"t":"p","x":"Thus this card is dual in its meaning. It reassures of incoming prosperity yet it advises you to maintain a degree of balance in your perspective regarding itas also a sense of detachment."}],"id":"four-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Greed and hoarding, black marketing and corruption, keeping secrets, nouveau riche and so now overspending, reckless investments, disrespect to money and other resources around you, renouncing worldly possessions in order to lead a simpler life, sharing of intellectual and material possessions with an open heart"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles04.png"},{"name":"Five of Pentacles","num":5,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Five","start":264,"end":267,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Venus in Taurus","Favourable Color":"Black White Brown","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Difficult card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Five of pentacles is a card of misery and misfortune. It symbolizes adversity and a loss of what you consider to be of value to you. Tremendous inner courage is required to tide over the down period."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : This is a rather desolate looking card with two helpless, impoverished human figures wearily trudging along in heavy snow. They are cold, tired and hungry and seem to be lacking even the basic necessities of life. One of them is supported on crutches while the other’s feet are bare as she walks on the icy ground."},{"t":"p","x":"All the fives are difficult cards in the Tarot and this one is especially so. The Five of Pentacles is a bad omen whenever it appears in the spread. Its severity however will be influenced by the surrounding cards. When this card appears some form of loss is imminent. There may have a substantial financial downturn and your fortune cycle has really dipped. You might have speculated in a venture which has sunk and so there is a financial crisis. There would have been a sudden loss of material wealth and you are really feeling the pinch. There might be a damage or loss to a business property or premises."},{"t":"p","x":"Since this card is about impoverishment, it can also be perceived impoverishment. The returns you were expecting from a venture did not materialize as per your desire or business forecast; it leaves you confounded and feeling a loss strongly. You may have been eyeing an expensive property or bidding for a lucrative deal that could enhance your prestige in the fraternity. If you do not acquire that due to external reasons, you would again perceive it as a loss. Loss of face in such ways of projected extravagance is also an integral part of this card’s subliminal message. Wealth is a highly subjective term and how much wealth is enough wealth to make you feel wealthy is really a very personal take on the concept. Hence this\"felt poverty” should also be explored when this card comes up in a reading."},{"t":"p","x":"The thoughts and worries regarding money may be getting in your way. You may be too attached to money or worried about success and failure in an excessive manner to the extent that it is affecting your peace of mind and what kind of productivity:output ratio you start expecting at your workplace. This card can also denote a sense of loneliness and isolation. It could be voluntary in that you feel disconnected from your immediate environment, if you are perceiving they are financially or culturally superior to you. They may not be isolating you deliberately yet your complex kicks in and you start alienating yourself by not accepting invitations and turning anti-social."},{"t":"p","x":"This card can also indicate a real outcasting by your family or your social group if you are felt to be breaking the accepted norms by your unconventional behaviour. The impoverishment here can be real in terms of loss of emotional support and understanding.It could even translate you being detached from your family or ancestral property as a punitive measure. Whatever the form, the five of pentacles is a card of suffering and lack of support and succour. Its important to keep the inner reserves optimistic when this card is playing out in your life. In the image, the figures are at a disadvantage yet they are bravely moving and traversing the difficult terrain. Five is a number of change in the Tarot so the difficult situation you are facing will not last forever. It may even be a catalyst for positive change. You may receive enlightenment as to who are your real well wishes and who are superficial. It might even change your perspective towards the blessings you have and be in gratitude when your wealth is restored by your sheer determination and faith in a higher force."}],"id":"five-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Positive card indicating end of unemployment or low finances, Financial breakthrough, community recognition, windfall gains, count your blessings, being practical about revenue sources and doggedly pursuing abundance goals, financial help coming in"}],"tone":"challenging","img":"Pentacles05.png"},{"name":"Six of Pentacles","num":6,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Six","start":267,"end":269,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Moon in Taurus","Favourable Color":"Red Purple Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Karmic card. Very Positive","body":[{"t":"p","x":"This is a card of having surplus resources. It teaches that Money is an Energy- The more it Flows; The More it Grows. It indicates charity, generosity and sharing and a fair flow of resources such that resource balance is maintained. Its a very positive card in all respects."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : A respectable and affluent looking man wearing purple robes denoting his high status stands distributing coins to beggars. He is secure with his own condition of resources and is generously sharing his bounty with those who are n need. In his hand, he holds scales and much like the Justice card, this indicates balance of karma and the cause and effect cycle of Life."},{"t":"p","x":"This is a situation where you are likely to give or receive money. Mostly its about receiving as the Universe is in your favour and your desires are being fulfilled.Although pentacles as a suit represent money and material possessions, your emotions are a valuable resource. Thus this card will also pertain to your emotions about the give and take money. When this card appears you are in a state of gratitude and subservience to the Universe. You may be feeling a large heartedness and will go in for a donation or a charity gesture. You might make small gestures to help those who are underprivileged. As pentacles also denote knowledge as a resource, you could even selflessly give of your knowledge or technical expertise without expecting any payback. Its a time to be free flowing with your resources, of any kind. It dies not always have to be about money or material possessions only. Anything that the person receiving from you holds in value pertaining to you is significant here. Your time and presence and an empathetic ear may be the resources he will appreciate from you. You may also be at the receiving end at times in your life. This card teaches that one must not be shy or even arrogant when you are in need of support. It could help you recover at that time so take the help. You will be able to repay the kindness in the future. This card carries the message that all flow of resources is linked to a larger cycle in the cosmos. What you give should be done so in a humble manner. You should be grateful that you are in a position to help someone. The universal abundance is flowing through you and you are merely the channel who is in a privileged status to be at the giving end."},{"t":"p","x":"Let that not become condescension or arrogance. When you help but with a doubtful heart, or with grudge in your heart that help is not counted as good karma. Similarly while receiving, be humble and do not cross your boundary and come across as desperate. The karmic scales are always being calculated so mind the emotion with which you give and receive both. When this card comes in a reading its a sure sign to balance the scales. You could be either giving more of yourself or less than required. Its time to analyse and balance your give and take in life-material or emotional."}],"id":"six-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Problem card in financial flows, money blockage, payments being held up, profits not coming in, debts, expecting financial help from others, no balance as you may be expecting total help from outside or not accepting any help at all, financial stalemate, exploiting human resources by not rewarding for their service, being non\u0002charitable, non recovery of loans given out"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles06.png"},{"name":"Seven of Pentacles","num":7,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Seven","start":269,"end":272,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Saturn in Taurus","Favourable Color":"Green Yellow Orange","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Moderate Positive card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Seven of pentacles in an assessment period of the dedicated labour put in so far in the pentacle journey. Its a time to pause and review the past accomplishments and make any calibrations if needed, to keep the progress going. Imagery : A young man is taking a break and leaning on his work tool is carefully analysing the fruit in his garden, the labour he has put in to obtain the produce. He admires the seven pentacles hanging from the lush vegetation. The way he is leaning suggests he is fatigued, He is focused on long term goals and thus only partakes for his pleasure one of the pentacles while he reinvests the others to expand his project. This is a period of assessment of past inputs and the resultant output. Time to take stock of your achievements and also plan the future course of action. This card may indicate that results are taking a longer than expected time to pour in and hence you may be dismayed where the lag is. This card indicates confusion and indecision if the planning has been worthwhile and where the changes can be introduced for the future performance to be of a higher level."},{"t":"p","x":"Its the time to take stock that though you may be working hard but are the efforts in the right direction? Are you working smart? Do not take your skills and expertise for granted, this card says. Think of fresh ways to use them. Do not change the ingredients but rather the techniques and processes you are using the resources in, to reach your objectives. Sevens also indicate a time to introspect keeping the long term life goals in perspective so take this time to align your responsibilities with your long term goals. Be clear where you want to take your life down the timeline and then plan backwards and check if present performance / efforts are synergising with long term achievements."},{"t":"p","x":"Seven of pentacles is also about making major changes in the way you have allocated your resources. The current allocation may not be bringing you peace or prosperity. Thus you may decide to end some part of your resource allocation and reinvest in avenues which make you happier or make you feel more secure."},{"t":"p","x":"You might decide to leave a stable corporate job and farm the land in the countryside that you inherited from your family. It could mean work that excites you and cost of living being lower could actually make you feel richer at the end of the day. The satisfaction of organic farming would only add value to your self worth."},{"t":"p","x":"Similarly a woman who took few years off to raise her family now finds that her efforts are not being needed so much at home front so there is an effort: output ratio imbalance. She decides to go back to part time consulting work and adjusts her working style to online consulting. She now has a good income apart from the sense of identity she now finds reestablished."},{"t":"p","x":"These kind of calibrations may occur at various junctures in your life. When you feel dissatisfied with the deliverables coming to you then its time to take some smart decisions and re invest your future time and efforts into avenues that bring you greater of what kind of wealth you desire."},{"t":"p","x":"Weigh up you physical and mental skills and make a list of what you can offer to a future employer or to your self employment venture. Its a time to revisit and refresh and maybe upgrade the skills that make you productive."},{"t":"p","x":"When the seven of pentacles comes up, there is definitely a tinge of regret that creeps into you. You are disappointed for some reason. Carefully analyse how you can astutely change your time and skill allocation so that physical or material or spiritual satisfaction may accrue to you in the coming times."}],"id":"seven-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"realizing that efforts are wasted and giving up on a project or a relationship, disillusionment and sadness, repeating same mistakes as in past and getting into a failure loop, repetitive negative emotional patterns, ignoring advice and pointers to improve the situation at hand"}],"tone":"mixed","img":"Pentacles07.png"},{"name":"Eight of Pentacles","num":8,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Eight","start":272,"end":275,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Sun in Virgo","Favourable Color":"Brown Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"This card carries the energy of Patience,Concentration and the Pursuit of Perfection with Passion. Focus on performance and not get swayed by emotional waves."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : A hard working young man is working laboriously on a single pentacle. He is chiseling out the design on the circular base and creating the pentagram on it with total focus/ One pentacle awaits at his feet while 6 others are hanging on what looks like a tree trunk, bearing testimony to his sustained efforts in the past."},{"t":"p","x":"The eight of pentacles refers to those situations in your life when you need to remove yourself from all distractions and temptations of the outside world (as symbolised by the town in the distance) and be fully engrossed in the responsibility that has been allocated to you. Astrologically this is a position of Sun in Virgo which shows that individual excellence and craftsmanship can be achieved only by meticulous and careful attention to detail towards the work at hand. He is focusing on what he Needs to do rather than what he wants to do. By not listening to the inner voices that can distract him, this young man remains busy in his work. By being mindful of each small gesture and thought he is moving towards perfecting his learning and moving up the ladder of progress. When this card comes in a reading, its time to work hard and diligently. This is not a card of immediate gratification but when your diligence is noticed by those in power, your rise will be inevitable. You should be confident of your unique skill set and if you feel that you need further learning then make tangible efforts to upgrade your knowledge."},{"t":"p","x":"You could be joining a new course or join an apprenticeship program or join an organization for the main purpose of gaining work experience. Even if your subject of choice is unconventional or pioneering, have the courage to pursue it with sincerity. It will turn out to be a very fruitful venture. In your career there may come a time when a new project has to be initiated. This will require your complete attention. For a while, you might need to become a workaholic who thinks about his work all the time. This kind of attention will yield excellent fruits later. Do not be discouraged if it calls for excessive detail oriented activities as its the micro achievements that will lead to achievement of major goal. Exercise restraint and resilience."},{"t":"p","x":"This card in the relationship is also prophetic. It signals that this is a stable and solid alliance and with time will become more perfect and harmonious for the parties involved. There will be many moments of mutual happiness and perfect balance and they will help to develop each other’s talents and skills. This relationship will make your fortunes rise."},{"t":"p","x":"The eight of pentacles may also come up when you are going back to a productive activity after a gap. This is a strong and positive indicator of success. It says that work comes naturally to you and that you wish to be a useful contributor to society. This sense of service and practical skills will be applauded and make you happy and energized."},{"t":"p","x":"This card calls conclusively for success in any venture, including money gains when the work ethic is of sincerity, systematic approach to work and a genuine joy in the work you are doing even if it is mundane and repetitive in nature."}],"id":"eight-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Delay or denial of promotion and advancement opportunities at work, hard work not getting rewarded, lack of interest in perfecting the task at hand, impatience to get results, attention deficit, ADHD disorder, poor quality of work, disappointing card in relationships as calls for putting in more effort"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles08.png"},{"name":"Nine of Pentacles","num":9,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Nine","start":275,"end":277,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Venus in Virgo","Favourable Color":"Green","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Nine of Pentacles in a card of joyfulness and enjoyment of abundance in life. The arduous work is behind her and a period of achievement and happiness awaits."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : A beautiful and affluent woman is standing in the middle of the vineyard surrounded by lush fruits of her hard work and astute management of resources."},{"t":"p","x":"This is astrologically symbolised by Venus in Virgo and denotes luxuries and financial rewards gained by astute business or professional judgement. When this card comes up, you can be assured of unexpectedly good financial and material gains."},{"t":"p","x":"A promotion, pay hike, high paying job, win in lottery, appreciation in property, buying a new luxurious house are all the blessings of the Venus energy inherent in nine of pentacles. You have reached a point in your life where everything is going in your favour. You have reached a very secure and comfortable place of security. Material benefits are the most prominent amongst these security factors. You now have a great deal to show for all your past efforts and struggles. It shows the feeling of self - assurance and a calm confidence that what you have built around you is tangible and real. This confidence is so authentic because it is not a gift or an inheritance. It has been built, brick by brick by your own hard work, resource management and sheer dedication towards your work."},{"t":"p","x":"You may have overcome negative feedback, discouragement and deception along your way till here and you feel validated and at complete peace with the world because of the karmic payback being so positive. This card may also indicate you going in for a lifestyle product or an expensive object such as a new car, branded clothes or accessory, costly furniture or taking an exotic trip. These are outer manifestations of your inner sense of having arrived in the society. A gray undercurrent here is that you may be tempted to give in to extravagances but generally the nine of pentacles figure will make luxuries a part of life in an aware manner. You have not got to this point by being foolish with your money."},{"t":"p","x":"If surrounded by cards that encourage enjoyment like the Sun or 9 of cups, its your signal that now you must enjoy the fruits of your labour and Indulge in sensual pleasures.Your previous struggles have given you the spiritual understanding about the flow of money and you are possessing the inner strength to enjoy your material and creative freedom and not get trapped into it."},{"t":"p","x":"The nine of pentacles is excellent for marriage and any type of romantic collaboration queries. It indicates a passionate and well grounded union that will bring bounty in the long run. As an advice card, this card asks you to be in gratitude to your hard earned abundance. You are capable enough to have created this edifice and your calibre is so high that no other person can negate it or take it away from you. You have to ability to create and procreate. Card of self assurance, empowerment and self sufficiency."}],"id":"nine-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Spending more than you can afford to build self esteem, low profits and financial blocks, creative businesses shutting down, getting into easy money by social contacts, overindulgent luxury loving habits, shallowness and superficiality. At times guidance card to enjoy the bounty you have earned by your hard work and toil."}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles09.png"},{"name":"Ten of Pentacles","num":10,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Ten","start":277,"end":280,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Mercury in Virgo","Favourable Color":"Red Yellow Green Red","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Extremely Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"Ten of Pentacles is the\"Satisfaction Card” and denotes the culmination point of material and emotional security. Attainment of all things that bring a sense of satisfaction to you. Imagery : The aged man with white beard sits contentedly under an archway dressed an ornate expensive cape. The cape is decorated with moon crescents and grapes indicating the union of spirit and matter; He is looking out towards his son and his daughter in law who are engrossed in a conversation. The young grandson playfully reaches to the dog. 10 golden pentacles adorn various parts of this image displaying an environment of affluence and solidity. The Ten of pentacles is an incredibly fortunate card to receive in any query related to future prospects. It indicates material satisfaction and a blissful married life. It denotes comforts of all types- whether financial or health related or spiritual. Ten of pentacles deals with permanence and security. All the efforts and struggles you have encountered till translate into fruits that will only grow and multiply with time. The bounty is not just for the present but for future times as indicated so strongly by the presence of three generations co-existing harmoniously in the card image."},{"t":"p","x":"Relationship problems if any will be resolved soon as you understand the true value of each other on a humane level and will make a strong resolve to stay together and build a stronger future. It may also indicate buying a new home or creating your own customized space within a larger unit which will carry your stamp as a couple."},{"t":"p","x":"In love affair, you are inextricably bound to each other and will have the resilience to face any opposition and still stay united and loyal to each other. If related to conception, this card is a strong indicator of happy news regarding fertility. The child will be healthy and will grow up surrounded by the warmth and love of an extended family. Ancestral lines are strongly indicated when this card appears. The security that so surrounds you may have been passed down through the generations. It could herald the initiation or progress in family business or gains through family held property. You may come into inheritance or receive a cherished family heirloom. When this card comes up with regards to choice of profession you are being guided by destiny to pursue the family business or the family profession such as architecture, chartered accountancy or medicine if many of your relatives are already following them. You are likely to receive invaluable references and advice from those already engaged in that line of profession. With this card its time to celebrate your family bonds. You are blessed to be surrounded by the genuine warmth and experience of your family and must put in your efforts to strengthen the familial bonds."}],"id":"ten-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Rebellion against traditions and norms, rejecting family practices and walking down new paths, getting into unconventional means of business, entrepreneurship on individual basis, financial uncertainty, feeling of who am I and what am I doing here?, nuclear family and small family, selling ancestral home or property, attraction to new and aversion to the old."}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles10.png"},{"name":"Page of Pentacles","num":11,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Page","start":280,"end":283,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Personification of Earth (Element Only)","Favourable Color":"Yellow Green Red","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Stable Card of New Beginnings","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Page of Pentacles is a cautious, business minded young person who plans and analyses prior to taking action. He is loyal and reliable and is rooted to the reality of life. The image shows a young man holding a disk of pentacle in his hands and gazing reverently in it. He is well dressed and looks pleased with himself. The setting is lush countryside. As a situation this card is the arrival of good or pleasant news. It could be a person who will bring you good news about work or could mean a communication, mail or a meeting offer with regards to consolidation of your work or security plans. The situation is still young,. Pages indicate the early stages of a project and since the pentacles are connected with finance, security and the physical body, the project could pertain of one of these and will require careful nurturing. You are at the planning stage and a strong foundation at this stage can mean the difference between final success or failure. At this a fruitful opportunity for expansion is present but it is still an idea and will need intensive implementation. When this page comes along, some news regarding your monetary health is on the way. It would not be a large amount unless surrounding cards indicate profits and gains but will be of pleasant proportions nevertheless. You could also receive some useful information related to investment opportunity or a job offer you were awaiting."},{"t":"p","x":"If life has been stressful of late, the news carried by this reliable Page could bring respite and stability. There might be an opportunity to experience which provides you artistic or cultural refinement."},{"t":"p","x":"This page carries an opportunity of reinventing yourself. The coin in the page’s hand is a new opportunity which he is handling with sensitivity and attention and obviously delighting in the unfolding of the new interest. There might be the beginning of a new course, a new fitness or makeover program, a new job experience, a new artistic venture, a new work challenge or even a new competition which requires meticulous preparation."},{"t":"p","x":"An opportunity to begin anew has presented itself in the present context and it must be graciously accepted. Its a means to reinvent yourself. T would require being practical and organised; not going into flights of fancy but rather to ground yourself and be sincerely interested in each step of the process."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person, this page is cautious and stable. He is not swayed by emotions. obviously refined and cultured, his personal demeanour is important to him. He wants people to appreciate him for his classy behaviour and his well presented exterior."},{"t":"p","x":"He is also very sensitive to others’ needs and will go out of his way to systematize the issue for the other. He has an innate command over financial and business matters and approaches each new venture as a chance to add value to it by useful contributions."},{"t":"p","x":"He is grounded in his perspective to life and his ideas are matter of fact and practical. He may not go info fancy high education but will be successful in his profession or business because he goes about it in a logical and empathetic manner. With his ears close to the ground, he is natural at changing market trends and is also a calm and analytical people’s person. He is an excellent team worker and provides implementable ideas that bring positive results."},{"t":"p","x":"Being very practical in nature, he is not romantic or emotional or even fanciful. He believes in action more than speech and conversations. Some may find him staid and boring if looking for more exciting company. However there is a solidity and reliability in him that makes him an indispensable friend and a partner for life."}],"id":"page-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Lack of growth in matters related to security and productivity, unfocused and unorganised attitude, poor budgeting skills, losses and poor returns financially, not having a head for numbers"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles11.png"},{"name":"Knight of Pentacles","num":12,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Knight","start":283,"end":286,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Leo / Virgo","Favourable Color":"Yellow Brown Red","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Promising and Hopeful Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Knight of Pentacles denotes practical and sustained efforts directed towards a goal and as persona attributes a detailed oriented and dedicated person interested in material matters. The heavy black horse and the full armoured knight is a man on a mission. The road ahead indicates his path of ambition he is willing to traverse slowly and steadily. He holds the pentacle disk directly in his line of vision, making him focussed on his goal at all times."},{"t":"p","x":"As a situation when this Knight comes in a reading, it is time for the material manifestation idea that had originated with the Page of Knights to transmute into an executable plan. The knight of pentacles is a very devoted worker. He is meticulous and carrying properties of the Earth element which symbolizes astrologically the signs of Taurus, Virgo and Capricorn, he is obsessed with his vision and pays no heed to distractions. When this card comes up a work opportunity will come along that will require unflinching detailed oriented efforts from you. There will be no time for leisure and pleasure. Instead of getting bored or distracted, its the time to become extra hardworking and perform your duty like a penance. It could even signal a situation that has come to a temporary halt. The knight of Pentacles is an overcautious, slow moving character of the Tarot Court and this is translated in the progress of the situation that is being analyzed. You may have reached an impasse with someone so all you can do is wait it out for the flow of events to happen. It will require patience and the surrender that though you want to act, it would not be useful."},{"t":"p","x":"Perhaps there is a clash of ideologies with the other players in the situation. You would need to stand firm if you feel you are morally in the right. You may even be feeling a sense of dullness or stagnation at your place of work when this knight trudges along in the reading. Maybe the sheer routine of your daily activity is making you feel irritated. On the positive note, when this knight comes up in a reading it shows you have more patience and capacity to slog than you would imagine yourself to have. Its time to utilize those inherent skills as the work at hand is requiring mundane, clerical and repetitive approach to work."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person, the knight of pentacles is practical, determined, and you can easily repose your trust in him. If you belong to another suit, he may appear to you rather stolid and slow moving, at times incapable to take quick decisions. He is not very invigorating company and is reticent by nature. In feelings, he may be undemonstrative but his loyalties run deep. He is a steadfast and faithful lover and friend. Being from the earth element, there are hidden fires raging inside and they possess a depth of passion and sensuality. This knight is an asset to an organization as he is the pillar that may hold diverging energies together. He is particular about deadlines and deliverables and focused on customer delight. Any work related to property, project management, Money management, Banking, Business, General Management, Hotel Industry, Teaching, education dissemination among others would be suitable for him."}],"id":"knight-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Skills not being fully honed, less staying power, no competitive spirit, lacking determination to self improve, apathy towards body and health, lack of hygiene, indifference to physical and emotional environmental clutter, poor allocation of time and energy being spent"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles12.png"},{"name":"Queen of Pentacles","num":13,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"Queen","start":286,"end":289,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Sagittarius / Capricorn","Favourable Color":"Green Red Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Very Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The Queen of pentacles is a calm, nurturing, nature oriented, practical woman of achievements. She creates an environment of warm energy and reassurance in her domain. Success and fertility are indicated."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The beautiful queen sits on a decorated throne in her red robes and golden crown. She holds the golden disk in her hands and gazes at it lovingly. Around her vines bloom and trees flourish. The challenging mountains recede in the background. A brown hare is about to jump into the image showing the queen’s fertility. It also cautions that for prosperity to sustain, one must think before chasing after success. The Queen of Pentacles appears as an assurance of success and fertility. She denotes achievements and progress in all matters of material world. She also gives out the secret to acquiring this wealth."},{"t":"p","x":"Sheer hard work and the judgement of how and when to spend are the twin ingredients of success in the world of outward manifestations. When this card appears, you will have a fabulous opportunity to move ahead in your career aspirations. Your efforts will be lauded and your seniors will support you."},{"t":"p","x":"You will however have to believe mainly in your own skills and will power. Be steadfast and continuous in your work. Its this ambition which will make you squash the opposition and make you emerge as the winner. Your attitude is extremely important if you want to harness the promised riches of this card. If the correct attitude falters, then the gains would not reach you."},{"t":"p","x":"You are a clear and fearless communicator. You do not waste your energies in unnecessary talking but will happily share all information required to get the work done. Your task orientation is a glowing example of your professionalism and your admirers learn the tricks of the trade from you. With this card, rest assured you are a role model for many aspirants. When this card appears your home may be beckoning you for some management and discipline. Your practical and logical decisions appease the human emotions and people take their responsibilities more seriously. In your warm yet stern manner you keep all processes under control and when the work is done, you let your guard down and also have a good time bolstering your fame as a good hostess."},{"t":"p","x":"Banking and money management are in your blood so with this card, be prepared to get some accounts in spanking order. Monitor the expenses and make intelligent choices regarding how much to spend and how much to invest. Your shrewd businesswoman instincts may be required in the present situation."},{"t":"p","x":"You should be investing in material or emotional ventures that will last for long. Its prudent to go for high quality items since their performance will be optimal over a longer duration. You are attracted to natural fabrics and all things natural. Being naturally close to Mother Earth and its treasures, this Earthy Queen will encourage you to live simply yet comfortably. As a woman, the Queen of pentacles is very calm and patient. She can teach you wise use of resources so you can become self sufficient and do not need to depend on others for your sustenance. She is a big advocate of financial independence and will have her secret egg’s nest stored away. She can be an excellent confidante as she never gives away secrets. Averse to gossip, she has few but long lasting friendships who share her taste for aesthetics and common sense."},{"t":"p","x":"A loyal friend and a fantastic business woman, the Queen is an asset who will keep giving you service for a long time. Invest in her. You will stay wealthy."}],"id":"queen-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Undeveloped creativity, not able to make use of talents and skills, Relying on others to make decisions, low self confidence and low self awareness, afraid of action and responsibilities, may blame others for own failure"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles13.png"},{"name":"King of Pentacles","num":14,"arcana":"minor","suit":"Pentacles","rank":"King","start":289,"end":292,"meta":{"Element":"Earth","Planets":"Venus, Mercury, Saturn","Astrological Significance":"Cusp of Aries / Taurus","Favourable Color":"Green Purple Yellow","Chakra Associated":"Root/Muladhara Chakra"},"rating":"Extremely Positive Card","body":[{"t":"p","x":"The King of Pentacles is the emblem figure of wealth, prosperity and financial success. Signifies high ambition, superior status, generous sharing of bounty, kingmaker, materialistic satisfaction."},{"t":"p","x":"Imagery : The King of Pentacles sits in the shadow of his own success. He sits on a throne adorned with bulls carvings and vines. The robe he wears is also adorned by the multiplicity inducing grapevine. He holds the golden disk in his lap and is fully engrossed in its contemplation. The castle in the background denotes his riches earned over time with determination."},{"t":"p","x":"His gold glistens, and he's very serious about his wealth. He's regal, he's reached the pinnacle of his success, he has riches and material possessions. This level of professional success and almost fanatical ambition is the message of the card. If you wish to reach the pinnacle of material success, are you prepared to make the emotional compromises involved in the process? His iron boots suppress the living creature which symbolizes his emotions and sensitivities. If you wish to become like him then your emotional bondings will have to be suppressed. The overwhelming thought in your mind should be only of your financial and material progress. Its an all consuming Passion you will have to exhibit."},{"t":"p","x":"Like all kings, the King of Pentacles represents motivation. This card can also refer to a man, in particular, someone who is either a pragmatic businessman, or someone with deep connections to the land. You may be coming in contact with such a person who will be in a more established position to you but will give you important technical or monetary help to move up the ladder of success."},{"t":"p","x":"This card s represents everything that comes to mind when you think of wealth or success; control, power, security, possessions, and more. So be prepared for work for it and you are destined to receive plenty."},{"t":"p","x":"Your capacity to multiply money is also being awakened now. Do your market research, follow your shrewd instinct of being a money magnet, tap on your networking contacts. Make some sharp moves to rule the market and beat the competition. Your market savvy and killer instincts are all required in full flamboyance now."},{"t":"p","x":"As a person, being in a King of Pentacles prototype, you are being advised to be cautious financially. Keep your money details to yourself and do not get into any reckless partnerships."},{"t":"p","x":"Help a smart but cash deficit young businessman launch himself. You are a king maker and its your duty as well as your interest to help others rise materially. You are a good leader of people, and are an excellent example of how to become an affluent and powerful person even if the beginnings had been modest. You can also be a great financial advisor or fund manager. Sometimes you back political figures by being their financial backer too. Power is tempting to you but since you do not like the limelight, you prefer to give sensible money advice from behind the curtains."},{"t":"p","x":"In relationships you are a loyal and dutiful companion. You are no demonstrative and do not have much affection to squander. Time is money to you your work will always remain your first priority. However you have no parallel when it comes to your protective and caring attitude. A natural nurturer, you want to provide the best for your family and cherished friends and do it with humility and grace."},{"t":"p","x":"A man of steel, you show the world how grit and grace can combine to make the diamond sparkle. Your authentic shine cannot be missed."}],"id":"king-of-pentacles","reversed":[{"t":"p","x":"Greedy and avaricious person or energy, very conscious of monetary & financial security, conservative, cautious investor, possessive, jealous, workaholic, overindulgent, exploitive of loved ones"}],"tone":"positive","img":"Pentacles14.png"}];
